window.EB_SB_ADD({"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/10g48u9UtpzswyOa":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Melodian","Pyric"],"abilities":[{"n":"Rage and Relaxation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Aestivals are most often in their languid state, where they are permanently Slowed 1 and under the effects of Sanctuary. If they take damage from any source, they become awakened until the end of their next turn, losing the slowed condition and the effects of sanctuary. While awakened, they are Quickened (the extra action can be used only to Stride, Climb, or Strike), and they deal an additional 4 fire damage with their Strikes and with their Ignition cantrip.</p><p>Effect: Awakened</p>"},{"n":"Rest a While","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the aestival's reach uses a move action or leaves a square during a move action it's using</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The aestival attempts an Athletics check to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the aestival's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Wildfire Cloak","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>While the aestival is awakened, all terrain they move through becomes fiery, hazardous terrain, dealing 5 fire damage to any creature who moves into one of these squares. The hazardous terrain lasts until the start of the aestival's next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Heatstroke","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>An aestival's fists sap energy, much like a day of hard labor beneath a baking sun. An affected creature must succeed at a DC 21 Fortitude save or become Fatigued.</p>"},{"n":"Summer Blaze","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The aestival is awakened</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The aestival Strides or Climbs and then makes two fist Strikes against a single enemy. Apply the multiple attack penalty to these Strikes normally. If both Strikes succeed, the target also takes 1d6 persistent fire damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/h2a3QXsiASd0zWaB":{"lang":["Common","Fey"],"gear":["Staff","Dragon Bile (2)","Nightmare Vapor (2)"],"notes":{"per":"blightsense 20 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Blightsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An agiyeft senses any creature that is poisoned or diseased, and knows the type and current stage of all poisons and diseases carried by any creature within range.</p>"},{"n":"Toxin Manipulation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. An agiyeft can alter the toxins in a creatures body, even turning them into neurotoxins. When any creature in the aura attempts a save against a disease or poison the agiyeft may grant a +1 status bonus or –1 status penalty to the save, and can choose to change it into a Will save instead of a Fortitude save.</p>"},{"n":"Hemodermal Spray","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["healing","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The agiyeft takes piercing or slashing damage.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The agiyeft flings medicinal toxins in their blood at a creature within 20 feet, either healing it 5d6 healing Hit Points, or dealing 5d6 poison damage (DC 37 basic Fortitude save). The agiyeft chooses which.</p>"},{"n":"Venom Touch","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>hen an agiyeft deals piercing or slashing damage with a Strike they may expose the creature to Agiyeft's Meddling, Agiyeft's Whim, or any other poison they have on them. Any poison applied to a Strike this way gains the Injury trait, and has a DC 37 Fortitude or the poison's listed DC, which ever is higher. If the target is already suffering from a poison they take 1d6 poison damage instead.</p>"},{"n":"Agiyeft's Meddling","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["healing","poison","virulent"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 37 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> fast healing 1, Clumsy 1, Enfeebled 1, and Stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> fast healing 3, Clumsy 2, Enfeebled 2, and Stupefied 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> fast healing 5, Clumsy 3, Enfeebled 3, and Stupefied 3 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Agiyeft's Whim","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["healing","poison","virulent"],"f":"","d":"<p>A strange concoction of various ingredients the agiyeft has collected. At each stage the creature must attempt a flat check against that stage's listed DC. On a failure the creature takes poison damage equal to the amount of dice rolled for that stage, and on a success the creature regains Hit Points equal to half the amount rolled</p><p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 37 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> DC 6 Flat and 8d6 poison damage (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> DC 12 Flat and 10d6 poison damage (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> DC 18 Flat and 12d6 poison damage (1 round)</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/QicNy5FUxJaXz3gN":{"lang":["Common","Spirituan","Truespeech"],"gear":["Staff"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status vs. illusions"},"abilities":[{"n":"Dulling Radiance","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","light","mental","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. The aglys is surrounded by an aura of bright light. This light disorients creatures whose eyes are already overwhelmed, giving them mind-dulling hallucinations. Dazzled creatures in the aura are Stupefied 1, and Blinded creatures in the aura are Stupefied 2.</p>"},{"n":"Focused Flash","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","light","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet of the aglys targets the aglys with an attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The aglys reflects intense light off their staff and armor toward their assailant. The creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty on the triggering attack roll and is Dazzled until the end of its turn. The concealment from the dazzled condition applies to the triggering attack. If the attack misses, the triggering creature takes 4d6 persistent fire damage.</p><p>Effect: Focused Flash</p>"},{"n":"Shatter Control","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Aglyses are especially susceptible to powerful sound waves. When an aglys takes sonic damage, any creature affected by the aglys's Crusade, Paranoia, Subconscious Suggestion, or Subjugating Light can immediately attempt another Will save with a +2 circumstance bonus, using the new result only if it is better than the original result.</p><p>An aglys who takes sonic damage must also attempt a DC 45 Will save. On a failure, the aglys's dulling radiance aura and purging luminance ability are suppressed until the end of the aglys's next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Purging Luminance","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","light"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that is hit by one of the aglys's strikes is Dazzled for 1 round. On a critical hit, if the creature was temporarily immune to Subjugating Light, it is no longer temporarily immune.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Mind Sear","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","light","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The aglys forces their will upon everyone in a 30-foot emanation, dealing 20d6 mental damage (DC 45 basic Will save). A creature that fails the save is also Dazzled for 1 round, or Blinded for 1 round on a critical failure. The aglys can't use Mind Sear again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Subjugating Light","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","incapacitation","light","manipulate","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The aglys's manipulative light shines deep into a creature's mind. This has the effects of a 10th-rank Dominate spell (DC 45 Will save), except the maximum duration is 1 minute and the target is also Dazzled for the spell's duration. The target is temporarily immune to Subjugating Light for 10 minutes.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/FOd8ChzFup4GXt9N":{"lang":["Fey","Melodian"],"abilities":[{"n":"Fortissimo","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The creature with the lowest initiative ends their turn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> As the alvalek's internal music reaches a crescendo, the alvalek sings an ear-piercing high note, creating a shockwave that deals 2d6 sonic damage to all non-alvalek creatures within 10 feet. Each creature must attempt a DC 20 Fortitude save. If a creature is in the area of two or more Fortissimos, they attempt a single save with a –2 circumstance penalty.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Deafened for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is deafened for 1 minute and Stunned 1.</p>"},{"n":"Leading Step","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The alvalek dances forth to a song only they can hear and Steps up to 10 feet. If they have a creature Grabbed, they violently reposition that creature to another space in their reach with a dancing flourish, dealing the creature 5 piercing damage.</p>"},{"n":"Shifting Tempo","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["primal","time"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The alvalek has a creature Grabbed</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The alvalek taps their foot to a new rhythm, attempting to slow down or speed up the tempo. The grabbed creature can attempt a DC 21 Will save to negate the effect. If the save fails, the alvalek and the grabbed creature become either Slowed 1 or Quickened as time flows with the new tune; the extra action from quickened can only be used to Step or use Leading Step. The change in tempo persists until the grabbed condition ends or the alvalek uses Shifting Tempo again.</p>"},{"n":"Eager Partner","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An alvalek is not Immobilized when Grabbed by another creature of Medium size or smaller. They can treat the grabbing creature as being grabbed by them for the purposes of meeting the requirements for Leading Step and Shifting Tempo. An alvalek's nature forbids them from interrupting an ongoing dance; they can't attempt to Grab a creature that is already grappled.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Vpxo7NnWMRRHRrXu":{"lang":["Fey","can't speak any language"],"abilities":[{"n":"Foliage Body","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An amber bramble can Hide and Sneak in forests, even if it doesn't have cover.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Splash","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature hits the amber bramble with an attack that deals piercing, slashing, or bludgeoning damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bramble retaliates by flinging the sap from its injury on its assailant. The bramble makes a sap glob Strike against the creature. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the amber bramble's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Cloying Sap","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sap of an amber bramble rapidly hardens, restricting movement. Those exposed to the plant's cloying sap take a –10-foot circumstance penalty to their Speeds until they Escape it.</p>"},{"n":"Sap Toxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 18 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 1d4 poison damage and stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 1d4 poison damage and Stupefied 2 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Sap Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The amber bramble sprays a deluge of sap around itself in a 10-foot emanation. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 18 Reflex save to avoid the sap. On a failure, the creature is exposed to the amber bramble's cloying sap and sap toxin. On a critical failure, the sap covers the creature's face, restricting their breathing. Until they Escape from the cloying sap, they must hold their breath or begin suffocating.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/hyEtgjiuY2VUZbrD":{"lang":["Common"],"abilities":[{"n":"Protect the Scene","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet would use an action with the emotion trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The amphitwister detests interruptions to the show, whether they be Demoralizing hecklers or people spinning magic to take control of the narrative. The triggering creature must succeed at a DC 30 Will save or the triggering action is disrupted.</p>"},{"n":"Fashion Disaster","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The amphitwister envelops all creatures in its space in an array of comically mismatched clothing. All creatures in its space must attempt a DC 27 Reflex save to avoid being costumed.</p><p>Effect: Fashion Disaster</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes a –15-foot status penalty to their Speeds and a –2 circumstance penalty to Deception, Diplomacy, Intimidation, and Performance checks until they Escape the clothing.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is also Immobilized until they remove the clothing.</p>"},{"n":"Mirror Shards","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The swarm ejects a storm of mirror shards. All creatures in a 15-foot burst within 120 feet of the swarm take 4d6+9 piercing damage (DC 27 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Places, Please!","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The amphitwister's props arrange themselves, gathering into four adjacent squares. This reduces the swarm's size to Large but increases the damage of its Prop Barrage to 3d12. The swarm remains Large until it spends another action with the move trait to disperse to its original size.</p>"},{"n":"Prop Barrage","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Each foe in the swarm's space takes 3d8 bludgeoning damage (DC 30 basic Reflex).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/G6RBUSzmvCzEWpTc":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Empyrean","Melodian","Protean","Utopian"],"lore":[["Music Lore",19]],"gear":["Repair Toolkit","Unintelligible Sheet Music"],"notes":{"ac":"(25 when at 65 HP or fewer), hard core","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. auditory"},"abilities":[{"n":"Self-Invented","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An amplifighter's familiarity with their heavily modded chassis allows them spent one minute to Repair themselves (DC 26). Their proficiency rank in Crafting is master.</p>"},{"n":"Terrifying Performance","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The amplifighter can use Performance instead of Intimidation to Coerce or Demoralize. On a critical success to perform either of these actions, the target is also Deafened for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves Vs. Auditory","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Hard Core","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The amplifighter's tinkering has made them rigidly resilient, but their overclocked core is a bit unstable. When reduced to 65 Hit Points or fewer, the chassis protecting their core cracks. They lose their resistance to physical damage and their AC is reduced to 25. While their chassis is cracked, whenever they take physical damage, they deal 4d4 sonic damage to all creatures in a 10-foot emanation (DC 28 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Jarring Interruption","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature uses a concentrate action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Be it blaring horns for a casting mage or a celestial choir for a teleporting fiend: every amplifighter has a knack for making the wrong noise at the right moment. They attempt a melee Strike against the triggering creature; on a hit, the target loses the triggering action unless it succeeds at a DC 26 Will save. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the amplifighter's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Amp it Up!","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The amplifighter turns the volume of their loudspeakers up to eardrum-shattering levels. All creatures in a 30-foot emanation take 7d4 sonic damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save). Creatures that fail the saving throw are Deafened for 1 round (or for 1 minute on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/KemOBoo7qirkvu0B":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","Requian"],"lore":[["Midwifery Lore",7]],"gear":["Shortbow","Arrows (20)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Spirit Touch","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An amutu's Strikes affect incorporeal creatures as though etched with a <em>ghost touch</em> property rune and deal 1d6 void damage to living creatures or 1d6 vitality damage to undead.</p>"},{"n":"Ominous Hoot","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","divine","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The amutu lets loose a loud otherworldly hoot that terrifies their foes. Each creature in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a DC 18 Will save. Regardless of the result, creatures are temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Fleeing for 1 round and Frightened 3.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/DvqOmRtyzIlVvumY":{"notes":{"ac":"(18 when broken), construct armor"},"abilities":[{"n":"Construct Armor (Hardness 5)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Like normal objects, an animated orchestra has Hardness. This Hardness reduces any damage the swarm takes by an amount equal to the Hardness. Once an animated orchestra is reduced to fewer than half its Hit Points, or immediately upon being damaged by a critical hit, its construct armor breaks, removing the Hardness and reducing its Armor Class to 18.</p>"},{"n":"Woodwinds","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The animated orchestra is targeted by an attack and can see the attacker</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Woodwind instruments play a quick and frenzied melody, creating a swirling barrier of sound. The animated orchestra gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Brass","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The animated orchestra's brass instruments resonate with power and let loose a thunderous blast of sound dealing 3d10+5 sonic damage in a 30-foot cone (DC 19 basic Fortitude save). On a critical failure, the target is Deafened for 1 minute. The animated orchestra can't use Brass again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Percussion","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The animated orchestra unleashes a thunderous barrage of percussive strikes against each creature in its space, dealing 2d8 bludgeoning damage (DC 19 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Strings","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The animated orchestra's stringed instruments hum with magic as they weave a slicing melody into the air. The melody crescendos into a ferocious symphony of supernatural blades, dealing 2d6+5 slashing damage in a 10-foot burst within 120 feet (DC 19 basic Reflex save).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/AWNYprN4tWMiriAu":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Jyoti","Petran","Speak with animals, Speak with plants, Truespeech"],"notes":{"ac":"(33 when broken), pottery armor","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Pottery Armor (Hardness 15)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Each arahabaki is encased in pottery armor. Like normal objects, the pottery armor has Hardness. This Hardness reduces any damage the arahabaki takes by an amount equal to the Hardness. Once an arahabaki is reduced to less than half their maximum Hit Points, or immediately upon being damaged by a critical hit, their pottery armor breaks, they lose their immunities, and their Armor Class is reduced to 33. While the armor is broken, the radius of their healing aura decreases to 15 feet and their fly speed increases to 60 feet. The arahabaki can repair or reconstruct their pottery armor with 10 minutes of meditation.</p>"},{"n":"Healing Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. All allied creatures in the aura gain fast healing 5 and a +2 status bonus to all saves against poison and disease for as long as they remain in the aura. After any creature afflicted by a condition spends at least 1 minute within the aura, the aura attempts a counteract check against all afflictions affecting it with a +28 modifier, as an 8th-rank Cleanse Affliction. The aura can't attempt another counteract check against the same case of the affliction for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Protection","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature would attack one of the arahabaki's allies that is within the healing aura</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The arahabaki casts Sanctuary on the ally before the attack connects. The attacker must attempt a Will save against the <em>sanctuary</em> as normal.</p>"},{"n":"Purification","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>An arahabaki's Strikes deal 2d6 additional vitality damage to undead and 2d6 additional spirit damage to unholy creatures that aren't undead.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Statue","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Until the next time they act, the arahabaki appears to be a statue. They have an automatic result of 50 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as a statue.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/CQDGfdZwNisX21JR":{"lang":["Common","Luxan","Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"lore":[["Genealogy Lore",23]],"notes":{"speed":"wasteland walker"},"abilities":[{"n":"Crystalline Memory","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An archival monitor can use Genealogy Lore to Recall Knowledge on any topic related to the memories of an ancestor.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Flashing Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","light","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The archival monitor Strides. If they end that Stride adjacent to at least one other creature, they suddenly display their reflective frill in a blinding flash of light. Each adjacent creature must succeed at a DC 28 Will save or become Dazzled and Off-Guard for 1 round. The monitor then makes a Strike against one adjacent creature.</p>"},{"n":"Kaleidoscopic Cage","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate","fire","light","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The archival monitor creates an immobile, spherical cage of solidified light in a 30-foot radius centered around themselves. If the cage is created in a creature's square, the creature is repositioned to the nearest unoccupied square outside of the sphere; this is forced movement. The cage has an AC 10, Hardness 12, and 80 Hit Points, and it's immune to critical hits and precision damage. The cage sheds bright light in a 60-foot radius from its center (and dim light for the next 30 feet). Creatures that end of their turn inside of the cage take 2d6 fire damage (DC 28 basic Fortitude save). The cage lasts until the end of the archival monitor's next turn, but they can Sustain the cage for up to 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Solar Beam","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire","light"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The archival monitor is in bright light</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The archival monitor angles their reflective frill to focus ambient light into a 60-foot line. If the line hits a Kaleidoscopic Cage, it bounces off at an angle of the monitor's choice. All creatures that the beam passes through at least once take 11d6 fire damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). Creatures that critically fail become Blinded for 1 round. The archival monitor can't use Solar Beam again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Wasteland Walker","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The archival monitor ignores difficult terrain and uneven ground caused by rubble.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/qhVmX1JmdP5ydGg5":{"lang":["Common","Empyrean"],"abilities":[{"n":"Metallic Pair","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Every argentaurem is created alongside a partner, with one made of gold and the other made of silver. The gold one can make gold claws and gold jaws Strikes and use Growl, while the silver one can make silver claws and silver jaws Strikes and use Retrieve. While within 100 feet of each other, the pair can communicate telepathically. If the pair is more than 100 feet apart, they are both Sickened 1 and Drained 1 and can't remove these conditions in any way. While a pair of argentaurems is two level 8 creatures, each of which rolls its own initiative and has three actions per round, an argentaurem encountered without its partner is a level 7 creature.</p>"},{"n":"Share Life","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":["divine","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> An argentaurem and its partner are within 100 feet of each other</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The argentaurem and its partner's Hit Points both become equal to the average of their two totals, rounded down. The argentaurem and its partner can't use this ability again for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Share Mind","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The argentaurem and their partner must both roll a Will save, a Perception check, or an initiative roll</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> An argentaurem and its partner are within 100 feet of each other</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Both the argentaurem and its partner roll and use the higher of their two results.</p>"},{"n":"Expose Flank","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a pair of argentaurems are adjacent to the same creature, they are always flanking it, regardless of their positions.</p>"},{"n":"Growl","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gold argentaurem lets out a terrifying snarl. It attempts an Intimidation check to Demoralize all enemies within 30 feet. This Intimidation check doesn't take the –4 circumstance penalty for the argentaurem not speaking a language. As usual for Demoralize, affected enemies are then temporarily immune for 10 minutes.</p>"},{"n":"Throat Rip","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The gold argen-taurem's last action was a successful gold jaws Strike against a creature that the silver argentaurem has Grabbed in its silver jaws</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gold argentaurem rips out a chunk of the creature's throat. The creature takes 2d8+9 piercing damage (DC 26 Fortitude save). On a failure, until the creature receives healing, it must succeed at a DC 5 Flat before performing an action that requires speech or the action is lost.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/hrP4KOpUZuij6t7z":{"lang":["Common","Empyrean"],"abilities":[{"n":"Metallic Pair","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Every argentaurem is created alongside a partner, with one made of gold and the other made of silver. The gold one can make gold claws and gold jaws Strikes and use Growl, while the silver one can make silver claws and silver jaws Strikes and use Retrieve. While within 100 feet of each other, the pair can communicate telepathically. If the pair is more than 100 feet apart, they are both Sickened 1 and Drained 1 and can't remove these conditions in any way. While a pair of argentaurems is two level 8 creatures, each of which rolls its own initiative and has three actions per round, an argentaurem encountered without its partner is a level 7 creature.</p>"},{"n":"Share Life","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":["divine","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> An argentaurem and its partner are within 100 feet of each other</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The argentaurem and its partner's Hit Points both become equal to the average of their two totals, rounded down. The argentaurem and its partner can't use this ability again for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Share Mind","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The argentaurem and their partner must both roll a Will save, a Perception check, or an initiative roll</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> An argentaurem and its partner are within 100 feet of each other</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Both the argentaurem and its partner roll and use the higher of their two results.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Expose Flank","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a pair of argentaurems are adjacent to the same creature, they are always flanking it, regardless of their positions.</p>"},{"n":"Retrieve","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The silver argentaurem Strides once and then Leaps up to 20 feet in any direction (including vertically). If it ends this movement adjacent to a creature, it can attempt to Grapple that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Tear Wound","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The silver argentaurem's last action was a successful silver claws Strike against a creature that is taking persistent bleed damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The silver argentaurem digs its claws into the wound, pulling it open farther. The creature takes 2d6+8 piercing damage (DC 26 basic Fortitude save). On a failure, the amount of bleed damage it is taking increases by 1d6; this increase is not cumulative.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/wEW1Zqfje16Icnu1":{"lang":["Astral","Common","Thalassic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Quest Lore",19]],"abilities":[{"n":"Severed Strands","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever the astral flotsam takes slashing damage, they become Clumsy 1 until the end of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Psychic Vortex","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the astral flotsam hits with a wave crash Strike, the target must succeed at a DC 23 Will save or become Stupefied 1 (Stupefied 2 on a critical failure). This condition lasts until the target hits the astral flotsam with an attack roll, the astral flotsam fails a saving throw against a spell cast by the target, or 1 minute passes, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Drown In Thought","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The astral flotsam sends a thoughtform to overwhelm all creatures in a 30-foot cone with an onslaught of their thoughts. All creatures in the area take 6d6 mental damage (DC 25 Will save). The astral flotsam can't use Drown in Thought again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is Off-Guard until the end of its next turn.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is off-guard for 1 minute. The target can attempt a new DC 25 Will save at the end of each of its turns to end this condition early.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature takes double damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/uM7DcDqwVGzX2YlW":{"abilities":[{"n":"Discordant Echo","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The attunement arsenal takes damage from a Strike with a metal weapon or an unarmed attack that is made of metal</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each creature in a 10-foot emanation takes 4d6 sonic damage (DC 30 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Sonic Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Any time an attunement arsenal would be affected by an effect with the sonic trait, it loses any slowed condition it has and gains HP equal to half the damage the spell would have dealt. If the arsenal starts its turn in an area that deals sonic damage, it gains 2d8 healing HP. It doesn't gain these benefits from its own abilities.</p>"},{"n":"Vulnerable to Teleportation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a spell with the teleportation trait is cast within 10 feet of the attunement arsenal, the attunement arsenal is teleported up to 10 feet in a direction of the caster's choice and loses its resistance to physical damage for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Spatial Shift","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The attunement arsenal's last action was a successful syncopated slam Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The attunement arsenal teleports to an open space within 10 feet of the target of its Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Disorienting Relocation","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The attunement arsenal's teleportation beam erratically relocates its targets. Due to the flaws in the foci that make up the arsenal's body, this teleportation is unsteady, making it stomach-churning to endure. A creature hit by a teleportation beam Strike must attempt a DC 33 Fortitude save. This teleportation is forced movement. It can move targets into hazardous spaces, but it can't place them in occupied spaces or inside of a solid wall; if it would otherwise do so, it instead moves the target as far as it can in its randomly selected direction.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature can teleport 5 feet in a direction of its choice.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature teleports 5 feet in a random direction.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature teleports 15 feet in a random direction and is Sickened 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature teleports 30 feet in a random direction and is Sickened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Rending Warp","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","sonic","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The attunement arsenal creates a resounding clang with its fists, activating the planar-hopping items that make up its form and pulling nearby creatures into unstable portals. All creatures in a 20-foot emanation take 5d8 sonic damage (DC 33 basic Reflex save). Creatures that critically fail are also teleported to an open space that is 10 feet closer to the attunement arsenal, or adjacent to the arsenal if they were less than 15 feet away; this is forced movement.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/izlYqIkyX7xkjMJf":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Melodian","Muan","Requian","Sussuran"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Life from Death","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["healing","primal","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature within 30 feet dies</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The dying creature is level 2 or higher</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The autumnal is strengthened by the fleeting life essence, gaining 5 temporary Hit Points that last for 1 minute.</p><p>Effect: Life from Death</p>"},{"n":"Whirling Cloak","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Leaves swirl about the autumnal whenever they use a move action to move at least 5 feet, granting them concealment until the end of their current turn.</p>"},{"n":"Dance of Leaves","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The autumnal Strides or Flies twice, making a leaf blade Strike against a creature at any time during the movement.</p>"},{"n":"Mark for Reaping","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","curse","death","misfortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The autumnal singles out a creature within 60 feet for reaping. A mark of a scythe appears on the creature's body, which must then roll a DC 20 Fortitude save to determine the mark's duration. While the mark lasts, any autumnal who Strikes the marked creature does an additional 1d4 precision damage. This damage is void if the marked creature is living, or vitality if they are undead. In addition, if the marked creature is living, it must roll twice and take the lower result on any recovery checks to reduce its dying condition. The mark disappears automatically if the autumnal uses Mark for Reaping on another creature or if the autumnal dies.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The mark disappears immediately.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The mark lasts for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The mark lasts for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The mark lasts for 10 minutes.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/5bDdx5eJRbuMXjrp":{"abilities":[{"n":"Stormglide","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An azappus seed can navigate even the most perilous gusts with ease. It does not treat wind as difficult terrain or need to Maneuver in Flight in high winds.</p>"},{"n":"Superstorm Aura","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["air","aura","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. Powerful winds buffet and propel the azappus seed. The air within the aura is difficult terrain for flying creatures that do not have the air trait. Creatures starting their turn in the aura that are not Grabbed by the azappus seed must attempt a DC 35 Fortitude save. Flying creatures that fail are pushed just outside of the aura, while creatures standing on the ground or another solid surface are knocked Prone.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Greater Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>3d12+7 bludgeoning, DC 37 basic Fortitude</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC. A creature that fails this save falls Unconscious, and a creature that succeeds is then temporarily immune to falling unconscious from Greater Constrict for 1 minute.</p></p>"},{"n":"Crushing Gale","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["air","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The azappus seed generates a cylinder of tornado-force winds within 60 feet that blow directly down toward the ground, affecting all creatures in the area except itself. The cylinder has a 25-foot radius and is 100 feet tall. The cylinder sends airborne creatures careening toward the ground. Flying creatures in the area that fail a DC 37 Reflex save are launched toward the ground in a bubble of air, taking 4d6 untyped damage as they land; they are knocked Prone on a critical failure. If the cylinder includes the ground, all creatures and unattended objects on the ground then take 15d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 37 basic Fortitude save). The azappus seed can't use Crushing Gale for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Lightning Storm","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The azappus seed fills the air around it with devastating arcs of lightning. All creatures in a 30-foot emanation take 4d12 electricity damage (DC 37 basic Reflex save). Creatures that fail the save are Shocked.</p>"},{"n":"Thunderpeal","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The azappus seed's last action was Lightning Storm</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A deafening roar of thunder emanates from the azappus seed, dealing 5d6 sonic damage to each creature in a 60-foot emanation (DC 37 basic Fortitude save). Creatures within the superstorm aura that fail are Deafened for 1 minute, or for 24 hours on a critical failure.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/MRn81FXBaF5wCvDM":{"lang":["Common","can't speak any language"],"lore":[["Magic Item Lore",7]],"abilities":[{"n":"Magic Item Lore","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>This skill pertains to magic items, both knowing about what types of magic exist and Identifying Magic to determine the properties of magic items.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Inject Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature invests a curseling that is using item mimicry, the curseling injects the creature with its egg-laden venom. The creature must attempt a DC 16 Fortitude save. The creature only notices the injection on a critical success.</p><p><strong>Curseling Venom</strong> (curse, mental, poison)</p><p><strong>Onset</strong> 1 day</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> The curseling establishes a mystical bond to its wearer. The wearer becomes unwilling to remove the item, even during circumstances like bathing or sleeping where keeping the item on is unusual. Removing the item forcefully requires a successful Athletics check against the higher of the curseling's Fortitude DC and the wearer's Fortitude DC and deals 1d8 persistent bleed damage to the wearer. Removing the curseling at this stage breaks the curse. (1 week)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> As stage 1, but removing the curseling no longer breaks the curse. It continues to take up an invested item slot and can choose to return to the wearer 24 hours later. The wearer develops a compulsion to hoard metal. (1 week)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> The creature is compelled to gather its metal hoard and then seek out a fire to fall asleep next to. If it falls asleep next to a fire, its body explodes in flames and juvenile curselings emerge from its corpse (1 week).</p>"},{"n":"Item Mimicry","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The curseling takes the form of a magic item. It can be worn and invested, granting the item's usual benefits. As long as the curseling remains perfectly still, its identity is difficult to discern. Using Identify Magic to recognize a curseling requires a critical success. By default, a beastmaster's curseling takes the form of its own bespoke magic item called a <em>beastmaster's helm</em>.</p><p>A <em>beastmaster's helm</em> appears to be an uncommon primal invested 4th-level item with — Bulk. While wearing this helm on its head, a creature gains a +1 item bonus to Nature checks, which increases to +2 for Nature checks to Command an Animal, as well as a +1 circumstance bonus to Initiative rolls. The wearer can also use Animal Speech once per hour.</p><p><strong>Animal Speech</strong> 2 (concentrate, manipulate, primal)</p><p>The wearer can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with animals for 1 minute.</p><p>By spending 1 week reshaping its form, the beastmaster's curseling can reforge itself into the cursed version of a common worn and invested magic item of level 4 or lower that grants a +1 item bonus to a skill, or back from one of these forms into its <em>beastmaster's helm</em> form.</p>"},{"n":"Retreat into Shell","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The curseling pulls its body into its protective item shell. It gains Hardness 3, which lasts until it spends an action with the move or attack trait.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/nLH70MUha0HBFJAD":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Melodian"],"abilities":[{"n":"Friend To All","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>By default, all creatures are considered allies to the beat hopper for the composition spells. A creature can attempt a DC 22 Will save at the start of its turn to avoid being treated as the beat hopper's ally for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Natural Metronome","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The beat hopper is always moving their body to a beat. If they can't do so for whatever reason (such as by being Immobilized or Paralyzed), they are Sickened 1 until they can follow the beat again.</p>"},{"n":"Resonant Tempo","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The tempo of the beat hopper's composition spells resonates profoundly through the bodies of those who hear them, generating the following additional effects.</p><ul><li><strong>Courageous Anthem</strong> This inspiring performance helps steady the hearts and bodies of those who hear it. In addition to its normal effects, creatures affected by this performance are unaffected by the Quickened and slowed conditions, and they are also unaffected by both status bonuses and status penalties to their Speeds.</li><li><strong>Rallying Anthem</strong> Creatures affected by this gradually building performance focus so intently on preparations to shore up their defenses that they lose some of their offensive power. In addition to its normal effects, hey take a –10-foot status penalty to their Speeds and a –1 status penalty to attack rolls.</li><li><strong>Triple Time</strong> Creatures affected by this frantic performance are quickened, in addition to the performance's normal effects. They can only use this extra action to Stride their full Speed (if they want to go somewhere nearby, they can do so by taking a circuitous path or circling back).</li></ul>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/MxfZ3ij71GSle8RC":{"abilities":[{"n":"Camouflage","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The blood fern can Hide in natural forest or grassland environments even if it doesn't have cover.</p>"},{"n":"Toxic Burst","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","poison","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature bites into the blood fern (such as by making a successful jaws Strike)</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The poisonous fruit at the center of the blood fern explodes in a burst of toxic nectar. All creatures in a 20-foot emanation take 3d6 poison plus 3d6 void damage (DC 32 basic Fortitude save). The blood fern can't use Toxic Burst again until the fruit regrows, a process that takes about 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Toxic Finale","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a blood fern is destroyed while its fruit is still intact, the fruit automatically explodes. This has the effects of Toxic Burst.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Draining Roots","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The strong roots of the blood fern dig in search of fresh blood. At the end of the blood fern's turn, all creatures Grabbed by the blood fern take 3d6 void damage (DC 29 basic Fortitude save). Undead grabbed by the blood fern instead take 3d6 force damage, as the plant leeches void energy from their bodies. The blood fern can maintain a grapple with up to four creatures with its roots.</p>"},{"n":"Uproot","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The blood fern uproots itself and pounces atop its prey, crushing them beneath its strong roots. The fern drops all grappled creatures, then Leaps 10 feet into an area that contains at least one creature. Each creature in the area where the blood fern lands takes 4d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 29 basic Reflex save). The blood fern then immediately attempts Athletics checks to grapple up to four creatures that failed the Reflex save; these attempts neither apply nor count toward the blood fern's multiple attack penalty. All creatures in the area are then moved in the closest unoccupied square adjacent to the blood fern; this is forced movement.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/IT3gZsPrpSKbLaBB":{"lang":["Fey"],"abilities":[{"n":"Bouncy","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy critically fails a Strike against the bolbalos</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The bolbalos chooses a target within reach or range of the triggering attack, using themselves as the origin of the attack. The attacker then rerolls the attack against the new target.</p>"},{"n":"Curious Nature","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Bolbaloses are intrinsically curious and trusting of others. During the first round of combat, the bolbalos is Off-Guard until they have acted. If the penalty to AC from being off-guard causes them to take damage, they are Quickened for 1 round. They can use this extra action only to Stride or Step.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Push","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Improved Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"},{"n":"Sticky Slime","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A Large or smaller creature hit by the bolbalos's red slime is covered by quickly hardening goo and must attempt a DC 25 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes a –10 foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds for 1 round or until it Escapes.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, and the creature is Sickened 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Immobilized for 1 round or until it Escapes and is sickened 1.</p>"},{"n":"Trample","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Medium or smaller, belly, DC 28 basic Reflex. A creature that critically fails the saving throw is knocked Prone.</p><hr><p><p>The monster Strides up to double its Speed and can move through the spaces of creatures of the listed size, Trampling each creature whose space it enters. The monster can attempt to Trample the same creature only once in a single use of Trample. The monster deals the damage of the listed Strike, but trampled creatures can attempt a basic Reflex save at the listed DC (no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, double damage on a critical failure).</p></p>"},{"n":"Ponderous Push","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Bolbaloses thoroughly enjoy moving things around with their bellies. They can Shove creatures using only their bellies, and they can Shove creatures up to two sizes larger than themselves.</p>"},{"n":"Blundering Slam","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The bolbalos spins around, haphazardly slamming any enemies surrounding them. They make a belly Strike against each enemy within reach. These attacks count toward their multiple attack penalty, but their multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after all the attacks. After using Blundering Slam, the bolbalos becomes Stunned 1 and can't use this ability again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/DWWWNXYafjswVMIL":{"lang":["Petran","Voltan"],"notes":{"speed":"earth glide"},"abilities":[{"n":"Glow","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","light"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. The lightning that makes up a boltspiker's body emits bright light. The boltspiker can spend one action to shroud the glow within their crystals, after which the aura remains suppressed until they spend one action to reactivate it.</p>"},{"n":"Electrical Discharge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature touches the boltspiker or Strikes them with a metal weapon in melee</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Electricity surges into the triggering creature, dealing 2d12 electricity damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Boltspike","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a boltspiker hits a creature with a crystal lance Strike, they attempt to stake them to the ground. The target must attempt a DC 22 Fortitude save. A creature that fails a check to Escape from the spike takes 1d6 electricity damage.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 1d6 electricity damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes 1d6 persistent electricity damage and takes a –10 foot status penalty to their Speeds until they Escape.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes 1d6 persistent electricity damage and becomes Immobilized until they Escape.</p>"},{"n":"Glide Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The boltspiker's crystals gather power as they move through earthen material. The boltspiker Burrows at least 10 feet and then attempts a lightning whip Strike. If the Strike hits, it deals an additional 1d12 electricity damage.</p>"},{"n":"Ride the Lightning","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The boltspiker generates and then rides a powerful electric current. They move up to 150 feet in a straight line through the air without triggering reactions. If they are above the ground at the end of this movement, they fall safely to the ground at the end of their turn.</p>"},{"n":"Earth Glide","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The boltspiker can Burrow through any earthen matter, including rock, as well as unworked metal and gemstone deposits. When they do so, the boltspiker moves at their full burrow Speed, leaving no tunnels or signs of their passing.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/cIJGmU6O0zRfhzos":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Any four additional languages"],"lore":[["Library Lore",17]],"abilities":[{"n":"Internal Library","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The book beast has eaten tomes on a wide variety of subjects over the course of their lifetime. They can roll a Library Lore check at a –2 penalty in place of any check to Recall Knowledge.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Book Form","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The book beast changes its appearance into that of a Tiny book or reverts their appearance back to their true form. When taking the form of a book, the book beast can choose what their cover looks like as well as the text and illustrations that appear on each page. If the content includes complex diagrams or illustrations, the book beast must roll a Crafting check to determine their quality. In addition to replicating non-magical books, a book beast can take the form of a spellbook that contains all of the spontaneous spells they can cast. The book beast can't make Strikes in its Book Form.</p>"},{"n":"Digestive Synthesis","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The book beast is adjacent to an unattended book, scroll, or other written work</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The book beast spends 1 minute to physically devour the written work, absorbing the knowledge held within as if it had read the entire text. If the writing contains knowledge of specific arcane spells, such as a wizard's spellbook or a scroll, the book beast can freely retrain any number of their spontaneous spells into arcane spells of the same rank from the devoured source.</p>"},{"n":"Sticky Page","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a book beast successfully Grabs a creature larger than themselves with their jaws, they exude bookbinding glue from their mouth and then attach their cover to that creature. The Grabbed creature is not Immobilized, but if it moves, the book beast moves with it. While the book beast is attached, the book beast is Off-Guard and the attached creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to its saving throws against the book beast's spells. If the attached creature is Medium or smaller, it also takes a –5-foot status penalty to its Speeds.</p><p>Effect: Sticky Page</p>"},{"n":"Ordinary Book","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The book beast is in its Book Form</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Until the book beast acts, they resemble an inanimate book. They have an automatic result of 30 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as a book.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/zRZ4Rp9CgVyLDfSw":{"lang":["Aetheran","Aklo","Common"],"abilities":[{"n":"Cranium Shell","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first time the braincase would be reduced to 0 HP, they are reduced to 1 HP instead as the shell shatters, exposing their brain. The shell remains broken until the braincase is restored to full HP. While their brain is exposed, any damage the braincase takes kills them regardless of their current HP.</p>"},{"n":"Don't You Dare!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The braincase is the target of a ranged attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The braincase attempts to Demoralize the attacking creature. This ignores any temporary immunity the creature has to Demoralize attempts from the braincase and doesn't make them temporarily immune to Demoralize.</p>"},{"n":"Obstructing Palm","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 20 feet moves closer to the braincase</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The braincase is in Six Palms Stance</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The braincase makes a force palm Strike against the creature. If the Strike critically hits, the creature is also knocked Prone, interrupting the movement. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the braincase's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Force Bubble","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["force","manipulate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The braincase molds an opaque bubble of magical force around a creature within 60 feet (DC 33 Reflex negates). On a failed save, the creature is Immobilized and Blinded until the bubble is popped (AC 10, Hardness 5, HP 30, BT 15); the bubble breaks automatically after 1 minute. Bubbles are immune to critical hits and precision damage. At the end of the braincase's turn, they can affect each active force bubble, moving it up to 30 feet, popping it, or both.</p>"},{"n":"Six Palms Stance","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","force","occult","stance"],"f":"","d":"<p>The braincase creates a massive, six-armed torso from magical force. Theirs size increases to Gargantuan, and they can use their force palm Strike and Obstructing Palm reaction. They gain an additional reaction each round, but their second reaction must be used for a different action than their first reaction. The stance breaks if the braincase Casts a Spell.</p>"},{"n":"Telekinetic Shove","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The braincase's last action was a successful telekinetic beam Strike against a creature of size Huge or smaller</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The braincase attempts to push the creature away, rolling a spell attack roll against the creature's Fortitude DC. On a success, the creature is pushed back 20 feet (40 feet on a critical success). This attack roll neither applies nor counts toward the braincase's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Telekinetic Trip","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The braincase's last action was a successful force palm Strike against a creature of size Huge or smaller</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The braincase attempts to Trip the creature, using their spell attack modifier in place of their Athletics modifier. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the braincase's multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Hu4oKiWwfFaTfExj":{"lang":["Fey","can't speak, Speak with animals"],"abilities":[{"n":"Kaleidoscopic Coat","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The cabyar can change the colorful patterns of their fur to better blend in with their surroundings, allowing them to Hide in areas of dim or bright light even when they don't have cover.</p>"},{"n":"Practiced Diver","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The cabyar can hold their breath for up to 5 minutes before they begin to drown.</p>"},{"n":"Flash of Colors","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["occult","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The cabyar is targeted by an attack, and they can see the attacker</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cabyar swiftly flashes the multi-colored patterns of their fur, gaining concealment against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Radiance","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The cabyar is practiced at shining their light beams directly into their target's eyes. A creature hit by a light beam Strike must succeed at a DC 20 Fortitude save or be Dazzled for 1 round. On a critical failure, or if the creature was already dazzled, it is instead Blinded for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Entrancing Pelt","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","mental","occult","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The cabyar twirls around, causing light to dance through its shimmering pelt. Creatures in a 20-foot emanation must attempt a DC 22 Will save. Once a creature attempts this Will save, it is immune to any cabyar's Entrancing Pelt for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Off-Guard for one round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Dazzled and off-guard for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled and off-guard for 1 round and Stunned 1.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Jni4fknPPMHgW0u9":{"lang":["Common","Fey"],"abilities":[{"n":"Curious Aroma","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","mental","olfactory","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet. A creature entering or starting its turn in the cactopie's aura must succeed at a DC 19 Will save or become Confused for 1 round. A creature who succeeds at the save becomes temporarily immune to curious aroma for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Bed of Spines","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The cactopie has a creature Grabbed in one of their roots</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cactopie attempts to pull the creature in and smash it against their spiny body. The creature attempts a DC 22 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is moved to a square adjacent to the cactopie of the cactopie's choice. This is forced movement.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, but the creature also takes 2d4+2 piercing damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As success, but the creature also takes 4d4+4 piercing damage and 1d6 persistent bleed damage.</p>"},{"n":"Pollen Burst","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The cactopie unleashes a cloud of toxic pollen from their flower in a 20-foot emanation. Each creature in the area must attempt a DC 19 Will save. Creatures that are frightened from Pollen Burst gain weakness to piercing 5 for as long as they remain frightened. The cactopie can't use Pollen Burst again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 3.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/NbIYYVxOBB3Zq3Oj":{"lang":["Common","Sakvroth"],"lore":[["Engineering Lore",22]],"gear":["Thieves' Toolkit (Infiltrator)","Shortsword","Warhammer"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity gremlin deals an additional 3d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Deceptive Shuffle","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity gremlin Strides up to half their Speed and attempts a Feint, in either order.</p>"},{"n":"Wrecking Blows","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity gremlin makes two warhammer Strikes against a wall, ceiling, or floor in reach. The object's Hardness is halved for the purpose of determining the damage from these Strikes, and it applies only once after combining the damage from both Strikes. If the calamity gremlin brings a wall's Hit Points to zero, they can take a free Step or Stride through the breach.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity gremlin can take on the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid. This doesn't change their Speed or their attack and damage modifiers with their Strikes, but it might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Calamity","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["curse","primal"],"f":"once per month","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per month</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The calamity gremlin spends 8 hours laying a terrible curse upon area with a radius of up to 100 feet. The curse triggers between one day and one year later at a time set during its creation and results in some kind of violent misfortune, such as an exploding cannon or a collapsing bridge. The exact effects are up to the GM. Typically, the curse creates a hazard of up to 7th level. If the calamity gremlin is interrupted while laying the curse, their magic is still expended, preventing them from using calamity again for 1 month. A calamity gremlin can only have one calamity active at a time; creating a new calamity automatically ends the curse on any previously affected location. A calamity gremlin who appears to perish as a result of their own calamity curse emerges 2d4 days later, having somehow survived.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/6V6xBT4YoprzwmQe":{"abilities":[{"n":"Grabbing Trunk","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A Medium or smaller creature hit by the calliophant's trunk is Grabbed. When the calliophant moves, it can bring the grabbed creature along with it, repositioning the creature to any square within its reach. This is forced movement.</p>"},{"n":"Crank the Heat","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The calliophant has at least 1 gallon in its water reservoir</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The calliophant expends 1 gallon of water from its water reservoir to create steam. Until the start of the calliophant's next turn, creatures that hit it with an unarmed attack or a melee attack or who otherwise touch it take 3d6 fire damage. A Grabbed creature takes this damage once at the start of that creature's turn.</p>"},{"n":"Drink Water","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calliophant's uses its trunk to siphon up to two gallons of water from a source within fifteen feet into its water reservoir.</p>"},{"n":"Steam Scream","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","sonic","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The calliophant has at least 1 gallon in its water reservoir per action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The calliophant expends 1 gallon of water per action to produce an ear-splitting steam-powered tune, dealing sonic damage to all creatures in an emanation (DC 30 basic Fortitude save). The radius of the emanation and amount of sonic damage depend upon the number of actions spent.</p><p>1 5d6 sonic damage in a 5-foot emanation</p><p>2 10d6 sonic damage in a 15-foot emanation</p><p>3 15d6 sonic damage in a 30-foot emanation</p>"},{"n":"Trample","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p> Large or smaller, foot, DC 30 basic Reflex</p><hr><p><p>The monster Strides up to double its Speed and can move through the spaces of creatures of the listed size, Trampling each creature whose space it enters. The monster can attempt to Trample the same creature only once in a single use of Trample. The monster deals the damage of the listed Strike, but trampled creatures can attempt a basic Reflex save at the listed DC (no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, double damage on a critical failure).</p></p>"},{"n":"Water Reservoir","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calliophant holds a reservoir of water that it can turn to steam to power some of its abilities. When full, the reservoir holds 6 gallons of water.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/emlbedHMQ2JOFeZh":{"lang":["Fey","Petran","Thalassic"],"lore":[["River Lore",18]],"notes":{"speed":"earth glide"},"abilities":[{"n":"Allied Waters","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Water doesn't impair a cascadian's vision. They ignore concealment from water.</p>"},{"n":"Riparian","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When not touching water or solid ground, the cascadian is Slowed 1 and can't use reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Surge Back","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["primal","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 10 feet hits the cascadian with a melee Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cascadian's waters channel some of the momentum of the attack back on the attacker, who must attempt a DC 26 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The attacker is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The attacker takes an amount of bludgeoning damage equal to half of the damage of the triggering Strike.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the cascadian only takes half damage from the triggering Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Attune With Nature","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","manipulate","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The cascadian is in contact with both water and solid ground</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cascadian enhances their attunement to the world around them. While attuned, they are Immobilized, but they gain lifesense 60 feet, and the ranges of their tremorsense and wavesense increase to 200 feet. The attunement remains active until the cascadian Dismisses it.</p>"},{"n":"Share Enlightenment","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","incapacitation","manipulate","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The cascadian is Attuned with Nature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cascadian shares their attunement all creatures within 30 feet (DC 26 Will save negates). A willing creature can choose to receive the results of a failure.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Immobilized for 1 round and gains tremorsense (imprecise) 30 feet and wavesense (imprecise) 30 feet while it is immobilized.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Paralyzed for 1 round, and gains tremorsense (imprecise) 60 feet and wavesense (imprecise) 60 feet while it is paralyzed.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the paralysis lasts for 4 rounds. The creature can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns to reduce the remaining duration by 1 round, or end it entirely on a critical success.</p>"},{"n":"Earth Glide","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Cascadian can Burrow through dirt and stone at their full burrow Speed, leaving no tunnels or signs of their passing.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ApOANbPfkpqEnY1A":{"lang":["Common cant speak any language"],"abilities":[{"n":"Thoughtsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The cathartic slime senses all non-mindless creatures at the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Condensed Form","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The cathartic slime is in its dispersed form</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cathartic slime condenses into a single blob on the edge of the body of water.</p>"},{"n":"Dispersed Form","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The cathartic slime is in its condensed form and is beside or inside a body of water</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cathartic slime disperses itself into the body of water, expanding its size to a maximum of a 20 foot cube. It can't expand into occupied squares. While in its dispersed form, the cathartic slime loses soften mind but gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Athletics checks to Grab and a +4 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks while it remains in the body of water. It also gains resistance 5 to bludgeoning and weakness 5 to electricity.</p>"},{"n":"Emotional Drain","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A creature is Grabbed by the cathartic slime or has ingested water infested by the cathartic slime in its dispersed form</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cathartic slime attempts to trap a creature in an emotional turmoil. The creature must attempt a DC 22 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Emotional Drain for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is Slowed 1 for up to 1 minute. It can attempt a DC 22 Will save at the end of each of its turns to end the condition.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is Paralyzed for up to 1 minute. It can attempt a DC 22 Will save at the end of each of its turns to end the condition.</p>"},{"n":"Soften Mind","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by the cathartic slime's pseudopod or slime glob Strike must succeed at a DC 19 Will save or be Stupefied 1 for 1 round (or 1 minute on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/DLmtdaeJCQFL8STN":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Thalassic"],"lore":[["Sailing Lore",24]],"notes":{"hp":"life shell"},"abilities":[{"n":"Fascinated by Music","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Musical performances can enthrall a ceasg, at least until the performer shows signs of hostility. A creature can attempt a Performance check to Perform against the ceasg's Will DC.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The ceasg is Fascinated by the performer for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The ceasg is fascinated by the performer for 3 rounds.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The ceasg is temporarily immune to the performer's attempts to fascinate them with a Performance for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, and the ceasg can use a reaction to Stride or Swim toward the performer. If this movement places the performer within their reach, they can make a jaws Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Life Shell","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ceasg keeps their soul in a magical container made from a hollow piece of organic material such as an egg, seashell, or skull. The shell has Hardness 10 and 40 Hit Points. Destroying the shell deals 6d10 mental damage to the ceasg (DC 35 basic Will save). If the ceasg is slain while the shell is intact, the ceasg and any creatures they have swallowed dissolve into water and reform at the location of the life shell in 1d8 days. A swallowed creature is not dead during this time and can't be restored to life.</p>"},{"n":"Protect Hostage","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the ceasg's stomach is reduced to 0 Hit Points or would die of suffocation</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature is Unconscious but not dying. It doesn't take further damage from the ceasg's Swallow Whole, and it doesn't need to breathe.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ceasg changes into a Medium humanoid. In this form, they lose their swim speed and their land speed changes to 25 feet. They lose their tail and jaws Strikes and gain a fist Strike that deals the same amount of bludgeoning damage as the tail Strike.</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fulfill Desire","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ceasg can duplicate any 6th-rank spell or produce an effect of similar scope, but only in response to the request of a non-fey creature. A creature whose desire is granted three times can never again benefit from that particular ceasg's Fulfill Desire.</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Large, 3d10+10 bludgeoning, Rupture 34</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/5DNeLNpWXjGk1Vpv":{"lang":["Common","Cryan","Fey","Luxan","Speak with animals"],"notes":{"per":"snow vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Snow Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Snow doesn't impair the chionad's vision; they ignore concealment from snowfall.</p>"},{"n":"Beacon Song","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The chionad's Enthrall innate spell has a range of 1,200 feet. For every 120 feet beyond the initial 120 feet, the save DC decreases by 2.</p>"},{"n":"Mountain Dependent","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A chionad is mystically bonded to a single cold peak. If they descend below the snow line or fly more than 300 feet from the mountain, they become Drained 1, increasing the value by 1 for each missed day and reducing by 1 only when they ascend above the snowline. A chionad can perform a 24-hour ritual to bond to a new location.</p>"},{"n":"Radiant Burst","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["light","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that takes damage from a northern light Strike must succeed at a DC 26 Fortitude save or be Dazzled for 1 round (or Blinded for 1 round on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Aurora","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate","polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The chionad transforms into a wall of shimmering green, blue and violet light that is 10 feet high and up to 20 feet long. These squares do not need to be in a straight line, but the aurora can't manifest into occupied squares. While in aurora form, the chionad gains resistance 8 to physical damage and is immune to precision damage. They can't cast spells, activate items, or use actions that have the attack or manipulate trait. The aurora sheds dim light in a 20-foot emanation. Creatures, objects, and magic can pass through the aurora. Foes that pass through the aurora take 4d8 cold damage (DC 26 basic Reflex). The aurora provides concealment on attacks from the chionad's foes that pass through it, but does not hinder the attacks of the chionad's allies. The chionad remains in aurora form until they Dismiss this effect, after which they can't transform into an aurora again for 1 hour.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/DU2WvoIscz8H8BY0":{"lang":["Common","Cryan","Draconic","Empyrean","Fey","Luxan","Speak with animals"],"notes":{"per":"snow vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Snow Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Snow doesn't impair the chionad's vision; they ignore concealment from snowfall.</p>"},{"n":"Tied to the Land","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A chionad queen is intrinsically tied to a specific region, such as a glacier or a mountain range. This otherwise functions as the standard nymph queen tied to the land ability.</p><hr><p>A nymph queen is intrinsically tied to a specific region. As long as the queen is healthy, the environment is exceptionally resilient, allowing the nymph queen to automatically attempt to counteract any spell that would harm the environment (such as the Blight ritual), using her spell DC with a counteract rank equal to the highest-rank druid spell she can cast.</p><p>When the nymph queen becomes physically or psychologically unhealthy, however, her warded region eventually becomes twisted or unhealthy as well. In that case, restoring the nymph queen swiftly heals the entire region.</p>"},{"n":"Beacon Song","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The chionad's Enthrall innate spell has a range of 1,200 feet. For every 120 feet beyond the initial 120 feet, the save DC decreases by 2.</p>"},{"n":"Nymph's Beauty","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","incapacitation","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. DC 34 Will save. On a failed save, the creature is Dazzled and Off-Guard for 1 minute. A chionad queen's aura is filled with a soft rainbow of colors that shed dim light; she can suppress this additional light as a free action.</p>"},{"n":"Aurora","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate","polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The chionad transforms into a wall of shimmering green, blue and violet light that is 10 feet high and up to 20 feet long. These squares do not need to be in a straight line, but the aurora can't manifest into occupied squares. While in aurora form, the chionad gains resistance 8 to physical damage and is immune to precision damage. They can't cast spells, activate items, or use actions that have the attack or manipulate trait. The aurora sheds dim light in a 100-foot emanation. Creatures, objects, and magic can pass through the aurora. Foes that pass through the aurora take 10d8 cold damage (DC 38 basic Reflex). The aurora provides concealment on attacks from the chionad's foes that pass through it, but does not hinder the attacks of the chionad's allies. The chionad remains in aurora form until they Dismiss this effect, after which they can't transform into an aurora again for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Radiant Burst","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["light","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that takes damage from a northern light Strike must succeed at a DC 38 Fortitude save or be Dazzled for 1 round (or Blinded for 1 round on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Inspiration","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nymph queen inspires a single intelligent creature by giving that creature a token of her favor, typically a lock of her hair, though it can be some other significant object as well. As long as the creature carries her token and remains in good standing with her, the creature gains a +1 status bonus to all Crafting checks, Performance checks, and Will saves.</p>\n<p>If the nymph grants her token to a bard, and she's the bard's muse, the queen chooses one additional benefit granted by her token: a +1 status bonus to all Lore checks, a +2 status bonus to Performance checks when determining the effects of compositions, a +4 status bonus to untrained skill checks, or a +2 status bonus to Will saves against fey.</p>\n<p>Effect: Nymph Queen's Inspiration</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Nymph queens can transform between their original form, which looks much like a typical nymph of their kind, and any Small or Medium humanoid form, typically choosing a more humanoid-looking version of their natural form.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Focus Beauty","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","incapacitation","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The chionad queen focuses her beauty upon a target, who must attempt a save against her nymph's beauty aura. A chionad queen can Focus Beauty on a given creature only once per turn. On a failed save, if the target was already affected by the chionad queen's beauty, it's Blinded until its sight is restored via sound body or similar effect. The chionad queen can Dismiss this effect.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/vS7bq6QETpbbkpl5":{"lang":["Common","Cryan","Fey","Speak with animals"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Frightful Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet DC 26 Will</p><hr><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fateful Impact","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the chionad shadow hits a creature with their claw or prismatic shadow Strike, the creature must attempt a DC 26 Fortitude save. Whatever the result, the creature is temporarily immune to the same chionad shadow's fateful impact for 24 hours.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Drained 1 for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Doomed 1 and drained 1 for 1 hour.</p>"},{"n":"Instill Loneliness","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The chionad shadow unleashes their inner darkness and briefly becomes a vision of loss and futility. All creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 26 Will save. Creatures that fail the saving throw can't treat any other creature as an ally or be treated as an ally by any other creature for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/YkM8O1icEEnqKDbb":{"lang":["Astral","Chronan","Common","Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"lore":[["Chronology Lore",45]],"notes":{"speed":"unfettered movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Retroactive Continuity","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","prediction"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature makes an attack roll against the chronos algorithm</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The chronos algorithm predicts the attack and changes history to avoid it. It gains a +4 circumstance bonus to its AC against the triggering strike. Afterwards, it relocates to a free space within 5 feet. As it is altering events rather than physically moving, this is not a movement or teleportation effect.</p>"},{"n":"Calculated Agility","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The chronos algorithm's multiple attack penalty with agile attacks is –3 for its second attack and –7 for subsequent attacks.</p>"},{"n":"Chronological Reconfiguration","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The chronos algorithm chooses a creature within 100 feet that is benefiting from a magical effect that grants the Quickened condition and attempts a counteract check against the effect (counteract modifier +42). On a success, the target loses the quickened condition. Additionally, the chronos algorithm either becomes quickened or makes the target Slowed 1; this effect persists for 1 minute or for the duration of the counteracted effect, whichever is shorter. The chronos algorithm can use the extra action from being quickened only to Stride or Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Recursive Loop","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The chronos algorithm travels through time, looping back to the current moment. A duplicate of itself appears in an unoccupied space within 30 feet, and both copies make a Strike. Both Strikes count toward the chronos algorithm's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after both attacks. After both Strikes are made, or if the action is interrupted, one copy of the chronos algorithm's choice vanishes. Any damage or effects applied to the vanishing copy are negated.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/5ntrfhh87s4LuqTv":{"lang":["Draconic"],"notes":{"speed":"cavern crawler"},"abilities":[{"n":"Cavern Crawler","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The coal drake's lithe form allows them to traverse caves and tunnels with ease. The coal drake can move through a gap at least 2 feet wide without Squeezing and can Squeeze through a gap at least 1 foot wide.</p>"},{"n":"Flint Sparks","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by the coal drake's tail Strikes must attempt a DC 21 Fortitude save; the creature is then temporarily immune to flint sparks for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1d4 rounds.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Blinded for 1d4 rounds and dazzled for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Coaldust Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","earth"],"f":"","d":"<p>The coal drake spews forth a billowing cloud of coal dust in a 20-foot cone. All creatures within the cloud become Concealed, and all creatures outside the cloud become concealed to creatures within the cloud. The cloud persists for 1d6 rounds, during which time the coal drake can't use their Coaldust Breath again. If an open flame enters the cloud, or if any attack or effect with the fire trait occurs within it (such as the coal drake's tail Strike), the cloud ignites, dealing 5d6 fire damage to each creature within it (DC 21 basic Reflex save). The cloud then dissipates prematurely, but this explosion doesn't allow the coal drake to recover the use of Coaldust Breath more quickly.</p>"},{"n":"Draconic Frenzy","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The coal drake makes two Fangs Strikes and one Tail Strike in any order.</p>"},{"n":"Speed Surge","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"3 times per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> three times per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The coal drake Strides, Flies, or Climbs twice.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/EcxPzS4UtxQDYpP3":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Thalassic","Seaspeech"],"gear":["+1 Striking Coral Longspear"],"abilities":[{"n":"Seaspeech","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The coenosteum knight can converse with aquatic animals and plants, as speak with animals and speak with plants.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Inject Venom","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The coenosteum knight's last action was a successful coral longspear Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The coenosteum knight injects nematocyctic venom into the target, producing it from their skin and channeling it through the grooves in their longspear into the target's body. If the attack was a critical hit, the creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to their saving throw against the poison.</p>"},{"n":"Bioluminescence","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["light","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The coenosteum knight has 61 or more Hit Points remaining</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The coenosteum knight intensifies the natural light that emanates from their body. All creatures within a 30-foot emanation must attempt a DC 23 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is temporarily immune to bioluminescence for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Blinded for 1 round, then dazzled for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Leech Life","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["death","primal","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The coenosteum knight has 60 or fewer Hit Points remaining</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The knight desperately draws in the vitality from nearby creatures to shore up the damage to their reefs. Each creature within 20 feet of the knight that is not in the knight's square takes 6d6 void damage (DC 26 basic Fortitude save). The knight gains 6d6 temporary Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Nematocyctic Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 23 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 2d6 poison damage, Clumsy 1, and Enfeebled 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 3d6 poison damage, Clumsy 2, Enfeebled 2 (1 minute)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 4d6 poison damage, clumsy 2, enfeebled 2, and Slowed 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Paralyzed (1 round)</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/9e8ZEx9Epf4QvTq9":{"lang":["Fey","Necril","can't speak any language"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Death's Perfume","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["aura","olfactory","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. Living creatures that enter or start their turn in the corpse flower's aura must succeed at a DC 27 Fortitude save or be Sickened 1 (or Sickened 2 on a critical failure). A creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Corpse Pollen","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison","unholy","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 28 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 2d8 void damage and Clumsy 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 3d8 void damage and Clumsy 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 3d8 void damage, clumsy 2 and regains half as many Hit Points from all healing (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> 4d8 void damage, clumsy 2 and gains no benefit from healing (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> dead.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Corpse Commander","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>All vine mummies within 100 feet that the corpse flower created with Ensnare Corpse immediately spend their reactions to Stride or Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Corpse Pollen Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["poison","primal","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>All creatures in a 30-foot burst around the corpse flower take 4d8 void damage (DC 28 basic Fortitude save) and are exposed to corpse pollen. Creatures with void healing instead regain 4d8 healing Hit Points. The corpse flower can't use this ability again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Ensnare Corpse","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The corpse flower is adjacent to a creature that they killed with their corpse pollen in the last 24 hours</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The corpse flower spends 10 minutes to ritually wrap the corpse in their vines, drink the liquids out of their body, and reanimate it as an independent vine mummy under their command. A vine mummy has the statistics of a mummy guardian, except it is mindless and lacks the Blighted Consumption reaction. Vine mummies are not minions, but they have a vague understanding of their creator's will, allowing them to follow their creator, stand guard over a location, or attack their creator's enemies.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/UxX0d3X3wSXLGxlO":{"lang":["Envisioning"],"lore":[["Mathematics Lore",36]],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Envisioning","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>100 feet. A fractrix can communicate mentally with any creatures in the aura using wordless psychic projections. They don't need to share a language, though the aeon's meaning to non-aeons can be vague and is often mysterious. An aeon can use this ability to communicate flawlessly with any other aeon on the same plane as themselves.</p>"},{"n":"Vulnerability to Randomness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Because the cosiadifex relies so strongly on their ability to connect cause and effect and understand the true nature of causality, the rare instances of true randomness in the universe are capable of confounding them and throwing them off their stride. Whenever the cosiadifex witnesses a random activity or effect, such as the actions of a Confused creature, the effects of a protean's warpwave, or a wild magic effect from a wellspring dragon, they are Stupefied 1 for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Knockdown","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Cascading Disaster","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The cosiadifex makes a shard Strike, attempting to trigger an improbable set of circumstances that brings disaster to their enemies. If the Strike hits, the cosiadifex can make another Strike at a different target within 30 feet of the target they just hit, repeating this process until they miss a Strike. The cosiadifex can't target the same creature twice with this ability. The damage type of any Strikes after the first depends on the nature of the chain reaction caused, such as dealing fire damage by causing an oil lantern to explode. Any fortune effects that apply to the first Strike apply to every Strike in the chain.</p>"},{"n":"Ominous Wingbeat","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","concentrate","divine"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cosiadifex's mantle ripples slightly, disturbing the air in an impossibly precise fashion that stirs up a tornado that appears at the beginning of the cosiadifex's next turn. The tornado has a 15-foot radius and is up to 100 feet tall. The wind imposes a –4 circumstance penalty to physical ranged attacks, and the air in the area is greater difficult terrain for flying creatures. Creatures that enter or begin their turn within the tornado take 10d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 38 basic Fortitude save). Creatures that fail the save are also thrown 20 feet upward (or 40 feet on a critical failure). A creature can only take damage or be thrown by Ominous Wingbeat once per round. The cosiadifex can Sustain the tornado to extend the effect for up to 1 minute; when they do, they can also move the tornado up to 50 feet in any direction.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/RIbSLkvi6vEFgr4s":{"lang":["Aklo","Fey","Sakvroth"],"abilities":[{"n":"Spelltwisting Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet, creatures who Cast a Spell in the aura, including the cranklejack, must succeed at a DC 23 Will save or the spell becomes a surge of wild magic. Either roll on the Wild Magic table from Battlezoo Dragons: Misfit Dragons or on any other wild magic table you prefer.</p>"},{"n":"Chaotic Gizmos","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cranklejack unleashes an unpredictable flurry of attacks that even the cranklejack themself can't predict. Roll 1d6 twice. For each roll of 1 or 2, nothing happens. For each roll of 3, the cranklejack makes a hammer Strike, for each roll of 4, the cranklejack make an impaling spike Strike, for each roll of 5, the cranklejack makes a saw Strike, and for each roll of 6, the cranklejack makes a volt fist Strike. If the cranklejack makes two Strikes, they can choose which order to make them.</p>"},{"n":"Twice for Bad Luck","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["misfortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The cranklejack hits the same foe with a second Strike on the same turn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Once is a coincidence, but twice is just bad luck. The foe becomes extremely unlucky (DC 26 Will save; the foe must roll this Will save twice and take the worse result). On a failure, the creature must roll twice and take the worse result on all checks for 2 rounds.</p><p>Effect: Twice for Bad Luck</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/2LKpIw7ELV0TAW1i":{"lang":["Melodian","Petran","Common","can't speak"],"notes":{"hp":"harmonic resonance"},"abilities":[{"n":"Echolocation","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A crystal chimling can use their hearing as a precise sense at the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Crystal Chimes","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A crystal chimling ordinarily has four chimes. A creature can attempt to sever one of the chimling's chimes by specifically targeting it and dealing damage equal to the chime's Hit Points. A chime that is not completely severed returns to full Hit Points at the end of any creature's turn.</p><p>Each chime has 5 HP and is immune to area damage.</p>"},{"n":"Harmonic Resonance","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["auditory","healing","primal","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p>The crystal chimling has regeneration equal to the number of chimes they have, which can't be overcome except by severing the chimes. They can replace a severed chime by finding and bonding with a suitable crystal in a process that takes 1 week.</p><p>Effect: Chimes</p>"},{"n":"Lucky Charm","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","fortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> An ally within 30 feet of the chimling fails or critically fails a saving throw</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The crystal chimling's chimes ring for luck. The ally rerolls the saving throw and uses the better result.</p>"},{"n":"Sonorous Echo","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Another crystal chimling within 20 feet uses sonorous toll</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The crystal chimling echoes the sound, dealing 1d4 sonic damage to each creature in a 5-foot emanation (DC 18 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Sonorous Toll","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>A deep resounding toll deals 2d6 sonic damage to each creature in a 10-foot emanation (DC 18 basic Fortitude save). Crystal chimlings are immune to damage from Sonorous Toll.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/6dOXvySQfr0Bj8Qh":{"abilities":[{"n":"Icy Wings","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a crystalwing swarm takes damage from an area or splash effect with the fire trait, the butterflies' wings melt. Without their wings, the swarm loses their fly speed as well as their Mirage Swarm ability; this automatically ends Mirage Swarm if it was already active. Additionally, the swarm can't dazzle creatures with Dazzling Frostbite. The crystalwing swarm can spend an Interact action to regrow their wings.</p>"},{"n":"Dazzling Frostbite","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Each creature in the crystalwing swarm's space takes 1d6 cold damage. If the crystalwing swarm in bright light, the creature must also succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or be Dazzled for 1 round from the brilliance refracting off the swarm's wings.</p>"},{"n":"Mirage Swarm","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["illusion","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The crystalwing swarm is in bright light</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The crystalwing swarm spins light to appear to be larger than it actually is. The swarm chooses four adjacent squares and precisely channels light off of their wings so that those squares appear to have butterflies in them; the illusion persists until the beginning of the swarm's next turn. A creature can disbelieve this illusion with a successful DC 16 Perception check to Seek; once a creature has succeeded at this Perception check, they are temporarily immune to Mirage Swarm for 24 hours.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/f8fvVzhvZW3OivUn":{"lang":["Arboreal","Cryan","Fey","can't speak any language"],"notes":{"per":"snow vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Snow Vision","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Snow doesn't impair the dedstre's vision; they ignore concealment from snowfall.</p>"},{"n":"Encompassing Cold","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. The biting chill in the air around a dedstre is inescapable. The dedstre reduces the temperature to extreme cold, which deals 2d6 cold damage for every 10 minutes of exposure. Mundane cold-weather clothing does not protect against this effect.</p>"},{"n":"Winter's Cycle","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the dedstre hits a plant with an icicle Strike, the plant takes an additional 3 void damage (this damage is doubled on a critical hit).</p>"},{"n":"Boreal Camouflage","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The dedstre is in a boreal forest</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dedstre naturally blends into frozen woodlands. Until the next time they act, they appear as a normal tree and have an automatic result of 36 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as one.</p>"},{"n":"Chill Death","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["cold","death","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The frigid air around the dedstre snuffs out all life. All creatures in a 20-foot emanation take 4d6 cold damage, and plant creatures take 4 additional void damage (DC 25 basic Fortitude save). Creatures that fail the save are Drained 1 (Drained 2 on a critical failure).</p><p>Plant Damage: 4d6+4 void</p>"},{"n":"Sap Heat","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["cold","concentrate","primal"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dedstre attempts to counteract a single magical effect within 60 feet that either grants cold resistance or protection from cold environmental effects, with a counteract modifier of +15. On a success, the effect ends if it is temporary or is suppressed for 1 minute if it is permanent.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/tYQXLpoIJgdDGzPO":{"abilities":[{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A dewdrop ooze can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Cobble Together","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the dewdrop ooze takes sonic damage while Disincorporated, the dewdrop ooze is forcibly reformed into a single coherent entity, and can't use Regroup until after it Disincorporates again, and the ooze is Off-Guard for 1 round</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Engulf","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>DC 29 Reflex, 6d6 acid damage, Escape, Rupture 17</p><hr><p><p>The monster Strides up to double its Speed and can move through the spaces of any creatures in its path. Any creature of the monster's size or smaller whose space the monster moves through can attempt a Reflex save with the listed DC to avoid being engulfed. A creature unable to act automatically critically fails this save. If a creature succeeds at its save, it can choose to be either pushed aside (out of the monster's path) or pushed in front of the monster to the end of the monster's movement. The monster can attempt to Engulf the same creature only once in a single use of Engulf. The monster can contain as many creatures as can fit in its space.</p>\n<p>A creature that fails its save is pulled into the monster's body. It is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The creature takes the listed amount of damage when first engulfed and at the end of each of its turns while it's engulfed. An engulfed creature can get free by Escaping against the listed escape DC. An engulfed creature can attack the monster engulfing it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The engulfing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the engulfed creature cuts itself free.\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>A creature that gets free by either method can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, all creatures it has engulfed are automatically released as the monster's form loses cohesion.</p></p>"},{"n":"Disincorporate","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Until the next time it acts, the dewdrop ooze disperses its body into tiny droplets. It has an automatic result of 42 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as mundane dew. If the dewdrop ooze had any creatures Grabbed or engulfed, they are automatically released.</p>"},{"n":"Regroup","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The dewdrop ooze has used Disincorporate</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dewdrop ooze reforms into a single coherent entity. All creatures in a 10-foot emanation around the ooze are splattered with acid, taking 6d6 acid damage (DC 26 basic Reflex save). The ooze then uses Engulf. It can't use Regroup again until after it Disincorporates.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/REGya8TV5IQPPkrp":{"notes":{"per":"spacewarp sense (precise) 120 feet","speed":"dimensional squeeze"},"abilities":[{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A dimension ooze can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Spacewarp Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The dimension ooze immediately knows the precise origin point and destination of any creatures affected by a teleportation effect within the listed range. It can also pinpoint the location of any extraplanar spaces, even those within objects such as a <em>spacious pouch</em>.</p>"},{"n":"Devour Magic","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the dimension ooze's reach uses an effect with the teleportation or extradimensional traits</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The dimension ooze makes a pseudopod Strike against the creature. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the dimension ooze's multiple attack penalty. On a hit, the ooze attempts to counteract the effect (counteract modifier +20). If the counteract check succeeds, the ooze becomes Quickened until the end of its next turn. It can use the quickened action to Stride or Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Withdraw","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["extradimensional","occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The dimension ooze takes damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ooze retreats into a temporary extraplanar space until the start of its next turn. At the beginning of its next turn, it reappears in a random unoccupied space within 10 feet of its original location.</p>"},{"n":"Dimensional Squeeze","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dimension ooze can slip between the cracks of the physical world. When it moves or makes a pseudopod Strike, it treats any square within 30 feet as adjacent to it. This effectively grants its pseudopod Strikes 30 feet of reach and allows it to Step or Stride up to 30 feet despite its Speed unless this special ability is prevented from functioning.</p>"},{"n":"Engulf","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>DC 28 Reflex, 3d10 force damage, Escape, Rupture 15</p><hr><p><p>The monster Strides up to double its Speed and can move through the spaces of any creatures in its path. Any creature of the monster's size or smaller whose space the monster moves through can attempt a Reflex save with the listed DC to avoid being engulfed. A creature unable to act automatically critically fails this save. If a creature succeeds at its save, it can choose to be either pushed aside (out of the monster's path) or pushed in front of the monster to the end of the monster's movement. The monster can attempt to Engulf the same creature only once in a single use of Engulf. The monster can contain as many creatures as can fit in its space.</p>\n<p>A creature that fails its save is pulled into the monster's body. It is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The creature takes the listed amount of damage when first engulfed and at the end of each of its turns while it's engulfed. An engulfed creature can get free by Escaping against the listed escape DC. An engulfed creature can attack the monster engulfing it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The engulfing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the engulfed creature cuts itself free.\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>A creature that gets free by either method can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, all creatures it has engulfed are automatically released as the monster's form loses cohesion.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/mtGxBnlkfT1rOqgY":{"lang":["Common","Drumcap","Fey","can't speak any language except drumcap"],"notes":{"per":"low-light vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Impulsive Dispersal","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The drumcap takes bludgeoning damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The drumcap takes the full force of the attack on their cap, releasing a high concentration of hallucinogenic spores in a 5-foot emanation that persists for 1d4 rounds. Creatures who start their turn in the emanation take 2d4 poison damage (DC 17 basic Fortitude save) and are Dazzled for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Fascinating Cuteness","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","manipulate","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The drumcap beats happily at their cap and does a dance to distract those around them. All creatures within a 60-foot emanation must attempt a DC 17 Will save to avoid being entranced. This effect lasts for 1 round, but if the drumcap uses this ability again on subsequent rounds, they extend the duration. Once a creature succeeds at any save against Fascinating Cuteness, that creature is temporarily immune to Fascinating Cuteness for 24 hours.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Fascinated by the drumcap's cuteness.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the fascination does not end if the drumcap attacks one of the creature's allies; it still ends normally if the drumcap attacks the fascinated creature.</p>"},{"n":"Psychedelic Spores","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>With a successful cap Strike, a drumcap releases a small puff of hallucinogenic spores. The target must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or be Dazzled for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/4BQjFfinxOGmjWWv":{"lang":["Aklo","Can't speak"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The eldritch tyrant has a creature Grabbed in its mouth tentacle</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eldritch tyrant constricts the grabbed creature, crushing both its body and mind. The creature takes 3d12+4 bludgeoning damage and 2d6 mental damage, with a basic Fortitude save. On a failure, the creature is also Stupefied 1 for 1 minute, and on a critical failure, they're Stupefied 2 for 1 minute instead.</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Huge, 3d12 bludgeoning plus 2d6 mental, Rupture 39</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Grabbing Pull","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The eldritch tyrant's last action was a successful mouth tentacle Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eldritch tyrant pulls its victim in closer and then grabs it in place. The eldritch tyrant can move the creature it hit with its mouth tentacle towards it by an amount of its choosing. Then it Grabs the creature with its mouth tentacle. It can transfer the creature to be Grabbed by its jaws instead as a free action, depending on whether it is planning to use Constrict or Swallow Whole next.</p>"},{"n":"Fast Swallow","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The eldritch tyrant Grabs a creature with its jaws</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eldritch tyrant uses Swallow Whole.</p>"},{"n":"Mind-Tearing Roar","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental","occult","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The eldritch tyrant lets loose a powerful roar, tearing through the minds of all who hear it and terrifying them, while leaving their bodies battered by sonic damage. Creatures within a 120-foot emanation take 7d6 mental damage and 7d6 sonic damage with a DC 36 Will save, with the effects below. After using its mind-tearing roar, the eldritch tyrant can't use it again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is Frightened 2 and Fleeing for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/LEZUVizmJszf7Pta":{"lang":["Luxan","Talican","Utopian","Voltan"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Conductive Shell","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":["divine","electricity"],"f":"","d":"<p>The electrum juggernaut channels electricity through their metal frame. Until the beginning of their next turn, creatures that hit them with an unarmed attack or a melee attack or who otherwise touch them take 3d6 electricity damage. A Grabbed creature takes this damage once at the start of that creature's turn.</p>"},{"n":"Vanity","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The electrum juggernaut takes pride in their armor's gleaming radiance and becomes metaphysically weakened if the armor is soiled. When a creature adjacent to the electrum juggernaut takes piercing or slashing damage or uses an Interact action to soil the electrum juggernaut's armor, or when a creature uses a spell or ability that would reasonably cause the juggernaut to become dirty at the GM's discretion, the juggernaut must attempt a DC 28 Reflex save to avoid becoming stained. On a failure, the electrum juggernaut's AC is reduced to 31 and they lose both their resistance to physical damage and their Sparkling Armor ability. These effects last until the juggernaut spends 10 minutes cleaning their armor.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Electrum Armaments","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The electrum juggernaut's weapons are made of electrum, an alloy of gold and silver, and trigger weaknesses to both metals. They are built in to the juggernaut's body and can't be Disarmed.</p>"},{"n":"Sparkling Armor","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","light","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>While the electrum juggernaut is within bright or dim light, they sparkle majestically. Their attempts to Demoralize have the visual trait instead of the auditory trait, ignore the penalty for not sharing a language, and also dazzle the target for 1 round on a success or critical success.</p>"},{"n":"Wide Swing","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The electrum juggernaut makes a longsword Strike and compares the attack roll result to the ACs of up to two foes within their reach. They roll damage only once and apply it to each creature they hit. A Wide Swing counts as two attacks for their multiple attack penalty.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/BM9pN2xyIJaLRbHK":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Empyrean","Jotun","Melodian"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status vs. auditory or sonic effects"},"abilities":[{"n":"Booming Voice","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sound of an emirad's voice carries far. All listeners within 1 mile can hear the emirad loudly and clearly whenever the emirad speaks, even if other ambient noise would otherwise block the sound. The emirad can't choose to speak any more quietly even if they wanted to do so.</p>"},{"n":"Counter Performance","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p> The emirad can use Counter Performance at will.</p>"},{"n":"Listen to my Song!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","divine","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An auditory effect created by the emirad would be counteracted, or the target of an auditory effect created by the emirad would be unaffected due to an active spell or ability</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The emirad lets out a cry that will not be silenced. They attempt to counteract the triggering effect, using their Performance modifier as their counteract modifier. On a critical success that counteracts the effect, if the creature who created the triggering effect is within 1 mile, that creature gains weakness 5 to sonic damage for 1 minute.</p><p>Effect: Listen to my Song!</p>"},{"n":"Right to the Chorus","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The emirad becomes Quickened for 1 round. This additional action can only be used to make a sound bolt Strike, to cast Courageous Anthem or Rallying Anthem, or to begin or Sustain Resounding Refrain. The emirad is then Slowed 1 on their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Resounding Refrain","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The emirad's last action was a successful sound bolt Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The emirad stores up an echo of the sonic energy, preparing for a grand finale. The emirad can Sustain this ability for up to 1 minute. The first time the emirad ends their turn without Sustaining, they make a number of sound bolt Strikes equal to the total number of actions they have spent on Resounding Refrain. These attacks do not apply their existing multiple attack penalty. The multiple attack penalty on these Strikes increases when the emirad makes an additional sound bolt Strike on a creature that they have already targeted with one of their Strikes from Resounding Refrain.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/1TzMMIEpMfMskqWP":{"notes":{"hp":"egeneration 10 (deactivated by void)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Regeneration 10 (Deactivated by Void)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster regains the listed number of Hit Points each round at the beginning of its turn. Its Dying condition never increases beyond Dying 3 as long as its regeneration is active. However, if it takes damage of a type listed in the regeneration entry, its regeneration deactivates until the end of its next turn. Deactivate the regeneration before applying any damage of a listed type, since that damage might kill the monster by bringing it to Dying 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Flesh Conversion","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p>Plants, fungi, and creatures with void healing are immune to Flesh Conversion</p><p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 25 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Sickened 1 (1 hour)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Sickened 2 (1 hour)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> when rolling a recovery check, the creature's degree of success is one degree better (3 hours)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> the creature gains fast healing 5 (5 hours)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> the creature gains lifesense 60 feet and regeneration 10 (deactivated by void) (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 6</strong> the creature dies and its body is fully converted into new endless growth.</p>"},{"n":"Infectious Growth","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The living growth's last action was a successful parasitic tumor Strike that damaged a living creature. The damaged creature isn't Drained 4 and doesn't already have an infectious growth attached to it</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The parasitic tumor attempts to attach itself to the creature's body (DC 25 Fortitude negates). If it succeeds, the creature is Drained 1. This is cumulative with other drained conditions from infectious growth. At the end of each of its turns, a creature with an attached parasitic tumor must attempt a DC 25 Fortitude save. On a failure, the value of its drained condition increases by 1. If the value of the drained condition reaches 4, the parasitic tumor then falls off and develops into a new endless growth over the next 24 hours. The affected creature or an adjacent creature can remove the tumor with a successful DC 31 Medicine check. The tumor automatically falls off if the creature takes void damage or critically succeeds at their Fortitude save to resist the drained condition.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/BszbQD9VW4lpZcUy":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Can't speak, Death of the author"],"notes":{"hp":"rejuvenation, void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Death of the Author","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal inventor communicates by replaying past scenes of their speech during life. They can't say any words that they didn't say at least once while alive.</p>"},{"n":"Rejuvenation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When an eternal inventor is destroyed, it re-forms after 2d4 days in its creator's office or workshop, fully healed. An eternal inventor can only be permanently destroyed if the project that took the creator's life is successfully completed.</p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Jinx of Instability","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["curse","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet of the eternal inventor performs an action with the manipulate trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eternal inventor curses the object the creature is manipulating or the manipulating creature. The creature must attempt a DC 38 Will save. On a failure, the action is disrupted and the creature injures itself, taking 13 untyped damage of an appropriate type for the item or action's nature.</p>"},{"n":"Fire the Omnicannon!","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal inventor manifests a floating cannon in their square and fires it in their choice of two 30-foot cones or two 60-foot lines that point in opposite directions. The cannon deals 4d8 physical damage and 4d4 energy damage (DC 38 basic Reflex save). For each direction, they choose between bludgeoning, piercing, and slashing for the physical damage and between cold, electricity, fire, or sonic for the energy damage.</p><p>4d6 bludgeoning</p><p>4d6 piercing</p><p>4d6 slashing</p><p>4d6 cold</p><p>4d6 electricity</p><p>4d6 fire</p><p>4d6 sonic</p>"},{"n":"Instantaneous Calculation","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature resists or is weak to damage dealt by the eternal inventor, they automatically determine the resistance or weakness's type and amount.</p>"},{"n":"Relive Catastrophe","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal inventor replicates the accident that claimed their life, such the in-flight detonation of an alchemical jetpack attempting to break the sound barrier or the unstoppable rampage of a nigh-invincible construct that turned against its creator. Each creature within a 60-foot emanation around the eternal inventor takes 16d6 untyped damage of a type appropriate to the accident's nature, such as bludgeoning or fire (DC 40 basic Reflex save). Creatures that fail the saving throw are also flooded with the creator's dying despair, becoming Frightened 2, or Frightened 3 on a critical failure. The eternal inventor can't use Relive Catastrophe for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ri3dGbG8YJkuzk13":{"lang":["Common","Melodian","Can't speak"],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status to all saves vs. auditory or sonic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Musical Flourish","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal symphony is versatile with its musical performances. It can use Performance to Create a Diversion, Demoralize, or Feint.</p>"},{"n":"Encore","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the eternal symphony is reduced to 0 HP, it plays a final swan song before it is destroyed. It uses Battle Symphony.</p>"},{"n":"Reverberate","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["occult","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The instruments that make up the eternal symphony's body are susceptible to being played not only by itself, but also by its enemies. Whenever the eternal symphony takes bludgeoning damage or is affected by an air effect, all creatures adjacent to the eternal symphony take 1d6 sonic damage.</p>"},{"n":"Dissonance","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["auditory","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>Any creature hit by an eternal symphony's resonant vibration Strike must succeed on a DC 34 Fortitude save or become Stupefied 1 for 1 round (or Stupefied 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Accelerando","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal symphony increases the tempo of its music. It gains the Quickened condition for 1 minute and can use the extra action each round only to Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Battle Symphony","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal symphony plays a terrifying song of destruction in a 30-foot emanation. Each creature in the area takes 7d6 mental damage (DC 36 basic Fortitude save). A creature that fails this save is also Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Crescendo","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["occult","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal symphony gradually increases the intensity of its music. Until the end of its turn, sonic and auditory effects deal an additional 1d6 sonic damage. This effect is cumulative for each consecutive turn that the eternal symphony has used Crescendo (to a maximum of 4d6 extra sonic damage).</p>"},{"n":"Rhythmic Cadence","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The eternal symphony plays an infectious rhythm that inspires who hear it to dance uncontrollably. The eternal symphony makes two kick drum Strikes. Both attacks count toward the eternal symphony's multiple attack penalty, but the penalty increases only after both attacks. If both Strikes hit, each creature in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a DC 34 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Off-Guard until the end of its next turn.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Slowed 1 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Slowed 2 for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/IlxNDJjp74dTKBkp":{"lang":["Chthonian","Telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"ac":" all-around vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Inexorable","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The eunidoi recovers from the Paralyzed, slowed, and stunned conditions at the end of its turn. It's also immune to penalties to its Speeds and the Immobilized condition, and it ignores difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain.</p>"},{"n":"Predatory Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>As Improved Grab, but the eunidoi's Improved Grab does not end when it moves. Instead, it carries the Grabbed creature with it.</p><hr><p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Mindrot","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 28 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 2d6 mental damage and Stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 3d6 mental damage, Stupefied 2, and Off-Guard (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 4d6 mental damage, stupefied 2, and off-guard (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Rock Tunneler","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A eunidoi can burrow through solid stone at a Speed of 15 feet. It can leave a tunnel if it desires, and it usually does.</p>"},{"n":"Frightening Display","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","emotion","fear","mental","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The eunidoi's mandibles snap open, revealing a gaping mouth filled with bristled tongues. Creatures in a 30-foot emanation must attempt a DC 28 Will save, after which they are temporarily immune to further Frightening Displays for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 3 and can't reduce the value of its frightened condition below 1 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Ambush","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The eunidoi Strides or Burrows and then Strikes. If the eunidoi began this action hidden, it remains hidden until after the Strike.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/HlVB4lImHp4UdmEH":{"notes":{"per":"spellsense (imprecise) 60 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Spellsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The fallout sparrow swarm detects the magical resonance within magic items and within creatures that can cast spells.</p>"},{"n":"Fallout Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["arcane","aura","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. Fallout sparrows emit an aura of magical radiation. A creature that begins its turn in the area becomes Sickened 1 (DC 22 Fortitude negates).</p>"},{"n":"Strange Murmuration","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The fallout sparrow swarm is targeted by a spell</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The swarm Flies 15 feet toward the caster.</p>"},{"n":"Devastation Mimic","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","auditory","emotion","fear","mental","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The flock of sparrows emits an eerie, discordant birdsong, mimicking the sounds of explosions, collapses, and screams. Each creature within 20 feet must attempt a DC 25 Will save. On a successful save, the creature becomes temporarily immune to Devastation Mimic for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2 and takes 4d6 sonic damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is frightened 2 and takes 8d6 sonic damage.</p>"},{"n":"Fallout Rain","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The fallout sparrows Fly, spraying droplets of magically radioactive poison in their wake. All creatures in and below the squares that they Fly through must attempt a DC 25 Fortitude save. The swarm can't use Fallout Rain again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 3d6 poison damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 6d6 poison damage and is Sickened 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes 12d6 poison damage and is Sickened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Necrotizing Beaks","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The fallout sparrows' angry pecking deals 2d6 piercing plus 2d6 void damage to each enemy in the swarm's space (DC 25 basic Reflex save).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/zM1DZ9vUKsM9oL38":{"notes":{"per":"metalsense (imprecise) 60 feet","speed":"magnetic climb"},"abilities":[{"n":"Metalsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Due to its innate magnetism, a ferrofluidic ooze senses nearby chunks of metal of at least light Bulk.</p>"},{"n":"Demagnetize","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Overwhelming heat can interfere with the ferrofluidic ooze's magnetism. If the ferrofluidic ooze takes 50 or more fire damage at the same time, it temporarily loses its magnetic field. Until the end of its next turn, it loses magnetic attraction, magnetic climb, magnetic coating, magnetic hold, merger, and metalsense.</p>"},{"n":"Magnetic Hold","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 10 feet of the ferrofluidic ooze deals slashing damage to it</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ooze splits in half before quickly reforming due to its strong magnetic fields. The ooze attempts an Athletics check to Grapple the triggering creature; it does not need to have a free hand to do so. This check neither applies nor counts toward the ferrofluidic ooze's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Magnetic Attraction","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","metal","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ferrofluidic ooze manipulates its magnetic field to draw metal toward itself. Each creature within 30 feet that is either wearing metal armor or affected by the ooze's magnetic coating must attempt a DC 25 Fortitude save. This is forced movement. The forced movement ends once the creature is adjacent to the ooze. Unattended metal objects in the area with a Bulk of 10 or less are automatically drawn 20 feet toward the ooze.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature moves 5 feet toward the ooze.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature moves 10 feet toward the ooze.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature moves 20 feet toward the ooze.</p>"},{"n":"Magnetic Climb","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["metal","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ferrofluidic ooze can climb on any surface made out of metal, including ceilings and other inverted surfaces, though such surfaces are difficult terrain for it.</p>"},{"n":"Magnetic Coating","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["metal","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a ferrofluidic ooze hits a creature with a pseudopod or magnetic globule Strike, the creature is coated in magnetic fluid, becoming Clumsy 1. The creature can spend a single manipulate action to scrape off the fluid.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/fA3sxCyMCdFHJOLQ":{"notes":{"per":"metalsense (imprecise) 60 feet","speed":"(swim in lava or magma only)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Metalsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Due to its innate magnetism, a ferrous crab swarm senses nearby chunks of metal of at least light Bulk.</p>"},{"n":"Molten Digestion","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Ferrous crabs attempt to devour metal objects. At the start of the crabs' turn, all unattended metal objects in their squares take 2d6 untyped damage, ignoring Hardness. Each creature in the swarm's space who is wearing or carrying a metal item must attempt at a DC 20 Reflex save; on a failure, the crabs deal 2d6 untyped damage to one of their metal items, ignoring Hardness.</p>"},{"n":"Crushing Polarity","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["metal","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Each enemy wearing metal armor in the swarm's space takes 3d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 20 basic Fortitude save). Each target that fails the saving throw is Grabbed until the end of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Molten Claw","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Each enemy in the swarm's space takes 2d6 bludgeoning plus 1d6 fire damage (DC 20 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Reverse Polarity","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","metal","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ferrous crab swarm makes a molten claw attack and then magnetizes their foes. Each enemy creature in the swarm's space that is carrying at least 1 Bulk of metal objects must attempt a DC 20 Reflex save with the following effects.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature uses magnetic propulsion to their advantage. They can immediately Step.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature's ability to grasp metal items is hampered for 1 round. During that time, attempts to Disarm the target of metal items gain a +2 circumstance bonus, and the creature takes a –2 circumstance penalty to attacks with metal item or other checks requiring a firm grasp on the item. Additionally, if the creature is wearing metal armor, they are Off-Guard until the beginning of their next turn.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Any metal object (including weapons) that the creature is holding drop from their hand and lands in the creature's space. Additionally, if the creature is wearing metal armor, they are knocked Prone.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/sKFVjnck4SSE0wD0":{"lang":["Dwarven","Petran","Pyric","Talican"],"gear":["Forgemaster's Javelin","forgemaster's Warhammer"],"notes":{"speed":"magma glide"},"abilities":[{"n":"Unparalleled Crafter","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster knows the recipes for nearly all common, uncommon, and rare items, and is also capable of creating artifacts. They can Craft items during Downtime at 10 times the normal speed, ignoring all prerequisites.</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Forgemaster's Arsenal","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster's weapons are a <em>+3 major striking warhammer</em> that deals 4d6 additional fire damage and a <em>+3 returning major striking javelin</em> that deals 2d6 additional fire damage and has a range increment of 120 feet. On a critical hit, the Forgemaster's weapons deal 2d10 persistent fire damage as well as their typical critical specialization effects.</p>"},{"n":"Impossible Heat","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>All fire damage dealt by the Forgemaster's attacks and abilities bypasses fire resistance.</p>"},{"n":"Magma Glide","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster can burrow freely through both magma and solid rock. When passing throw solid rock, they can choose to leave a tunnel.</p>"},{"n":"Bellows","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster inhales mightily, then exhales a cloud of superheated gas, dealing 24d6 fire damage in a 120-foot cone (DC 48 basic Reflex save). The Forgemaster can't use Bellows again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Reforge Hammer","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster reshape their hammer into another one-handed melee weapon, changing the weapon's base damage dice, critical specialization effects, and traits accordingly.</p>"},{"n":"Titan's Reach","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack","earth","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster reaches through the very stone to strike at their enemies. The Forgemaster makes a single Strike against any enemy that they can see. This attack can be made at any range and ignores all cover and concealment.</p>"},{"n":"Unworthy Wielder","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The Forgemaster declares the target unworthy of bearing its weapon, and compels the weapon to rebel. The target takes 15d6 untyped damage of whatever type the weapon typically deals (DC 46 Will save). If the target is wielding an intelligent weapon, use the higher of the wielder's result and the weapon's result. Regardless of the result, the target is then temporarily immune to this effect for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> the target takes full damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double damage. They drop their weapon and can't pick it back up again for 1 minute; if the target is an intelligent weapon PC, they are instead stunned for 1 minute. The target can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of their turns to end this effect.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/4jNJTr3YiCUEpoUD":{"lang":["Envisioning"],"lore":[["Mathematics Lore",28]],"notes":{"ac":"all-around vision","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","per":"spatial reckoning"},"abilities":[{"n":"Envisioning","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>100 feet. A fractrix can communicate mentally with any creatures in the aura using wordless psychic projections. They don't need to share a language, though the aeon's meaning to non-aeons can be vague and is often mysterious. An aeon can use this ability to communicate flawlessly with any other aeon on the same plane as themselves.</p>"},{"n":"All-Around Vision","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster can see in all directions simultaneously and therefore can't be flanked.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Confusing Geometry","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","emotion","incapacitation","mental","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. A creature that ends its turn in the aura must attempt a DC 29 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Confusing Geometry for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Confused for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is confused for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Infinite Refraction","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["light","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The fractrix is targeted by an effect with the light trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The fractrix's body refracts the light in a dazzling display. Each creature within 30 feet must succeed at a DC 32 Fortitude save or become Dazzled for 1 round, or for 1 minute on a critical failure.</p>"},{"n":"Spatial Reckoning","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine","revelation"],"f":"","d":"<p>A fractrix automatically detects and identifies space-altering magic (including teleportation effects) and is only affected by the magic if they choose to be.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Angle of Invisibility","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When viewed from certain angles, a fractrix is imperceptible to the eye. The fractrix carefully aligns themselves. Until they move or use this ability again, they are Invisible to creatures viewing them from within a 60-foot cone of their choice. If an affected creature also occupies spaces outside of the area, the fractrix is instead Concealed to that creature.</p>"},{"n":"Recursive Coil","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The fractrix endlessly tightens their fractal tendril around a creature they have Grabbed or Restrained. The target takes 3d10 bludgeoning damage, and it takes 1d10 persistent bludgeoning damage at the end of each of its turns until it Escapes.</p>"},{"n":"Warp Geometry","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","teleportation"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The fractrix warps space in a 30-foot burst within 120 feet, distorting geometry in the area for 1 minute. When a creature uses an action with the move trait to enter a square in the area, it must attempt a DC 32 Will save. Each creature can only be affected by Warp Geometry once per round.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Warp Geometry for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The fractrix bends space, depositing the creature in another square within the warped area of the fractrix's choice. This is forced movement. If the creature has not yet moved their entire Speed, it can continue its movement from its new location.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is too disoriented to continue their movement.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/NER1xO7JnPOjIqJ1":{"notes":{"speed":"hopper"},"abilities":[{"n":"Unfathomable Leap","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The gargantoad's mighty leg muscles propel it forward with reality-warping force. It Leaps up to 1,000 feet horizontally and 500 feet vertically. It can choose to carry any number of creatures that it has Grabbed or Restrained along with it.</p>"},{"n":"Terrifying Croak","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The gargantoad lets out a deep, resonant bellow that inflicts primal fear in all who hear it. All creatures within 1 mile must attempt a DC 44 Will save, with the following effects. Creatures that succeed at the save are temporarily immune to Terrifying Croak for 24 hours.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is frightened 2. For the next hour, any time that its turn begins and it is able to see, hear, or otherwise perceive the gargantoad, it must attempt another Will save against Terrifying Croak.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the creature is Frightened 4.</p>"},{"n":"Tentacle Forest","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>The gargantoad attempts an Athletics check to Grapple all creatures within reach of its tentacles. If any creatures were already Grabbed or Restrained in its tentacles, the gargantoad extends the duration of that condition until the end of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Huge, 3d8 acid plus 3d10 bludgeoning, Rupture 50.</p><p>Creatures that begin their turn Swallowed Whole are exposed to numbing toxin.</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Numbing Toxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 42 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 6d6 poison damage and Slowed 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 8d6 poison damage and Slowed 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 10d6 poison damage and slowed 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> 12d6 poison damage and Paralyzed (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Hopper","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Gargantoads move in large hops, allowing them to easily clear obstacles. They ignore difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain from obstacles shorter than 50 feet tall in their path.</p>"},{"n":"Greater Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>4d6+15 bludgeoning, DC 40 basic Fortitude,  (creatures grabbed by tentacles only)</p><hr><p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC. A creature that fails this save falls Unconscious, and a creature that succeeds is then temporarily immune to falling unconscious from Greater Constrict for 1 minute.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fast Swallow","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The Gargantoad Grabs a creature with its tongue</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gargantoad uses Swallow Whole.</p>"},{"n":"Bone Crunch","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gargantoad's palette crushes down on the bitten target hard enough to splinter bone. The target must attempt a DC 42 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes no additional effects.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 1d6 persistent bleed damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes 3d6 persistent bleed damage and is Clumsy 1 for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes 5d6 persistent bleed damage and is Clumsy 2 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Aquatic Ambush (100 Feet)","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster is hiding in water and a creature that hasn't detected it is within the listed number of feet.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster moves up to its swim Speed + 10 feet toward the triggering creature, traveling on water and on land. Once the creature is in reach, the monster makes a Strike against it. The creature is Off-Guard against this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Pull 100 feet","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a success with a Strike that lists Pull in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Reposition the creature, moving it closer to the monster. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Pull lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pulled on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/i5YkN1V3TZw9VGWz":{"lang":["Common","Goblin"],"gear":["Dogslicer","New Consumable","New Consumable","Gasbelly Poison Flask (4)","Padded Armor"],"abilities":[{"n":"Bounce","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The gasbelly goblin is hit by an attack that deals bludgeoning or slashing damage, and the attack is not a critical hit</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gasbelly goblin flies 30 feet directly away from the attacker (this is not forced movement, and it triggers reactions as normal). The gasbelly goblin takes no bludgeoning or slashing damage from the attack. If they collide with an obstacle, the gasbelly goblin changes direction and continues moving until they have used up the full 30 feet of movement.</p>"},{"n":"Numbing Toxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>Direct exposure to a gasbelly goblin's poison causes numbness and tingling. A creature hit by a gasbelly poison flask Strike must succeed at a DC 20 Fortitude save or become Clumsy 1 for 1 round. Creatures exposed to only the splash damage do not need to attempt this saving throw.</p>"},{"n":"Belching Jet","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["move","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The gasbelly goblin moves up to 50 feet in a straight line. All creatures that the gasbelly passes adjacent to during this movement take 5d6 poison damage (DC 17 basic Fortitude save). The goblin can't use Belching Jet again until they drink a gasbelly poison flask.</p>"},{"n":"Quickfingered Poisoner","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gasbelly goblin Interacts to draw a gasbelly poison flask, then Strikes with it or drinks it.</p>"},{"n":"Spit Up and Slash","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>With a hiccup and a lurch, the gasbelly goblin Interacts to dredge up poison from their stomach, spitting it on to their weapon to prepare for a more deadly attack. The goblin then Strikes with their dogslicer; the Strike deals an additional 1d6 poison damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/BzCnCylJLRx25TBt":{"lang":["Necril","Sussuran"],"notes":{"speed":"swiftness"},"abilities":[{"n":"Refuge in Breath","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The gasping death is targeted by an attack from a creature it can see</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The gasping death is in a creature's lungs</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gasping death retreats into the creature's lungs, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to AC. If the attack critically misses, it hits that creature instead.</p>"},{"n":"Choke","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["air","primal","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The gasping death is currently in a creature's lungs</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gasping death attempts to suffocate the creature. The creature loses remaining rounds of air using the suffocation rules and takes void damage based on the results of a DC 25 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature prevents the gasping death from entering its lungs.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 2d4 void damage and loses 1 round of remaining air.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 4d4 void damage and loses 2 rounds of remaining air.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes 8d4 void damage and loses all of its remaining air.</p>"},{"n":"Suffocating Void","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["air","primal","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The gasping death is occupying the same space as another creature of size Huge or smaller that can breathe, and it is not currently in a creature's lungs</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gasping death surrounds the creature's face and attempts to enter its airways. The creature attempts a DC 25 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 2d4 void damage before expelling the gasping death.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 4d4 void damage as a portion of the gasping death enters its lungs. The creature must immediately begin holding its breath.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, and the gasping death can use Choke once as a free action.</p><p>While the gasping death is in a creature's lungs, it can't move from that creature's space, but it automatically moves with the creature. The gasping death can leave a creature's lungs as a free action.</p><p>A creature that begins its turn with the gasping death in its lungs can spend 1 action to attempt a DC 25 Fortitude save to cough it up. On a success, they expel the gasping death from their lungs, taking 2d6 slashing damage and 1d8 void damage as the elemental rakes at their lungs. On a critical success, they expel the gasping death without taking additional damage.</p>"},{"n":"Cloud of Death","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gasping death's form is mostly insubstantial. It can enter and occupy the same space as other creatures, and it can move through a gap at least 1 inch wide without Squeezing.</p>"},{"n":"Swiftness","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gasping death's movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Inhabit Corpse","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A creature with the gasping death in its lungs has died in the last round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gasping death puppets the creature as an undead shell. The gasping death can use its actions to force the creature's body to perform any of the actions it could have taken in life. If the gasping death takes 20 untyped damage, it is forcibly released from the creature's body.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/seUexbbY71PNZbZm":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Spirituan","Can't speak any language, Speak with animals, Speak with plants"],"lore":[["Terrain Lore",20]],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Domain Dependent","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A genius loci is mystically bonded to a sacred site, such as a secluded grove or pristine pond. The land within 1 mile of this site is the genius loci's domain. The appearance of the land within the domain subtly alters to reflect the genius loci's physical and emotional state. Likewise, damage to the land manifests on the genius loci. If the domain suffers from large-scale pollution or magical blight, the genius loci is Drained 1 until the land is restored. If the genius loci exits their domain, they become Sickened 1 and can't reduce the condition's value by any means until they return to their domain. They must succeed at a DC 26 Fortitude save every day they spend separated from their land or increase the sickened value by 1 (to a maximum of Sickened 4).</p>"},{"n":"Shifting Paths","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 60 feet Strides</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The land itself attempts to lead creatures astray. The triggering creature must attempt a DC 28 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Shifting Paths 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature's Speed is reduced by 5 feet for this Stride.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature's Speed is reduced by 15 feet for this Stride.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature Strides its full speed in a direction of the Genius Loci's choice. This is forced movement.</p>"},{"n":"Alter Terrain","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The genius loci is within their domain</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The genius loci reshapes the terrain in a 30-foot radius around them, making it easier or harder for other creatures to traverse. They can change normal terrain into difficult terrain, difficult terrain into normal terrain or greater difficult terrain, and greater difficult terrain into difficult terrain. Regardless of what they choose, they can freely move through altered terrain as through it were normal terrain. The altered terrain persists for 1 minute or until the genius loci uses this ability again, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Domain Wall","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The genius loci casts 5th-rank Wall of Ice, Wall of Stone, or Wall of Thorns; each genius loci has access to whichever of these spells most closely fits with the nature of their domain.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/vKkmWrkGJ9jkms1j":{"abilities":[{"n":"Eye in the Dark","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A giant gloom rat's eye can pierce most shadows. When its eye is opened, it can't be Concealed or Hidden by darkness, unless the effect can also block darkvision. When its eye is closed, it is naturally invisible in dim light and darkness, as its body blends with surrounding shadows.</p>"},{"n":"Light Snack","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["darkness","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The giant gloom rat's last action was a successful jaws Strike against a creature or unattended object, and that creature or object is emanating light</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The giant gloom rat attempts to counteract one source of light on the target, or an object it is holding or wearing, with a counteract modifier of +9. If the source of light is mundane, the light is automatically snuffed out. If the source is magical and the counteract check is successful, the giant gloom rat gains temporary Hit Points equal to double the counteract rank of the effect (minimum 2).</p>"},{"n":"Gloom Fever","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature afflicted with this disease takes a –2 status penalty to all visual Perception checks</p><p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 17 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> carrier with only the base effect (1d4 hours)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> light blindness (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> light blindness and Dazzled when in dim light (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Blinded when in bright light and dazzled when in dim light, gains low-light vision (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> blinded when in bright or dim light, gains darkvision (1 day)</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/yHSYMAL4hjB4PgBz":{"notes":{"speed":"long roots"},"abilities":[{"n":"Mangrove Freeze","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gungrove can spend 1 minute to plant itself in an area of shallow water. Until the next time the gungrove acts, it has an automatic result of 32 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as an inanimate mangrove tree.</p>"},{"n":"Long Roots","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Though it's quickest in water, the gungrove's roots are also dexterous on land. It can Step 10 feet and doesn't treat shallow water as difficult terrain.</p>"},{"n":"Explosive Ejection","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The gungrove critically hits with a cannonfruit Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The gungrove uses Deploy Sapling.</p>"},{"n":"Deploy Sapling","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The gungrove's last action was a successful cannonfruit Strike against a Small or larger living creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The fruit deploys into a sapling, trying to get its roots into the creature it struck. The creature attempts a DC 20 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The sapling fails to take hold, but its roots still hamper the creature's movement. The creature takes –5-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds for 1 round or until it Escapes, whichever comes first.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> Until the creature Escapes the sapling, it is Drained 1 and takes a –5-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> Until the creature Escapes the sapling, it is Drained 2 and takes a –15-foot circumstance penalty to its Speeds. After escaping the fruit, the creature is drained 1 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Beaching Barrage","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The gungrove propels itself out of water in a burst of immature cannonfruit. It Swims up to its Speed in a straight line, then Leaps up to 20 feet. At the end of its movement, creatures within a 10-foot emanation around the gungrove take 2d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 20 basic Reflex save); those that fail the saving throw are pushed 5 feet away from the gungrove.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/KlkCp1dJocJQVdnR":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Venenan"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Absorb Soul","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["death","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a living creature dies from poison damage inflicted by the harrophage's Strikes, spells, or diseases, the creature's soul joins with the collective of the dead already within the harrophage. The harrophage immediately recovers a number of Hit Points equal to three times the creature's level. Until the harrophage is destroyed, they attempt to counteract all effects that would resurrect the creature (counteract modifier +34).</p>"},{"n":"Noxious Malignance","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>60 feet. When a creature enters or starts its turn in the aura, it is exposed to noxichor.</p>"},{"n":"Overwhelming Infection","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet fails a saving throw against one of the harrophage's afflictions</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature is also Sickened 1, or Sickened 2 if the disease's Stage is 3 or more.</p>"},{"n":"Biobombardment","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The harrophage expels a shrieking green cloud of toxic gas from its mouth in their choice of a 120-foot line or a 60-foot cone. Living creatures in the area take 20d6 poison damage if the harrophage spends two actions, or 20d8 poison damage if they spend three (DC 44 basic Reflex save). If a creature critically fails, the stages of all diseases it has increase by 1. The harrophage can't use Biobombardment again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Noxichor","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","virulent"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 40 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Enfeebled 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> enfeebled 2 and Slowed 1 (2 rounds)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> As stage 2, and the creature experiences coughing fits and burning vision. The harrophage is Concealed from the target afflicted with noxichor and if the creature afflicted with noxichor is undetected or unnoticed to the harrophage, it becomes observed by the harrophage (2 rounds)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> As stage 3 (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> dead.</p>"},{"n":"Ossiophage","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","virulent"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 40 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> –5-foot status penalty to all Speeds (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> –10-foot status penalty to all its Speeds (2 rounds)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> –15-foot status penalty to all its Speeds (3 rounds)</p>"},{"n":"Red Haze","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 40 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 6d6 poison damage (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 8d6 poison damage (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 10d6 poison damage (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> 10d6 poison damage and take a –1 status penalty to all saves vs. disease.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/fyUXpBhc4PENZ3Ea":{"lang":["Common","Truespeech"],"notes":{"saves":"–2 status penalty to all saves vs. emotion effects"},"abilities":[{"n":"+4 Bonus to Sense Motive","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Get Them!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The hatemonger takes damage from a successful Strike or spell attack roll</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hatemonger directs a follower to get revenge. They choose one ally of 13th level or lower within 30 feet. That ally either Strides toward or makes a Strike against the triggering creature. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward any creature's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hatemonger can take on the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid. This doesn't change their Speed or their attack and damage modifiers with their Strikes, but it might change the damage type their Strikes deal.</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Echo Chamber","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> At least two creatures within 30 feet are frightened</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hatemonger feeds on fear. All frightened creatures within 30 feet take 7d6 mental damage (DC 33 basic Will save). The hatemonger gains a number of temporary Hit Points equal to the highest damage a single creature takes from this effect, and then can't use Echo Chamber again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Stoke Hatred","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hatemonger inspires fear, hatred, and violence. Each creature within 30 feet must attempt a DC 33 Will save. A creature that succeeds at the saving throw is temporarily immune to Stoke Hatred for 1 hour.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> For 1 round, the target gains a +2 status bonus on damage rolls and takes a –1 status penalty to AC. Effect: Stoke Hatred (Success)</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target becomes Frightened 2. The target can't reduce their frightened condition at the end of their turn unless it used a hostile action in that turn. While they are frightened, they gain a +4 status bonus on damage rolls. Effect: Stoke Hatred (Failure)</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the target is Confused for as long as it remains frightened.</p>"},{"n":"Willing Hate","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>After spending a minute talking to a willing creature, the hatemonger can amplify the creature's hatred. The target receives a +2 status bonus to Intimidation checks and damage rolls against people that they hate; this increases to a +4 status bonus against creatures that are frightened from an effect that they caused. However, whenever the target gains the frightened condition, the condition's value is 1 higher than normal. All attempts to Coerce or Lie to the target in an attempt to stoke hatred receive a result that is one degree of success higher than what was rolled. These effects last until the target makes a meaningful attempt to assist someone that they hate.</p><p>Effect: Willing Hate</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/VLVwalP4yKDZ0iAV":{"lang":["Common","Hemadae","Can't speak"],"abilities":[{"n":"Cold Contractions","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first time each round a hemadae drone takes cold damage, their metal plates recede and expose vulnerable points. They gain weakness 5 to piercing until the end of their next turn.</p><p>Effect: Cold Contractions</p>"},{"n":"Weld","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The hemadae drone's last action was a successful mandibles Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The drone disgorges superheated metal to weld their target to the ground. They attempt a Crafting vs. Fortitude DC check against the target's Fortitude DC. If the creature is not standing on a surface, it can take fire damage from this ability but can't become Grabbed or Restrained.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes 4d6 fire damage and is restrained until the end of the overseer's next turn or until they Escape.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 2d6 fire damage and is grabbed until the end of the drone's next turn or until they Escape</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>"},{"n":"Ferrodermia","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","disease","incapacitation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 25 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Clumsy 1 (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> clumsy 1 and Fatigued (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Clumsy 2, fatigued, and a –10-foot circumstance penalty to speed (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Paralyzed (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> petrified in metal (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 6</strong> death, and the victim's body transforms into a new hemadae drone that flies off to join other of their kind.</p>"},{"n":"Revolting Excretion","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hemadae drone sprays digestive fluids from their abdomen in a 15-foot cone, dealing 2d12 acid damage (DC 25 basic Reflex save). Each creature that fails the save is also Sickened 1 (or Sickened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ruNtTaxqgeJBRwRk":{"lang":["Common","Hemadae","Can't speak"],"abilities":[{"n":"Cold Contractions","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first time each round a hemadae overseer takes cold damage, their metal plates recede and expose vulnerable points. They gain weakness 10 to piercing until the end of their next turn.</p><p>Effect: Cold Contractions</p>"},{"n":"Experimental Defenses","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The hemadae overseer is targeted by an attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hemadae overseer interposes a defensive gadget in the way of the attack. The attack targets their Crafting DC instead of their AC. If the attack hits, the gadget explodes, dealing 5d4 piercing damage in a 5-foot emanation, and the overseer can't use Experimental Defenses again until they spend 10 minutes creating a new defensive gadget.</p>"},{"n":"Clamp Prey","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hemadae overseer makes a mandibles Strike against up to three different creatures. The attacks count toward the hemadae overseer's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after they make all attacks.</p>"},{"n":"Exothermic Expulsion","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hemadae overseer unleashes a blast of flame from their abdomen that deals 10d6 fire damage in a 30-foot line (DC 28 basic Reflex save). They can't use exothermic expulsion again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Ferrodermia","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","disease","incapacitation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 28 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Clumsy 1 (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> clumsy 1 and Fatigued (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Clumsy 2, fatigued, and a –10-foot circumstance penalty to speed (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Paralyzed (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> petrified in metal (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 6</strong> death, and the victim's body transforms into a new hemadae drone that flies off to join other of their kind.</p>"},{"n":"Weld","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The hemadae overseer's last action was a successful mandibles Strike or Clamp Prey</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hemadae overseer disgorges superheated metal to weld foes to the ground. They attempt a Crafting vs. Fortitude DC check against the Fortitude DC of each creature hit by their mandibles Strike, including all creatures hit during Clamp Prey. Creatures that are not standing on a surface can take fire damage from this ability but can't become Grabbed or Restrained.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes 4d8 fire damage and is restrained until the end of the overseer's next turn or until they Escape.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 2d8 fire damage and is grabbed until the end of the overseer's next turn or until they Escape</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is unaffected.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/z61Fi3Vg5oQ7G1Ub":{"lang":["Common","Hemadae","can only speak hemadae aloud, Telepathy 500 feet, Truespeech"],"notes":{"per":"hivesense (precise) 500 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Cold Contractions","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The first time each round a hemadae overseer takes cold damage, their metal plates recede and expose vulnerable points. They gain weakness 10 to piercing until the end of their next turn.</p><p>Effect: Cold Contractions</p>"},{"n":"Ferrodermia","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["arcane","disease","incapacitation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 30 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Clumsy 1 (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> clumsy 1 and Fatigued (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Clumsy 2, fatigued, and a –10-foot circumstance penalty to speed (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> Paralyzed (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> Petrified in metal (1 day)</p><p><strong>Stage 6</strong> death, and the victim's body transforms into a new hemadae drone that flies off to join other of their kind.</p>"},{"n":"Hivesense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["arcane","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>A hemadae queen can feel the minds of nearby members of their hive, detecting their locations as a precise sense.</p>"},{"n":"Assimilate","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature uses a concentrate action within 60 feet of the hemadae queen</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The queen assaults the mind of the triggering creature, dealing 2d6 mental damage (DC 30 basic Will save). On a failure, the queen puppets the creature's muscles to move them 10 feet in any direction (or 20 feet on a critical failure); this is forced movement. This movement does not disrupt the action, but it might move the creature out of range of their intended target. Cold Contractions As hemadae drone, except the piercing weakness is 10.</p>"},{"n":"Absorb the Fallen","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","healing"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The hemadae queen is adjacent to a dead hemadae and is not at full Hit Points</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hemadae queen absorbs the body into their own, regaining 5d8 healing Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Instruments of War","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hemadae queen fires one of the four cannons affixed to their abdomen. Creatures in a 50-foot line take 6d6 damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). Each cannon deals a different damage type and has additional effect on a critical failure. She can instead choose to fire two cannons simultaneously; if she does, she can't use Instruments of War again for 1d4 rounds.</p><p><strong>Cannon 1</strong> 6d6 acid, Sickened 1 on a critical failure</p><p><strong>Cannon 2</strong> 6d6 bludgeoning, knocked Prone on a critical failure</p><p><strong>Cannon 3</strong> 6d6 fire, 1d10 persistent fire on a critical failure</p><p><strong>Cannon 4</strong> 6d6 piercing, 1d10 persistent bleed on a critical failure.</p>"},{"n":"Mind over Metal","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hemadae queen releases a mental pulse in a 40-foot emanation that harms their enemies but inspires their minions. The screech deals 12d6 mental damage to non-hemadae creatures in the area (DC 28 basic Will save). Hemadae in the area can instead use a reaction to Fly, Step, or Stride; one hemadae in the area, of the hive queen's choice, can instead use a reaction to Strike. The hive queen can't use Mind over Metal for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/E4J2OpbzIKzBpEaM":{"lang":["Common","Cryan","Fey","Melodian","Sussuran"],"notes":{"per":"snow vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Snow Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Snow doesn't impair the hibernal's vision; they ignore concealment from snowfall.</p>"},{"n":"Blizzard Cloak","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A hibernal's passage leaves snowdrifts in their wake, making any square they move through difficult terrain to any non-hibernal until the start of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Eager Audience","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hibernal takes a –2 circumstance penalty to their Will saves and DCs against mental effects with the auditory or visual traits, as well as against attempts to Fascinate them.</p>"},{"n":"Snow Clone","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The hibernal takes damage from a physical attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The damage is reduced by 5 and the hibernal can immediately Step. If the attack was a melee Strike made from an adjacent square, the attacker takes 5 cold damage.</p>"},{"n":"Wintry Gust","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The hibernal Strides or Flies. Any creature adjacent to them at any point during the movement takes 4d6 cold damage (DC 17 basic Fortitude save). They can't use Wintry Gust again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/NGT6hgSBWtmpqwXh":{"lang":["Aklo","Astral","Speak in dreams, Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"lore":[["Dreamlands Lore",22]],"notes":{"per":"dreamsense (precise) 100 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Dreamsense (PRecise) 100 Feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>Hollow kraits clearly perceive all dreaming creatures within the listed range, as well as the content of the dreams. Any such creature becomes a valid target for the swarm's Dream Message and Nightmare spells.</p>"},{"n":"Speak in Dreams","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A hollow krait swarm can use telepathy on sleeping creatures without waking them up.</p>"},{"n":"Courage Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Hollow kraits revel in the fear they spread but are repulsed by bravery. The first time each round that the swarm is within range of an effect that grants creatures a bonus specifically against fear (such as a bard's courageous anthem), they take 3d6 mental damage. The damage can also be triggered when a creature critically succeeds at a saving throw against a fear effect or performs an act of exceptional bravery.</p>"},{"n":"Frightful Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>60 feet DC 26 Will</p><hr><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Nightmare Mind","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the hollow krait swarm is targeted by an effect with the fear trait, the swarm regains 4d8 healing Hit Points and is Quickened for 1 round instead of the normal effects. It can use the extra action from quickened to Stride or use Psyche Leech.</p>"},{"n":"The Abyss Gazes Back","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature that the hollow krait swarm can see uses a mental effect against the swarm</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The magic gives the triggering creature unwelcome insight into the swarm's hivemind. The triggering creature must attempt a DC 29 Will save.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is frightened 2, and the swarm is unaffected by the triggering mental effect.</p>"},{"n":"Psyche Leech","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The swarm deals 4d6 mental damage to each creature in its space (DC 29 basic Will save). A creature that fails the save is Stupefied 1 for 1 minute (Stupefied 2 on a critical failure). If a frightened creature is damaged by Psyche Leech, the value of the creature's frightened condition doesn't decrease at the end of its next turn and the hollow krait swarm regains 2d6 healing Hit Points. Sleeping creatures don't awaken as a result of damage from Psyche Leech unless they succeed on the Will save.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/eMdpcl5neTpRJ7CE":{"lang":["Khaotan","Truespeech"],"notes":{"speed":"spatial hop"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An interstitial sludge can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Disrupt Teleportation","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 120 feet of the interstitial sludge uses a teleportation effect</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The interstitial sludge unravels the magic, pulling from the void between the planes. The interstitial sludge attempts a counteract check (counteract modifier +30), with the following additional effects.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The triggering action is disrupted, and the creature using it is instead teleported within reach of the interstitial sludge.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The triggering action is disrupted, and the creature using it is instead teleported in a random square within 120 feet of the interstitial sludge but outside its reach, determined by the GM.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> A violent magical feedback shakes the interstitial sludge's essence, leaving Off-Guard until the end of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Light Weakness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If an interstitial sludge is hit by an attack with the light trait or fails a saving throw against an effect with the light trait, it is Sickened 1 in addition to the normal effects (Sickened 2 on a critical hit or critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Retreat to the In-Between","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The interstitial sludge is reduced to 0 Hit Points</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Instead of dying, the interstitial sludge is banished back to the space between planes. It casts 4th-rank confusion on all creatures within its reach. Creatures that critically fail their DC 38 Will save must roll a DC 38 Reflex save, on a failure, they are drawn into the space between planes; this is an incapacitation and teleportation effect.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Steal Vision","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["darkness","occult","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by a sludge ball Strike must succeed at a DC 36 Fortitude save or be Blinded for 1 round. While the creature is blinded, the interstitial sludge can see using the creature's typical visual senses, but the interstitial sludge loses its immunity to visual effects.</p>"},{"n":"Greater Constrict","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>0 bludgeoning, basic Fortitude</p>\n<hr>\n<p><p>The monster deals the listed amount of damage to any number of creatures Grabbed or Restrained by it. Each of those creatures can attempt a basic Fortitude save with the listed DC. A creature that fails this save falls Unconscious, and a creature that succeeds is then temporarily immune to falling unconscious from Greater Constrict for 1 minute.</p></p>"},{"n":"Spatial Hop","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The interstitial sludge gathers its body into a 15-foot square that includes at least one of its initial spaces. It then picks a square within 10 feet of that 15-foot square to move into, and then finally redistributes its body into 9 contiguous squares that include the chosen square.</p>"},{"n":"Tendril Explosion","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The interstitial sludge makes a pseudopod Strike against all creatures within its reach, as well as all other creatures within 30 feet; it takes a –2 penalty on the Strikes against creatures that aren't in its reach. These attacks count toward the interstitial sludge's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after it makes all its attacks. For any attack that hits, the interstitial sludge can choose to teleport the creature struck in any square inside its reach.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/XHQyGD12H4GPyKZy":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Diabolic","Empyrean"],"lore":[["Architecture Lore",28]],"notes":{"speed":"relentless tunneler"},"abilities":[{"n":"Adaptive Immunity","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":["divine","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The invulnerabug gains immunity to one of the following damage types of their choice; acid, bleed, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, force, mental, piercing, poison, precision, slashing, sonic, or void. This immunity lasts until the invulnerabug uses this ability again.</p>"},{"n":"Just Won't Die","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per day</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The invulnerabug would be reduced to 0 HP, or it would otherwise die or be destroyed</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The invulnerabug is reduced to 1 HP and doesn't die. If they have not yet cast Indestructibility, they cast it immediately.</p>"},{"n":"Prone Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When an invulnerabug is Prone, they lose their resistance to all damage; this does not impact any immunity granted by Adaptive Immunity.</p>"},{"n":"Burrow Into Flesh","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The invulnerabug's last action was a successful mandibles Strike against a Small or larger creature and the invulnerabug is not currently burrowing inside another creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The invulnerabug attempts to burrow into the target. The target must attempt a DC 37 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 3d6 persistent bleed damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The invulnerabug burrows inside the target. The target takes 6d6 persistent bleed damage. While the invulnerabug remains inside the target, the target is Off-Guard to the invulnerabug, the invulnerabug's mandible Strikes deal an additional 2d6 precision damage to it, and it can't end the persistent bleed damage. At the end of each of its turns, the target can attempt a DC 37 Fortitude save to expel the invulnerabug from its body. Additionally, the target or an adjacent creature can attempt a DC 40 Medicine check to Administer First Aid check to stop the bleeding, removing the invulnerabug on a success.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the target takes 10d6 persistent bleed damage and checks to remove the bug take a –2 circumstance penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Unyielding Maw","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The invulnerabug's mandibles are made of magically enhanced adamantine. They ignore up 20 points of a target's Hardness and up to 20 of their resistance to piercing damage.</p>"},{"n":"Relentless Tunneler","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The invulnerabug can Burrow through any physical substance with 20 or fewer Hardness, including wood, stone, and metal. They always leave tunnels behind when they do so.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/36omoZn0hs38loHU":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Draconic","Empyrean","Fey","Telepathy 60 feet"],"lore":[["Alcohol Lore",13]],"notes":{"saves":"+2 status to all saves vs. fear"},"abilities":[{"n":"Expunge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 30 feet fails a saving throw to reduce its sickened condition</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kabrus forces the target to spew unholy bile in a 15-foot cone. The kabrus chooses the direction of the cone, which can't include the target. The target and each creature in the cone take 2d6 acid damage (DC 22 basic Fortitude save). After spewing the bile, the value of the creature's sickened condition is reduced by 1.</p>"},{"n":"Life of the Party","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. Creatures in the aura other than demons take a –1 circumstance penalty to Will saves, Perception checks, and saving throws against drugs.</p>"},{"n":"Sobriety Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a kabrus is targeted by a spell or other effect that counteracts or resists poison, they take 4d6 mental damage.</p>"},{"n":"Kabrus Brew","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 22 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 8 hours</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Sickened 1, Stupefied 1, +2 status bonus to saves against fear effects (6 hours)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Drained 1, sickened 1, stupefied 1 (1 hour)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Drained 2, sickened 1, stupefied 1 (1 hour)</p>"},{"n":"Drinking Contest","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","divine","emotion","linguistic","manipulate","mental"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The kabrus downs a conjured flagon of kabrus brew, then dares a creature within 30 feet to drink one too. The target must attempt a DC 22 Will save.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target must use its first action on its next turn to drink a flagon of kabrus brew, which manifests before it as part of that action. The dose doesn't require a free hand to drink, and can be drunk even if the creature is sickened.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target is compelled to outdo the kabrus. As on a failure, but it must spend two actions to drink two doses.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Azu15bQ29LefIGUe":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","Melodian","Sakvroth","Spirituan"],"gear":["Musical Instrument (Virtuoso handheld)"],"notes":{"saves":" +2 status to all saves vs. magic","speed":"(earth and wood only)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The kunthalaka takes on the appearance of any Medium humanoid. This doesn't change the kunthalaka's Speed or their attack and damage modifiers with its Strikes but might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning). They lose their burrow speed and typically lose their mandibles Strike unless the humanoid form has a similar unarmed attack. They also lose their all-around vision and can't use Stridulation.</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"+2 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Kunthalaka Neurotoxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 26 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Clumsy 1 and Stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Clumsy 2 and Stupefied 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> clumsy 2, stupefied 2, and Slowed 1 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Stridulation","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The kunthalaka rubs their mandibles together to emit a hypnotic tone. Each non-rakshasa creature within 60 feet must attempt a DC 26 Will save. The effects of Stridulation last for 1 round, but if the kunthalaka uses this ability again on subsequent rounds, they extend this duration by 1 round for any creature already affected.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is immune to Stridulation for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Fascinated by the kunthalaka.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the fascinated condition doesn't end if the kunthalaka uses hostile actions against the creature.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/El0xgIHXqaFZIgKD":{"lang":["Aklo","Astral","Chthonian","Common","Diabolic","Fey","Jotun"],"lore":[["Dreamlands Lore",17]],"notes":{"saves":"–2 status vs. effects that can immobilize"},"abilities":[{"n":"Coven","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A lace hag adds Never Mind, Sleep, and Web to their coven's spells. Their spell DC when leading a coven is 25.</p><hr><p><p>This monster can form a coven with two or more other creatures who also have the coven ability. This involves performing an 8-hour ceremony with all prospective coven members. After the coven is formed, each of its members gains elite adjustments, adjusting their levels accordingly. Coven members can sense other members' locations and conditions by spending a single action, which has the concentrate trait, and can sense what another coven member is sensing as a two-action activity, which has the concentrate trait as well.</p>\n<p>Covens also grant spells and rituals to their members, but these can be cast only in cooperation between three coven members who are all within 30 feet of one another. A coven member can contribute to a coven spell with a single action that has the concentrate trait. If two coven members have contributed these actions within the last round, a third member can cast a coven spell on her turn by spending the normal spellcasting actions. A coven can cast its coven spells an unlimited number of times but can cast only one coven spell each round. All covens grant the 8th-rank Cursed Metamorphosis spell and all the following spells, which the coven can cast at any rank up to 5th: Augury, Charm, Clairaudience, Clairvoyance, Dream Message, Illusory Disguise, Illusory Scene, Scouting Eye, and Talking Corpse. Individual creatures with the coven ability also grant additional spells to any coven they join. A coven can also cast the Control Weather ritual, with a DC of 23 instead of the standard DC.</p>\n<p>If a coven member's departure or death brings the coven below three members, the remaining members keep their elite adjustments for 24 hours, but without enough members to contribute the necessary actions, they can't cast coven spells.</p></p>"},{"n":"In My Domain","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The lace hag has stitched together a special realm in the Dreamlands where their hag nature is heightened. While in their domain, they gain weakness 10 to cold iron and the In My Domain spells.</p>"},{"n":"Stitch in Time","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The hag's last action was a successful claw Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature is bound in lace. It must succeed at a DC 21 Reflex save or become Immobilized and Slowed 1 until it Escapes.</p>"},{"n":"Phase Snare","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per hour</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lace hag is not on the Ethereal Plane</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hag calls upon their pet spiders in the Ethereal Plane to weave a 10-foot radius web, then phases the web into reality within 30 feet of her for 1 minute. All creatures that start their turn in the web's area must succeed at a DC 25 Reflex save or be Immobilized and Slowed 1 until they Escape or the web in their square is destroyed. Each square of the web can be destroyed by a single attack or effect that deals at least 20 slashing damage or 10 fire damage. A square has AC 5, and it automatically fails its saving throws.</p>"},{"n":"Silken Song","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lace hag is adjacent to a square of web from Phase Snare</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hag strums a gossamer-soft melody that casts 4th-rank Sleep (DC 23 Will). Creatures Immobilized by the web take a –2 circumstance penalty on their save.</p>"},{"n":"Dreamcatcher","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["curse","incapacitation","mental","occult","sleep"],"f":"","d":"<p>If a creature falls asleep while in contact with lace that the hag has spun, the fabric turns into a ribbon adornment and fuses with the creature's body unless it succeeds at a DC 23 Will save. From that point on, whenever the creature sleeps, its dream-self appears at a random location within the lace hag's domain. If the creature's dream-self is dead, Immobilized, or in contact with the lace hag, it can't awaken. Others can enter the lace hag's domain by sleeping while in contact with the dreamer's physical body. The accursed lace can be cut away using the lace hag's dreamshears with a successful DC 23 Crafting check; this is a two-action activity with the manipulate trait.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/8NtyayCkCOtng4lZ":{"lang":["Draconic","Fey","Can't speak any language"],"notes":{"speed":"storm walk"},"abilities":[{"n":"Hounding Jaws","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature the laelaps has designated with Hunt Prey Strides or takes an action with the teleportation trait while within the laelaps's reach</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The laelaps makes a jaws Strike against its prey. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the laelaps's multiple attack penalty. If this Strike hits, the distance covered by the Stride or teleportation effect is reduced by half. If it critically hits, the laelaps' prey stays in place, though other creatures affected by their action can still teleport or move.</p>"},{"n":"Howling Pursuit","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","auditory","emotion","fear","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The laelaps rushes forward, propelled by screaming wind that strikes fear into those that hear it. The laelaps Strides twice. If the laelaps passes within 5 feet of an enemy during this movement, that creature must attempt a DC 23 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> No effect.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Hunt Prey","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The laelaps designates a single creature it can see and hear, or one it is Tracking, as its prey. The laelaps gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception and Survival checks when Seeking and Tracking its prey. The first time each round that the laelaps hits its prey with a Strike, it deals an additional 1d8 precision damage. These effects last until it uses Hunt Prey again.</p>"},{"n":"Relentless Pursuit","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per minute</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The laelaps is grappled, Immobilized, Paralyzed, Petrified, Restrained, Slowed, or Stunned</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The laelaps removes any one of the listed conditions, but increases its drained value by 1 for 1 hour. This increase is cumulative with other uses of Relentless Pursuit, to a maximum of Drained 4. The laelaps can take this action even when a condition would normally prevent it from taking actions.</p>"},{"n":"Storm Walk","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["air","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The laelaps can walk on air as if it were solid ground while in an area of stormy or violent weather. It can ascend or descend at a maximum of a 45-degree angle.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/KdrqXxlSX9D7ATUI":{"lang":["Common","Daemonic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Thoughtsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The lethodaemon senses all non-mindless creatures at the listed range. When a lethodaemon detects a creature with thoughtsense, they also determine if the creature's memories have been magically modified, whether by the lethodaemon or another creature. If the other creature was attempting to be subtle about their manipulation, the lethodaemon must succeed at a Perception check against the DC of the memory-altering ability in order to detect it.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Drain Memory","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The lethodaemon rips away their victim's memories, leaving small gaps that disorient it. When a lethodaemon damages a creature with a melee Strike, the creature must succeed at a DC 33 Will save or become Stupefied 1. Further exposures to Drain Memory increase the stupefied condition's value by 1 on a failed save, to a maximum of Stupefied 4. The stupefied value reduces by 1 every hour.</p>"},{"n":"Mists of the Styx","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","water"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The lethodaemon calls upon the forgetful mists of the River Styx, gaining a 30-foot aura that clouds the minds of creatures within it for 3 rounds. All creatures that start their turn in the aura must attempt a Will save against Drain Memory. The mists are transparent to creatures whose minds are clear, but murky to those whose minds are clouded. All creatures within the aura become Concealed to stupefied creatures, and all creatures outside the mist become concealed to stupefied creatures within it.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/TgadmhyFfMq7PwIm":{"lang":["Common","Can't speak any language"],"abilities":[{"n":"Invigoration","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Proximity to fire invigorates the vital essence within a lifespark bandit. Whenever a lifespark bandit's fire immunity negates fire damage, the lifespark bandit becomes invigorated for one minute, granting them 2d6 temporary Hit Points and a +1 status bonus on Fortitude saving throws. When the invigoration ends, any remaining temporary Hit Points are lost. A lifespark bandit can't become invigorated from their own flames or those of another lifespark bandit.</p><p>Effect: Invigoration</p>"},{"n":"Scorch","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature hits the lifespark bandit with a melee attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> An arc of fire leaps and scorches the triggering creature, dealing 1d8 fire damage (DC 18 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Unwanted Addition","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fire","manipulate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lifespark bandit is invigorated</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The lifespark bandit sneaks a burning piece of vital essence onto an adjacent creature. The lifespark bandit must attempt a Thievery vs. Perception DC check against the target's Perception DC. On a success, the target takes 1d6 persistent fire damage and the lifespark bandit gains a +2 status bonus on damage rolls against this target for as long as this persistent damage lasts, and the lifespark bandit is no longer invigorated.</p>"},{"n":"Vital Theft","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lifespark bandit is not invigorated and has just hit a creature with their claws Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The lifespark bandit digs their claws into the creature, attempting to steal its vital essence. The lifespark bandit attempts a Thievery vs. Fortitude DC check against their target's Fortitude DC. On a success, the lifespark bandit becomes invigorated for 1 minute and the target takes 1d6 persistent void damage. On a critical success, the target also becomes Drained 1 for 1 hour.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/aWNt1vaZ7VJK0P63":{"lang":["Common","Luxan","Pyric","Spirituan"],"gear":["Lantern","Lantern (Hooded)","Repair Toolkit","Lamplighter's Pole"],"notes":{"ac":"(24 with lantern raised)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Dissolve in Darkness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a lightling is hit by an attack roll from or fails a saving throw against a darkness or shadow effect, they take 2d6 spirit damage in addition to the normal effects. They also take 2d6 spirit damage whenever they begin their turn in an area of dim light or darkness.</p>"},{"n":"Lantern Keeper","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["fire","light","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>Any lantern held by a lightling is magically empowered by the lightling's elemental essence, allowing it to be used as a shield that grants a +2 circumstance bonus to AC when the lightling Raises a Shield (Hardness 5, HP 30, BT 15). The lantern sheds magical bright light out to 60 feet and dim light for a further 60 feet beyond that. If the lantern is broken, the radius decreases to 15 feet of bright light and 15 feet of dim light. The lantern's light can be counteracted with an air, cold, darkness, shadow, or water effect (counteract DC 22), or snuffed out with a single successful DC 25 Thievery check to Disable a Device. Either method extinguishes the lantern until the lightling relights the lantern with an Interact action.</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block (Special)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the lightling uses a burning lantern to Shield Block an attack from an adjacent creature, that creature must succeed on a DC 19 Fortitude save or be Blinded for 1 round; this secondary effect has the light, occult, and visual traits.</p><hr><p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Focus Light","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","fire","light","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lightling's lantern is lit</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The lightling focuses a beam of light that travels to the edge of the lantern's range (typically 120 feet if the lantern isn't broken). All creatures in a line take 4d4 fire damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save). Creatures in dim light treat the result of their saving throw as one degree of success better.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/xrWNODagL0a9Jwbq":{"lang":["Astral","Chronan","Common","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Creator Lore",21]],"notes":{"ac":"all-around vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"All-Around Vision","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster can see in all directions simultaneously and therefore can't be flanked.</p></p>"},{"n":"Susceptible to the Future","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>lingering regrets can only exist in the past and react viscerally to being displaced in the future. Whenever a lingering regret is Quickened, their body congeals. They gain no extra actions from being quickened, instead losing their resistance to all damage.</p>"},{"n":"Return to the Past","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 60 feet of the lingering regret Steps or Strides</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The lingering regret launches the creature backward in time, returning it to the square it was in at the beginning of its Step or Stride unless it succeeds at a DC 26 Will save.</p>"},{"n":"Stagnant Sorrows","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The lingering regret's negative emotions flare up as they slice into nearby creatures with fractured moments of time laden with their deepest sorrows. All creatures in a 20-foot burst take 4d6 mental plus 3d6 slashing damage (DC 25 basic Reflex save). Squares in the burst are littered with broken shards of time, becoming difficult terrain for all creatures except the lingering regret until the beginning of the lingering regret's next turn. Creatures that end their turn in one of these squares must succeed at a DC 25 Will save or be Sickened 1 from the rush of emotions they emit (Sickened 2 on a critical failure). The lingering regret can't use Stagnant Sorrows again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Cruel Memories","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that takes damage from a regret's caress or regret's lash Strike is shoved back into memories of moments it regrets. It must succeed a DC 25 Will save or become Slowed 1.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/jDk6LrugCxgKnuxN":{"lang":["Common","Thalassic"],"abilities":[{"n":"Puddle From","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In its resting state, a liquefied's body is an immobile puddle, and other creatures can freely enter its space. A liquefied can temporarily solidify through applied pressure or quick impacts onto it. At the end of the liquefied's turn, if it was not exposed to any sources of pressure or movement since the end of its previous turn, such as taking force or physical damage or moving (either with an action or forced movement), it reverts to an immobile puddle.</p>"},{"n":"Bounce Back","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A melee attack that deals force or physical damage critically hits the liquefied</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The liquefied returns the momentum back to the attacker, attempting a fist Strike against it and adding any additional damage from Stored Momentum. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the liquefied's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Slow Movement Weakness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The liquefied's body's dramatic reaction to sudden impacts is lessened when the attacker's movements are slowed. Slowed creatures who Strike the liquefied with a melee attack ignore its resistance to bludgeoning and don't trigger its Bounce Back reaction.</p>"},{"n":"Stored Momentum","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A liquefied retains some of the force from its enemy's attacks and uses it to empower its own Strikes. Each time the liquefied takes force or physical damage, it gains a +2 circumstance bonus to damage on its next fist Strike. This bonus is cumulative, to a maximum bonus of +8 damage. The bonus damage decreases by 2 for every action the liquefied takes on its turn before Striking.</p><p>Effect: Stored Momentum</p>"},{"n":"Solidify and Devour","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A Medium or smaller creature steps onto the liquefied's space</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The liquefied is in its puddle form</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The liquefied attempts an Athletics check to pull the creature into its body. This functions as Swallow Whole against a Grabbed creature, except it does not have the attack trait (2d10+2 bludgeoning damage, Rupture 17).</p>"},{"n":"Disperse Pressure","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["move","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The liquefied expands its body out into a 20-foot radius puddle. All creatures in the area take 5d6 bludgeoning damage and must attempt a DC 26 Reflex save. The liquefied then gathers itself back up to occupy any 10-foot square within the radius.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is pushed up to 5 feet toward the outer edge of the puddle; this is forced movement.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature takes double damage and is pushed up to 10 feet.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/MZYS3YF9i5hdCkCL":{"abilities":[{"n":"Voltaic Charges","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The living lightning rod is Charged 2 at the beginning of the encounter.</p>"},{"n":"Electrical Absorbance","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the living lightning rod is targeted by or in the area of an attack or effect that has the electricity trait or deals electricity damage, the living lightning rod is Charged.</p>"},{"n":"Voltaic Overload","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["arcane","electricity"],"f":"","d":"<p>If a living lightning rod would be charged when it is already charged 3, it immediately vents the excess charge in an explosion. All creatures within 30 feet of the living lightning rod take 10d12 electricity damage (DC 36 basic Reflex save). Afterward, the living lightning rod loses the charged condition, is Stunned 3, and takes a –2 circumstance penalty to AC until the end of its next turn.</p><p>Effect: Voltaic Overload</p>"},{"n":"Lightning Rod","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature or area within 30 feet is targeted by an effect with the electricity trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The living lightning rod attempts a counteract check against the effect (counteract modifier +30). If the counteract check succeeds, the living lightning rod is Charged.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Gather Charge","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","electricity"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The living lightning is charged. All creatures adjacent to the living lightning rod take 2d12 electricity damage (DC 34 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Magnetic Pull","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The living lightning rod is charged and its last action was a successful lightning coil Strike against a creature within 60 feet</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The living lightning rod pulls the targeted creature toward itself; the creature must attempt a DC 36 Fortitude save to determine the distance.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is pulled 15 feet.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 30 feet and knocked Prone.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 60 feet and knocked prone.</p>"},{"n":"Thundergrip","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The living lightning rod is charged and has a creature Grabbed or Restrained in one of its fists</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The living lightning rod deals 2d12+10 electricity damage to the creature (DC 36 basic Fortitude) and extends the duration of the grabbed or restrained condition until the end of the living lightning rod's next turn. The value of the Living Lightning Rod's charged condition reduces by 1.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/hXhEADjr7NE2YMf8":{"lang":["Common","Cryan","Daemonic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"notes":{"per":"fear sense (varies) 1 mile"},"abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Fear Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>A lyodaemon can sense the minds of frightened creatures within 1 mile as a vague sense and within 60 feet as an imprecise sense.</p>"},{"n":"Curse of Lonely Death","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","curse","divine","emotion","fear","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>60 feet. A lyodaemon's sheer presence fills the mind with a primal fear of being alone. Whenever a non-fiend creature begins its turn in the aura, it must attempt a DC 29 Will save. On a failure, whenever the creature starts or ends its turn, it becomes Frightened 1 unless it is adjacent to an ally that it isn't hidden to it. It can't reduce its frightened condition at the end of its turn unless it is adjacent to a visible ally. The curse of lonely death persists for 1 day or until the lyodaemon that caused it is slain, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Frigid Fear","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["cold","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A frightened creature starts its turn within 60 feet of the lyodaemon</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature takes 1d6 persistent cold damage and takes a status penalty to its Speeds equal to 10 times the value of its frightened condition until end of its turn. If this penalty reaches or exceeds the creature's Speed, it is Immobilized.</p>"},{"n":"Crushing Sweep","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The lyodaemon makes a sledge fist Strike against all creatures within reach, taking a –2 penalty on the attack rolls. These attacks count toward the lyodaemon's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after they make all their attacks. Additionally, they can use Improved Push on every target they hit.</p>"},{"n":"Illusion of Isolation","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine","illusion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The lyodaemon tricks the senses of its foes, cloaking allies from their sight. All non-fiend creatures within 30 feet take 5d8 mental damage and must attempt a DC 32 Will save, with the following effects. A creature that succeeds on the saving throw is temporarily immune to Illusion of Isolation for 1 hour.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and the creature's allies are all Concealed from it for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and the creature's allies are all hidden from it for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and the creature's allies are all hidden from it for 1 minute. The creature can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns to end this effect early.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Push","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Improved Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/k4QJcBTET0kPQMdI":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Jotun","Spirituan","Thalassic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Ward","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The matsugami is bound to a stretch of coastline. They can merge with or emerge from their ward as a single action with the concentrate trait. While merged, they are Immobilized, but they recover Hit Points each minute as if they spent an entire day resting.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Disorienting Whirlpool","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The matsugami Swims twice, gathering the churning waters in their wake and pooling them around their fists. They then make a fist Strike. If the Strike hits, it catches the target in a condensed whirlpool, dealing an additional 3d6 bludgeoning damage and making the target Off-Guard until the beginning of its next turn. If the Strike misses, the whirlpool spreads out into the surrounding water in a 15-foot radius around the target. Until the start of the matsugami's next turn, any creature that enters or begins its turn in the whirlpool must succeed at a DC 40 Reflex save or take 3d6 bludgeoning damage and be off-guard until the beginning of its next turn. The whirlpool's waters are difficult to traverse, requiring a successful DC 35 Athletics check to Swim. Matsugami are immune to Disorienting Whirlpool.</p>"},{"n":"Flying Kick","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The matsugami Strides, makes a Long Jump, then makes a foot Strike. If the matsugami makes a successful Long Jump of at least 20 feet during this action, the strike's damage increases to 3d12+34.</p>"},{"n":"Suplex","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The matsugami has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The matsugami throws the creature, releasing it and dealing 2d10+18 bludgeoning damage (DC 40 basic Fortitude save). If the target is on land, it is knocked Prone; if it is underwater, it is instead Sickened 1 (or Sickened 2 on a failed Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Titan Wrestler","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The matsugami can attempt to Disarm, Grapple, Reposition, Shove, or Trip creatures of up to three sizes larger than them.</p>"},{"n":"Torrential Flurry","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The matsugami makes two fist Strikes. These attacks both count toward their multiple attack penalty, but the penalty doesn't increase until after both attacks.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/CTn9NWjMrAMjdEe5":{"lang":["Common","Melodian"],"gear":["Rapier","Glass Vial (3)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Warning Hum","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A mellifican hive doesn't need to speak to inspire primal fear. They don't take the typical penalty for Demoralizing without using a language.</p>"},{"n":"Gift of Honey","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mellifican hive spends 10 minutes gathering honey from their core and either feeds it to a creature or stores it in a container, allowing it to be consumed later with an Interact action. A living creature who consumes honey regains 1d8 healing Hit Points. A mellifican can't benefit from their own honey, though they can benefit from the honey of another mellifican. The honey remains magical until dawn, after which it becomes normal honey.</p>"},{"n":"Hive Defenses","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While inside the hive, the mellifican swarm lacks the typical weaknesses and immunities granted by the swarm trait (except for swarm mind). If a portion of the swarm leaves the hive, such as when using Swarm Surge, the mellifican hive gains weakness 3 to both area and splash damage.</p>"},{"n":"Harmonic Impalement","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The mellifican hive has just damaged a creature with a rapier Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hive hums in unison, sending harmful vibrations down the rapier that tear at the wound. The target takes 1d6 sonic damage (DC 17 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Swarm Surge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mellifican swarm surges out of the hive to irritate and drive away their foes. Each creature in a 15-foot cone takes 2d4 piercing plus 2 poison damage (DC 17 basic Fortitude save). Creatures that critically fail this saving throw also take 1 persistent poison damage. The mellifican hive can't use Swarm Surge again until they spend one action to recall these wasps to the hive; until they do so, they gain swarm weaknesses as listed in Hive Defenses.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/D9KBrbU35AqlNDCb":{"lang":["Common","Talican"],"notes":{"speed":"phases of matter"},"abilities":[{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"},{"n":"Phases of Matter","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A metallic phase elemental begins the encounter in one of the following forms.</p><p><strong>Gas Form</strong> The elemental is a shimmering cloud of gas. When this form, they can use their shard blast Strike, Phase Change, and Storm of Metal. They also gain a 30-foot fly speed.</p><p><strong>Liquid Form</strong> The elemental is a metallic goop. When in this form, they can use their liquid lash Strike, Phase Change, and Wild Splash. They also gain a 40-foot swim speed.</p><p><strong>Solid Form</strong> The elemental is a solid block of metal. When in this form, they can use their metal fist Strike and Phase Change. They also gain a 30-foot burrow speed and tremorsense (imprecise) 30 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Phase Change","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","metal","polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The metallic phase elemental's molecular structure shifts and vibrates, changing from one of their Phases of Matter to another.</p>"},{"n":"Storm of Metal","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["metal","move"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The metallic phase elemental is in their gas form</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The metallic phase elemental turns into a tornado of metal shards that tear apart all in their path. The metallic phase elemental Flies, passing through the spaces of creatures in their path. Creatures whose spaces the elemental enters during this movement take 4d6 slashing damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save). Creatures that critically fail also take 1d6 persistent bleed damage.</p>"},{"n":"Wild Splash","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The metallic phase elemental is in their liquid form</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The metallic phase elemental makes three liquid lash Strikes at a –2 penalty, each against a different target. These attacks count toward the metallic phase elemental's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after they make all their attacks.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/jUiUSoVJuv4SI0Jj":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Fey","Venenan"],"gear":["Rapier","Mug of Tears"],"abilities":[{"n":"Taunting Tumble","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The mirthless is targeted by a Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mirthless goads their attacker, then Strides up to half their Speed after the Strike resolves. Any ally who hears this taunt can use a reaction to Stride up to half their speed.</p>"},{"n":"Mug of Tears","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The mirthless is adjacent to a Prone creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mirthless makes a Strike against a prone creature's abdomen. If the Strike hits, the mirthless pours a distillate of poisoned tears from their goblet into the creature's mouth. The creature takes 3d6 poison damage (DC 22 Fortitude save). The creature is also slowed for 1 round on a failed saving throw, or for 3 rounds on a critical failure.</p>"},{"n":"Contagious Misery","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The mirthless's weapon begins the encounter covered with a dose of this poison, which originates from their tears. They can reapply the poison with Venom, To Thy Work.</p><p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 22 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1d6 poison damage and falls Prone</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 2d6 poison damage, falls prone, and Frightened 1</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 3d6 poison damage, falls prone, and frightened 1</p>"},{"n":"Surprise Attacker","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>On the first round of combat, if the mirthless rolls Deception or Stealth for initiative, creatures that haven't acted yet are Off-Guard to them.</p>"},{"n":"Venom, To Thy Work","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Weeping openly onto their rapier, the mirthless applies a dose of contagious misery to their weapon.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mirthless's Strikes deal an extra 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/8DD4vJlrctXuKss5":{"notes":{"ac":"(25 when broken), construct armor","speed":"cubic movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A monolithic cube can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Construct Armor (Hardness 10)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Like normal objects, a monolithic cube has Hardness. This Hardness reduces any damage the cube takes by an amount equal to the Hardness. Once a monolithic cube is reduced to fewer than half its Hit Points, or immediately upon being damaged by a critical hit, its construct armor breaks, removing the Hardness, reducing its Armor Class to 25, and activating its mercurial quickness.</p>"},{"n":"Mercurial Quickness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While a monolithic cube's construct armor is broken, it is Quickened. It can only use the additional action from quickened for Crushing Face. Additionally, it gains a mercury jet Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Crushing Face","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A monolithic cube's primary means of both attack and locomotion is to roll over, crushing everything in its path. The monolithic cube Strides. During this Stride, the cube can move into and through the spaces of creatures and objects that are Large or smaller. Unattended objects in the path of a monolithic cube's crushing face automatically take 10d10 bludgeoning damage. Each creature whose space the monolithic cube enters takes 2d10+6 bludgeoning damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save). Wobbling between two faces slightly destabilizes the cube. If the cube uses Crushing Face to move in the opposite direction of its most recent Stride on the same turn, the DC of the Reflex save is reduced to DC 24 basic Reflex .</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature moves to a square of its choice adjacent to the cube.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, moves to a square of its choice adjacent to the cube, and is knocked Prone.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is crushed by the cube, taking double damage. It is knocked prone and Restrained underneath the cube, sharing its space while restrained in this way. A creature can Escape to move to a square of its choice adjacent to the cube. If the cube leaves the creature's space, that creature is no longer restrained.</p>"},{"n":"Unstoppable Roll","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The monolithic cube is unaffected by difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain. Its Speed is always a multiple of 15 (such as 15, 30, or 45). It is unaffected by penalties that would reduce its Speed below 15. Bonuses to speed have no effect unless they would increase its Speed to a new multiple of 15.</p>"},{"n":"Grind","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The monolithic cube deals 2d10+8 bludgeoning damage to each creature currently Restrained by its crushing face (DC 28 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Cubic Movement","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A monolithic cube moves by rolling from one face to another, leaving all of the spaces it previously occupied. As such, it can Stride only in straight lines and in cardinal directions, and it must always move exactly 15 feet. Stepping is a two-action activity for a monolithic cube.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/tTjoslHWcyOZ1UiT":{"notes":{"ac":"(25 when broken), construct armor","speed":"cubic movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"The Die is Cast","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The faces of some monolithic cubes are etched with enormous numerals representing metaphysical concepts. Depending on which number is on the cube's top face, these numerals grant the cube immunity to a certain type of damage, while revealing a weakness to another. The numerals, the concepts they represent, and the immunities and weaknesses of each number follow.</p><p><strong>1. Might:</strong> Immunity to damage dealt by weapons and weakness 10 to spell damage.</p><p><strong>2. Frost:</strong> Immunity to cold damage and weakness 10 to fire damage.</p><p><strong>3. Lightning:</strong> Immunity to electricity damage and weakness 10 to sonic damage.</p><p><strong>4. Thunder:</strong> Immunity to sonic damage and weakness 10 to electricity damage.</p><p><strong>5. Flame:</strong> Immunity to fire damage and weakness 10 to cold damage.</p><p><strong>6. Magic:</strong> Immunity to spell damage and weakness 10 to damage dealt by weapons (apply only once per weapon Strike even if it has damaging property runes or the like).</p>"},{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A monolithic cube can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Construct Armor (Hardness 10)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Like normal objects, a monolithic cube has Hardness. This Hardness reduces any damage the cube takes by an amount equal to the Hardness. Once a monolithic cube is reduced to fewer than half its Hit Points, or immediately upon being damaged by a critical hit, its construct armor breaks, removing the Hardness, reducing its Armor Class to 25, and activating its mercurial quickness.</p>"},{"n":"Mercurial Quickness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>While a monolithic cube's construct armor is broken, it is Quickened. It can only use the additional action from quickened for Crushing Face. Additionally, it gains a mercury jet Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Crushing Face","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A monolithic cube's primary means of both attack and locomotion is to roll over, crushing everything in its path. The monolithic cube Strides. During this Stride, the cube can move into and through the spaces of creatures and objects that are Large or smaller. Unattended objects in the path of a monolithic cube's crushing face automatically take 10d10 bludgeoning damage. Each creature whose space the monolithic cube enters takes 2d10+6 bludgeoning damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save). Wobbling between two faces slightly destabilizes the cube. If the cube uses Crushing Face to move in the opposite direction of its most recent Stride on the same turn, the DC of the Reflex save is reduced to DC 24 basic Reflex .</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature moves to a square of its choice adjacent to the cube.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> As critical success, but the creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, moves to a square of its choice adjacent to the cube, and is knocked Prone.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is crushed by the cube, taking double damage. It is knocked prone and Restrained underneath the cube, sharing its space while restrained in this way. A creature can Escape to move to a square of its choice adjacent to the cube. If the cube leaves the creature's space, that creature is no longer restrained.</p>"},{"n":"Unstoppable Roll","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The monolithic cube is unaffected by difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain. Its Speed is always a multiple of 15 (such as 15, 30, or 45). It is unaffected by penalties that would reduce its Speed below 15. Bonuses to speed have no effect unless they would increase its Speed to a new multiple of 15.</p>"},{"n":"Grind","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The monolithic cube deals 2d10+8 bludgeoning damage to each creature currently Restrained by its crushing face (DC 28 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Cubic Movement","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A monolithic cube moves by rolling from one face to another, leaving all of the spaces it previously occupied. As such, it can Stride only in straight lines and in cardinal directions, and it must always move exactly 15 feet. Stepping is a two-action activity for a monolithic cube.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/on0oNx4vAXKQtrAR":{"lang":["Astral","Common","Cryan","Sussuran","Utopian","Omnilinguistic archivist"],"lore":[["Encyclopedic Lore",30],["Library Lore",30]],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Encyclopedic Lore","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The moonlight owl can use Encyclopedic Lore only to Recall Knowledge, but they can use it on any topic.</p>"},{"n":"Omnilinguisitic Archivist","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The moonlight owl understands all spoken and written language. Whenever the moonlight owl speaks, all creatures that can understand at least one language understands their words.</p>"},{"n":"Foreseen Attack","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["misfortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The moonlight owl is the target of an attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The attacking creature must roll twice and use the lower result.</p>"},{"n":"Foreseen Spell","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The moonlight owl would make a saving throw against a spell effect</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The moonlight owl rolls twice and uses the higher result.</p>"},{"n":"Frost Armor","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":["cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The moonlight owl's last action was a spell with the cold trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The moonlight owl uses excess cold energy from the spell to form armor out of ice, which lasts for 1 minute. While the armor is intact, the moonlight owl gains a +4 circumstance bonus to AC and loses their weakness to fire. If the owl takes fire damage, the armor melts.</p>"},{"n":"Impart Knowledge","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","concentrate"],"f":"once per hour","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The moonlight owl chooses any specific Lore skill and selects up to 10 willing creatures within 100 feet. They can't choose Encyclopedic Lore or other nonstandard Lore skills that cover a broad range of topics. Those creatures become trained in that Lore for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"That Which Should Not Be Known","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>The moonlight owl sends visions of forbidden knowledge into the minds of everyone nearby. All creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 36 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unharmed, and the forbidden knowledge is oddly useful. It gains a +2 circumstance bonus on its next check to Recall Knowledge and is temporarily immune to That Which Should Not Be Known for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 3 and Fleeing for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/2Q0TQoty0xVdFrls":{"lang":["Petran","Pyric"],"notes":{"per":"smoke vision, tremorsense in lava or magma only","speed":"swim in lava or magma only"},"abilities":[{"n":"Magma Dweller","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The mortarfish thrives in molten rock. They can breathe in lava or magma in addition to air. Additionally, while submerged in lava or magma, they gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Stealth checks.</p>"},{"n":"Smoke Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Smoke doesn't impair a mortarfish's vision; they ignore the Concealed condition from smoke.</p>"},{"n":"Magma Geyser","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The mortarfish is about to make a mortar shot Strike while they have a creature Grabbed or Restrained in their jaws</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mortarfish loads the creature onto the mortar shot. When they make the Strike, they launch the creature into an unoccupied space within 5 feet of the attack's target; this is forced movement. If the creature was restrained, it lands Prone. The launched creature takes the mortar shot's splash damage.</p>"},{"n":"Magma Wave","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The mortarfish is swimming in lava or magma</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mortarfish unleashes a wave of molten rock. All creatures in a 60-foot cone take 12d6 fire damage (DC 33 basic Reflex save). Creatures that fail the save also take 1d6 persistent fire damage. The mortarfish can't use Magma Wave again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Mortar Reload","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The mortarfish is swimming in lava or magma</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mortarfish draws molten rock into their mouth, forming it into a ball to prepare a mortar shot. If they do not currently have a creature Grabbed in their jaws, they can also attempt an Athletics check to grab a creature of size Large or smaller within 10 feet in their jaws. Mortar Reload is the only way that a mortarfish can reload their mortar shot.</p>"},{"n":"Volcanic Smokescreen","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The mortarfish spews a cloud of volcanic smoke in a 30-foot burst centered on themself. This smoke cloud remains for 1 minute. When a creature starts its turn in the smoke cloud or enters the smoke cloud, it takes 3d6 poison damage (DC 30 basic Fortitude save). All creatures in the smoke become Concealed, and all creatures outside the smoke become concealed to creatures within it. This smoke can be dispersed by a strong wind.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/7nYMSrk3GlYbCtjr":{"lang":["Common","Draconic","Luxan","Melodian"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Echolocation 30 feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A muse wyrm can use their hearing as a precise sense at the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Inspirational Lair","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>All creatures within a muse wyrm's lair gain a +2 circumstance bonus to checks to Craft and Perform. If a creature takes a hostile action against the muse wyrm, their bonus is replaced by a –2 circumstance penalty that affects them within the dragon's lair for the next 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Charming Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","emotion","incapacitation","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. When a creature enters the muse wyrm's aura, they must attempt a DC 27 Will save against a 5th-rank Charm spell. Regardless of the results of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to the dragon's Charming Presence for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Inspiring Mien","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fortune","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An ally fails a saving throw or a skill check within sight of the muse wyrm</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The muse wyrm's presence inspires the ally to greatness. The ally can reroll triggering check.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragon takes on the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid. They lose their fly Speed and Strikes and gain a Strike appropriate to their new form that uses the attack and damage modifiers of their claw strike, but might deal a different type of damage as appropriate (typically bludgeoning).</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Kaleidoscopic Scream","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation","occult","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The dragon releases a concussive blast of sound and color in a 60-foot cone. Each creature in the area takes 6d6 sonic damage (DC 30 Will save). The dragon can't use Kaleidoscopic Scream again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Stunned 1, Blinded for 1 round, and dazzled for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, is stunned 1, and is blinded for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/xzSxuGST2tbAfFs2":{"lang":["Planetary polyglot, Telepathy 10 miles"],"lore":[["Planetary Lore",30]],"notes":{"ac":"all-around vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"All-Around Vision","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster can see in all directions simultaneously and therefore can't be flanked.</p></p>"},{"n":"Planetary Lore","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Drawing upon the combined knowledge of all the beings caught in the supernova, the nebulite uses Planetary Lore in place of any skill to Recall Knowledge.</p>"},{"n":"Planetary Polyglot","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The nebulite speaks every language that was spoken by at least one person caught in the supernova.</p>"},{"n":"Accretion Disc","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>60 feet. Creatures within the aura treat any squares they enter that are moving farther away from the nebulite as greater difficult terrain. Creatures that start their turn within the aura are pummeled by superheated particles, taking 8 fire plus 8 piercing damage (DC 32 basic Fortitude save). On a failure, the creature is also moved 5 feet toward the nebulite (or 10 feet on a critical failure); this is forced movement. By making quick calculations, a creature can temporarily escape the nebulite's pull. If a creature spends 1 action and succeeds at a DC 30 Arcana check or DC 26 Astronomy Lore check, it ignores the greater difficult terrain until it is subjected to forced movement.</p>"},{"n":"Event Horizon","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. Creatures within the aura are undetected by creatures outside the aura and can't communicate with them except by magical means or telepathy. Creatures beginning their turn within the aura are Quickened. They can use the additional action to Stride or Strike, but can't use it to move farther away from the nebulite. A creature that leaves the aura during its turn loses the extra action and the quickened condition.</p>"},{"n":"No Breath","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A nebulite doesn't breathe and is immune to effects that require breathing.</p>"},{"n":"Gravitational Pull","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The nebulite's last action was a successful tendril or graviton Strike against a creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature is pulled in a direction of the nebulite's choice, either moving closer to the nebulite or maintaining its distance. This is forced movement. The creature must roll a DC 34 Fortitude save to determine the distance.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is pulled 5 feet.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 10 feet.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 20 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Fusion","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The nebulite forces a creature to move, and their path is blocked by another creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The movement ends, and both creatures begin to glow. At the end of each affected creature's next turn, the light violently flares around it. Creatures in a 10-foot emanation take 4d6 force damage (DC 31 basic Reflex save) and are Dazzled for 1 round on a failed save.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/wUPRdWzgRdi1nI6i":{"notes":{"ac":"(26 when broken), construct armor"},"abilities":[{"n":"Construct Armor (Hardness 10)","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Like normal objects, a necrosis engine has Hardness. This Hardness reduces any damage the necrosis engine takes by an amount equal to the Hardness. Once a necrosis engine is reduced to less than half its Hit Points, or immediately upon being damaged by a critical hit, its construct armor breaks, removing the Hardness and reducing its Armor Class to 26.</p>"},{"n":"Absorb Soul","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["death","divine","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A living creature within 30 feet of the necrosis engine dies</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The necrosis engine absorbs the creature's soul, converting it into fuel for their furnace. The necrosis engine is Quickened for 1 minute; it can use this extra action only to Stride or Strike. Until the necrosis engine is destroyed, it attempts to counteract all effects that would resurrect the creature (counteract modifier +22).</p>"},{"n":"Fiendish Wound","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>Injuries from a necrosis engine's necrotizing piston Strike fester with malevolent energy from Hell. Until the start of the necrosis engine's next turn, magically treating these wounds is particularly difficult. The malevolent energy attempts to counteract all magical effects that would restore Hit Points to the target (counteract modifier +21).</p>"},{"n":"Rev Engine","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The necrosis engine shifts into overdrive, releasing a 15-foot cone of sparks and flames. Creatures in the cone take 5d6 fire damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save). Creatures that fail their save are Dazzled until the end of their next turn as sparks cover their eyes.</p>"},{"n":"Soul Siphon","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["death","divine","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The necrosis engine attempts to steal a portion of the souls surrounding it. All living creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 26 Fortitude save. The necrosis engine can't use Soul Siphon again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Drained 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Doomed 1 and Drained 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is doomed 1 and Drained 4. For 1 minute, the necrosis engine's necrotizing piston Strike gains a status bonus to its fire damage equal to twice the value of the highest drained condition Soul Siphon inflicted.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/1sUMpix94v6oH2Sk":{"lang":["Aklo","Chronan","Common"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike (Bipedal Form Only)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Adaptive Resistance","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>A neoctri would take acid, bludgeoning, cold, electricity, fire, piercing, slashing, or sonic damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The neoctri gains resistance against one of the types of damage that they are about to take. They gain resistance 4 against bludgeoning, piercing, or slashing damage or resistance 8 against acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic damage. If they would take multiple types of damage at once, they chose which resistance to gain. The resistance lasts until the neoctri use adaptive resistance again.</p>"},{"n":"Throw Rock","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster picks up a rock within reach or retrieves a stowed rock and throws it, making a ranged Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Rapid Evolution","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The neoctri's last action was a successful pincer Strike against a living creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The neoctri tears and consumes the target's flesh. The target takes 1d6 persistent bleed damage. The neoctri then assumes either their large and strong bipedal form or their observant and nimble tripedal form. The form change persists for 10 minutes or until they use Rapid Evolution again, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Bipedal Form","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In their bipedal form, the neoctri becomes Large and the reach on their pincer and claw Strikes increases to 10 feet. They gain +2 status bonus to damage with their pincer and claw Strikes. They also gain the reaction Reactive Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Tripedal Form","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In their tripedal form, the neoctri gains scent (precise) 30 feet, as well as their choice of one of the following: a +20-foot status bonus to their Speed, a 20-foot fly speed, a 30-foot climb speed, or a 40-foot swim speed.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/liYjA8FnoevbQC6f":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Shadowtongue"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing","per":"fearsense (imprecise) 60 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fearsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nightmare shade is aware of all frightened creatures within the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Light Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An object shedding magical light (such as from the Light spell) is treated as though it has the <em>ghost touch</em> property when used to attack the nightmare shade.</p>"},{"n":"Nightmare Visions","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the nightmare shade damages a creature with their terrifying touch, the creature must succeed at a DC 24 Will save or become Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Consume Fear","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The nightmare shade consumes the terror of an adjacent frightened creature.</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature takes 4d8 mental damage (DC 26 basic Will save). If the creature failed the saving throw, the nightmare shade gains 5 temporary Hit Points (10 on a critical failure). Regardless of the result, the target's frightened condition is reduced by 1.</p>"},{"n":"Helpless Awakening","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","incapacitation","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nightmare shade targets an Unconscious creature that is not dying within 30 feet. The creature wakes up; if they were at 0 Hit Points, they regain 1 Hit Point. The creature must then attempt a DC 26 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Slowed 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Paralyzed. It can attempt a new Will save at the end of each of its turns to end the condition. The DC starts at 26 and cumulatively decreases by 1 on each attempt.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the DC does not cumulatively decrease.</p>"},{"n":"Night Terrors","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","darkness","emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nightmare shade produces a 30-foot emanation of black smoke. The smoke extinguishes all sources of nonmagical light and attempts to counteract any source of magical light within the area (counteract modifier +16). Creatures in the area take 5d6 mental damage (DC 26 Will save). The nightmare shade can't use Night Terrors again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, is Frightened 3, and is Confused for 1 round as their senses are overtaken with their worst fears.</p>"},{"n":"Enduring Torment","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a nightmare shade deals mental damage, they can choose to make the damage nonlethal.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/zZTxSLlG7xjk8XnV":{"lang":["Common","Jotun","Melodian","Necril","Sussuran"],"lore":[["Music Lore",31]],"notes":{"hp":"void healing","per":"cloudsight"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Cloudsight","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Nimbus dirges ignore concealment from weather conditions, including clouds and rain.</p>"},{"n":"Aura of Winds","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["air","aura","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. Nimbus dirges are constantly cloaked in harsh winds. All physical ranged attacks against them take a –2 circumstance penalty, and air within the aura is difficult terrain for flying creatures that don't have the air trait. When a creature enters or starts its turn within the aura, it must succeed on a DC 38 Reflex save or become Clumsy 1 until the end of its next turn (Clumsy 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Nostalgic Grief","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Nimbus dirges recall what it meant to make beautiful music to inspire others, and the sound of others performing from the heart overwhelms them with grief. A creature can attempt a Performance check in place of an Intimidation check to Demoralize them. If the creature rolls a success on the check, they get a critical success instead.</p>"},{"n":"Cacophonous Fury","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nimbus dirge's Strikes deals an additional 2d6 sonic damage to frightened creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Harmonic Discord","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["emotion","fear","mental","primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>The nimbus dirge unleashes hideous discord from their harp, sending a shockwave of pain and terror in all directions. All creatures within 30 feet take 15d6 sonic damage and must attempt a DC 38 Will save. The nimbus dirge can't use Harmonic Discord for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage and is Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage, is Frightened 3, and is Fleeing for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/NtdstHRK9m3YShVm":{"lang":["Aklo","Chthonian","Common","Draconic","Empyrean","Telepathy 200 feet"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Steady Spellcasting","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a reaction would disrupt an oligtharu's spell, the demon can attempt a DC 15 Flat, avoiding the disruption on a success.</p>"},{"n":"Temporal Corruption","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["divine","time"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The oligtharu casts Fabricated Truth. If at least one creature fails the save, the fabrication is consistent with that creature's knowledge of the world, and the oligtharu imagines a plausible chain of past events to justify the fabrication, the oligtharu can alter the timestream to turn the fabrication into the truth. The change persists as long as at least one creature believes it, after which point any created objects or creatures are destroyed and any transported objects or creatures are returned to their original locations. All creatures except those that failed the save against <em>fabricated truth</em> remember the original timestream and might notice discrepancies; creatures that critically succeeded automatically recognize what happened. This effect can't introduce hazards or creatures of 20th level or higher.</p>"},{"n":"Temporal Vertigo","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["disease","divine","time","virulent"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 41 Will</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Sickened 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Sickened 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Confused and sickened 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> confused, sickened 2, and Slowed 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> As stage 4, but the victim is also under the effects of the flicker spell (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 6</strong> death. The creature's body and soul are dragged into and lost in the Dimension of Time.</p>"},{"n":"Change Shape","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","polymorph"],"f":"","d":"<p>The oligtharu can take on the appearance of any Small or Medium humanoid. This doesn't change their Speed or their attack and damage modifiers with their Strikes, but it might change the damage type their Strikes deal (typically to bludgeoning).</p><hr><p><p>The monster changes its shape indefinitely. It can use this action again to return to its natural shape or adopt a new shape. Unless otherwise noted, a monster cannot use Change Shape to appear as a specific individual. Using Change Shape counts as creating a disguise for the Impersonate use of Deception. The monster's transformation automatically defeats Perception DCs to determine whether the creature is a member of the ancestry or creature type into which it transformed, and it gains a +4 status bonus to its Deception DC to prevent others from seeing through its disguise. Change Shape abilities specify what shapes the monster can adopt. The monster doesn't gain any special abilities of the new shape, only its physical form. For example, in each shape, it replaces its normal Speeds and Strikes, and might potentially change its senses or size. Any changes are listed in its stat block.</p></p>"},{"n":"Reimposition Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Righting the oligtharu's impositions on memory and time brings the demon intense mental anguish. Whenever the oligtharu's Fabricated Truth or Rewrite Memory is counteracted, the oligtharu takes 3d10+14 mental damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/faKRfJyWYKxMHKRL":{"lang":["Common","Fey"],"gear":["Blood Gem (9)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Daturic Poison","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 29 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 2d4 poison damage and Stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 3d4 poison damage and Stupefied 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 4d4 poison damage and Stupefied 3 (1 round)</p>"},{"n":"Mesmeric Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ouveliste deals an additional 3d6 precision damage on melee Strikes to Dazzled creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Returning Gems","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An ouveliste's blood gems have the <em>returning</em> property when thrown from their hands.</p>"},{"n":"Forgetter's Bliss","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","curse","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>An ouveliste targets an adjacent, willing creature and permanently suppresses all of the creature's memories of a particular person, incident, or conversation. If anyone mentions the suppressed subject to the creature, the creature takes 3d8 mental damage (DC 32 basic Will save). A creature can only take damage in this way once per day. The next time it falls asleep, it forgets everything it has learned about the suppressed subject. The counteract DC for removing the curse with Cleanse Affliction and similar effects is 32.</p>"},{"n":"False Fantasy","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","illusion","incapacitation","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ouveliste spins a pleasant hallucination unique to each viewer. All Dazzled creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 30 Will save against the hallucination and take 4d8 mental damage when the hallucination ends. Creatures that succeed at the save become temporarily immune to False Fantasy for 1 hour.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature mostly rejects the hallucination, but hazy images impair its vision. For 1 round, all creatures that are farther than 10 feet away from it are Concealed to it. When the hallucination ends, they take half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is pulled into the hallucination. They experience the visual disturbances from a success, are Stunned 1, and take full damage when the hallucination ends.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the visual disturbances last for 3 rounds, and the creature takes double damage when the hallucination ends.</p>"},{"n":"Beguiling Legerdemain","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","light","manipulate","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ouveliste juggles three glowing blood gems, mesmerizing onlookers. Creatures within 30 feet must attempt a DC 32 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Beguiling Legerdemain for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 3 rounds.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 6 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Toxic Blood","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature deals piercing or slashing damage to the ouveliste</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ouveliste's blood splashes onto the triggering creature, exposing them to daturic poison.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/4smcNzAu4KRcmSr3":{"lang":["Astral","Chronan","Telepathy 120 feet, Truespeech"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fortune Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A paradoxical past takes additional damage from attacks whose attack roll was altered by a fortune effect.</p>"},{"n":"Life Loop","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The paradoxical past's turn ends</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The actions the paradoxical past used on this turn are identical to those used on their previous turn and in the same order (Strike, Stride, Strike, for instance), though not necessarily in the same direction or against the same targets</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The paradoxical past gains 10 temporary Hit Points.</p>"},{"n":"Thoughtsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The paradoxical past senses all non-mindless creatures in the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Repeating Curse","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["curse","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by a paradoxical past's time loop must attempt a DC 25 Will save. On a failure, the creature must spend its last action on its next turn repeating an action it already performed that turn (such as Striding, Striking, or Casting a Spell), though not necessarily in the same direction or against the same targets. If the creature can't repeat itself, it loses this last action.</p>"},{"n":"Paradoxical Precision","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The paradoxical past deals an additional 2d6 precision damage on time loop Strikes benefiting from a fortune effect.</p>"},{"n":"Relive Past","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["fortune","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The paradoxical past repeats the actions it performed the previous turn with as close to the same specifics as possible—moving the same distance and direction or Striking the same targets with the same weapon, if able. Actions the paradoxical past can't repeat are lost with no effect. The paradoxical past rolls twice and takes the better result for any Strike made as part of this activity.</p>"},{"n":"Twin Timelines","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The paradoxical past makes two time loop Strikes against the same target. If the first Strike misses the target, the paradoxical past rolls twice and takes the better result on the second attack roll. This is a fortune effect.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/r9ic2WVVTwqJkSXl":{"lang":["Astral","Chronan","Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fortune Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A parallel present takes additional damage from attacks whose attack roll was altered by a fortune effect.</p>"},{"n":"Thoughtsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The parallel present senses all non-mindless creatures in the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Duplicate Swap","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The parallel present is targeted by a Strike while they have at least one duplicate</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The parallel present and the duplicate swap places. The triggering Strike resolves against the duplicate instead.</p>"},{"n":"Flickering Form","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The parallel present vanishes and reappears 10 feet away in a random direction, gaining 10 temporary Hit Points. Any duplicates of the parallel present also vanish and reappear in random directions. This effect can't cause the parallel present or their duplicates to enter hazardous terrain or an occupied space.</p>"},{"n":"Temporal Anchor","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The parallel present's condensed timeline anchors its targets to the present moment. A creature that is critically hit by the parallel present's timeline strike is Slowed 1.</p>"},{"n":"Duplicate","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fortune","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The parallel present creates two duplicates in spaces adjacent to themselves. These duplicates have the same AC and saving throw modifiers as the parallel present but disappear if they take any damage. While a duplicate exists, the parallel present can roll twice and take the better result on any Strike or saving throw (unless all duplicates had to roll a saving throw against the effect). If they do, a duplicate of their choice is destroyed after the attack roll or saving throw is resolved; they can't select a duplicate that also had to roll a saving throw. The duplicates mirror the parallel present's motions but do not move from the space where they were created except by Flickering Form. A creature that Seeks can identify a parallel present as real or a duplicate with a successful DC 35 Perception check. The parallel present can have at most six duplicates. Duplicates disappear after 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Convergence Strike","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The parallel present has at least one duplicate</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The parallel present vanishes and reappears adjacent to a creature within 20 feet. Any number of the parallel present's duplicates also vanish and reappear adjacent to the target creature. The parallel present attempts a timeline Strike against the target creature, gaining an additional die of damage for each duplicate adjacent to the target creature.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/etMVkUMHjWeC3ZFw":{"lang":["Aetheran","Common","Fey","Necril","Sakvroth","Spirituan"],"lore":[["Spirit Lore",27]],"abilities":[{"n":"Spiritsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The phasmogorgia senses the spirits of creatures, including living creatures, most non-mindless undead, and haunts within the listed range. As spiritsense detects spiritual essence, not physical bodies, it can detect spirits projected by spells such as project image or possessing otherwise soulless objects. It can't detect soulless bodies, constructs, or objects, and like most senses, it doesn't penetrate through solid objects.</p>"},{"n":"Ectoplasmic Ambrosia","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","death","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>40 feet. The phasmogorgia releases a constant haze of mystical spores that enraptures creatures, bringing them one step closer to death. When a creature with a soul starts its turn within is Doomed 1 unless it succeeds at a DC 30 Will save. A creature that succeeds at the save is temporarily immune to Ectoplasmic Ambrosia for 24 hours. Spirits that fail the Will save are also Fascinated by the phasmogorgia for 1 minute and can't willingly move away from it while they remain fascinated. If the phasmogorgia takes a hostile action against a spirit or any of its allies, the spirit can attempt a new saving throw to end the fascination at the start of its next turn. If a doomed creature dies within the aura, its soul is bound to the phasmogorgia, and it can't be resurrected until the phasmogorgia is slain.</p>"},{"n":"Phantasmorgasbord","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["healing","occult"],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The phasmogorgia digests captive spirits to rejuvenate itself, restoring 100 healing Hit Points. All creatures stunned by Soul Snatch and spirits Fascinated by Ectoplasmic Ambrosia take 5d6 force damage (DC 33 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Soul Snatch","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["incapacitation","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The phasmogorgia latches an ethereal hook to the soul of a creature within 30 feet. The target must attempt a DC 33 Will save. Creatures with no soul automatically critically succeed.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target is Stunned 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target's soul is shunted out of its body, stunning it for 1 round. While stunned in this way, the creature takes 2d8 force damage every time the phasmogorgia uses a ghost bomb Strike, as it includes the creature's soul in the projectile.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is stunned for 3 rounds. At the end of each of its turns, it can attempt a new Will save to end the effect.</p>"},{"n":"Spirit Swarm","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["force","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A swarm of spirits surges out of the phasmogorgia, dealing 5d6 force damage to each creature in a 40-foot cone (DC 33 basic Fortitude save). A creature that fails the save is also Drained 1 and Frightened 1 (Drained 2 and Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/5LfG4HCgUwer4RuB":{"lang":["Common","Sakvroth","Venenan","Speak with animals"],"gear":["Arsenic","Graveroot","Putrid Eggs (4)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Pilatatry Toxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 20 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1d4 poison damage and Sickened 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 2d4 poison damage and sickened 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 4d4 poison damage and Sickened 2 (1 round).</p>"},{"n":"Strange Taste","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 10 feet of the pilatatry Interacts to consume food or drink, including consumable items</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pilatatry quickly adds extra ingredients to the mix. The pilatatry attempts a Thievery check against the creature's Reflex DC. On a success, the target is exposed to pilatatry toxin.</p>"},{"n":"Corrupted Products","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pilatatry spends 1 hour tending to livestock, corrupting their products in secret. For 24 hours, all products produced from those livestock carry a latent form of pilatatry toxin, which the pilatatry can activate using Twisted Snack. Those who consume these modified products can detect an odd, unpleasant aftertaste with a DC 24 Perception check. Additionally, if a pilatatry corrupts the same animals' products each day for 1 week, they can attempt to Craft a common alchemical poison of their choice of 4th level or lower, using those products as the only ingredients.</p>"},{"n":"Twisted Snack","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The pilatatry causes the toxins in corrupted food to suddenly flare up. Each creature within 30 feet that has eaten food laced with Corrupted Products is exposed to pilatatry toxin. The poison gains the virulent trait when applied from this ability.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/IZ1hu6iuIsOfoVvA":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Truespeech"],"gear":["Rapier","Trinket (3)"],"notes":{"speed":"mobility"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fair Trade?","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An adjacent creature hits the pilfermin with a Strike while the pilfermin has a trinket in one of their hands</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pilfermin offers the trinket in exchange for their life. The attacker must accept the trade unless they succeed at a DC 26 Will save. If the attacker accepts the trade, the Strike misses. The attacker can accept the trinket into a free hand to gain a +2 status bonus to AC and saving throws against the pilfermin for as long as they hold the trinket, otherwise, the trinket falls to the ground in the attacker's space.</p><p>Effect: Pilferman Trinket</p>"},{"n":"Knock Loose","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The pilfermin's last action was a successful rapier Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pilfermin attempts to Disarm an object the creature they hit is holding. They gain a +4 status bonus on the Athletics check. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the pilfermin's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Mine Now","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pilfermin can Steal or Palm an Object that's closely guarded, such as in a pocket, without taking the –5 penalty, and they can Steal objects of up to light Bulk. They can't steal objects that would be extremely noticeable or time consuming to remove (like worn shoes or armor or actively wielded objects). They can attempt to Steal from a creature in combat or otherwise on guard. When doing so, Stealing requires 2 actions instead of 1, and they take a –5 penalty to the Thievery check.</p>"},{"n":"What Else Do I Got?","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> There is at least one trinket in the pilfermin's bag or unattended in an adjacent square</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The pilfermin takes a trinket into their free hand.</p>"},{"n":"Don't You Remember Me?","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["curse","incapacitation","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The pilfermin spends 10 minutes speaking to a humanoid target and then uses the details they've gleaned to implant false memories of a close relationship. The target must attempt at DC 28 Will save. Regardless of the results of the save, the target is temporarily immune to this ability for 24 hours.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and knows the pilfermin tried to enchant it.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target is unaffected and thinks the pilfermin was talking to them normally.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is friendly with the pilfermin for 24 hours, or until the pilfermin takes a hostile action against the target or its allies.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the target is helpful to the pilfermin.</p>"},{"n":"Mobility","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the pilfermin Strides to move half their Speed or less, that movement does not trigger reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A pilfermin deals an additional 2d6 precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/uQWWgf2d7AS9cp4t":{"lang":["Sussuran","Talican","Voltan"],"notes":{"speed":"swiftness"},"abilities":[{"n":"Dispersed Form","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Other creatures can occupy the same space as the plasma lasher. However, the gases in this space are not safe to breathe. A creature that ends its turn in the plasma lasher's space and does not hold its breath takes 2d6 poison plus 1d12 electricity damage and becomes Shocked.</p>"},{"n":"Metallic Core","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature occupying the same space as the plasma lasher can attempt to target their metallic core with a melee Strike or spell attack roll. The plasma lasher gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against such attacks, but they lose their physical resistance, instead gaining gains weakness 10 to bludgeoning damage.</p>"},{"n":"Sudden Discharge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the plasma lasher's reach uses a move action, or ends its turn occupying the same space as the plasma lasher</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A jolt of plasma strikes the target creature, dealing 3d12 electricity damage (DC 32 basic Reflex save). On a failed saving throw, the creature is Shocked for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Conductive Connection","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>A plasma arc forms between the plasma lasher's metallic core and a creature within 90 feet, dealing the creature 8d12 electricity damage (DC 32 basic Reflex save). On a failed saving throw, the electrical connection persists and the target creature becomes Shocked for 1 minute. The shocked condition automatically ends if the creature and the plasma lasher are ever more than 90 feet apart.</p>"},{"n":"Pulse Current","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The target creature is Shocked from the plasma lasher's Conductive Connection</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Current flow through the shocked creature, dealing 4d12 electricity damage (DC 32 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Swiftness","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The plasma lasher's movement doesn't trigger reactions.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/1TvvWS4tspelQjW8":{"lang":["Common","Cryan","Pyric","Sussuran"],"abilities":[{"n":"Anomalous Combustion","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>If a plisayasha takes fire damage after applying their resistance to fire, they lose their fire resistance and take 1d6 persistent fire damage. After the persistent damage ends, they can regain their resistance to fire by spending 10 minutes submerged in cold water.</p>"},{"n":"Flight or Swim Response","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The plisayasha takes damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The plisayasha attempts to escape. They Fly or Swim, up to half their Speed. This movement doesn't trigger reactions based on movement.</p>"},{"n":"Frigid Breath","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Inhaling an immense amount of air, the plisayasha inflates their belly enormously and then rapidly expels a powerful gust of glacial air in a 20-foot cone. Creatures within the cone take 4d8 cold damage and must attempt a DC 21 Fortitude save. The plisayasha can't use Frigid Breath again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is pushed 5 feet back from the plisayasha.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is pushed 10 feet back from the plisayasha. If Frigid Breath's cold damage ended the persistent fire damage from Thermic Compound, the creature is also Paralyzed for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Thermic Compound","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The plisayasha spits a scorching, viscous glob from their mouth, dealing 1d6 persistent fire damage in a 5-foot burst within 30 feet (DC 21 Reflex save negates). While a creature is taking this persistent fire damage, it also gains weakness 2 to cold. If the creature takes any cold damage while under the effects of Thermic Compound, the persistent fire damage from Thermic Compound immediately ends, after applying the cold weakness once. Unlike many other fire effects, Thermic Compound can be used underwater. The plisayasha can't use Thermic Compound again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/iNQzXZxN215iaoQC":{"lang":["Fey","Muan"],"notes":{"saves":"–2 status to all saves vs. air effects","speed":"forest passage, lightweight"},"abilities":[{"n":"–2 Status to All Saves Vs. Air Effects","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Pollen Eruption","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The pollen brawler is critically hit by a Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A puff of pollen erupts from the pollen brawler's body. All creatures within 10 feet of the pollen brawler is exposed to hay fever, and must attempt a Fortitude save against the poison.</p>"},{"n":"Hay Fever","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 22 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Sickened 1</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> sickened 1 and Dazzled for 1 round</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> Sickened 2 and dazzled for 1 round</p>"},{"n":"Forest Passage","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The pollen brawler ignores any difficult terrain caused by plants, such as bushes, vines, and undergrowth. Even plants manipulated by magic don't impede their progress.</p>"},{"n":"Among the Leaves","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>On the first round of combat, If the pollen brawler rolls Stealth for initiative while within vegetation, creatures that haven't acted yet are Off-Guard to the pollen brawler.</p>"},{"n":"Lightweight","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>In still air or mildly windy conditions, the pollen brawler can fly at a Speed of 10 feet. However, stronger winds can easily push the pollen brawler around. In stronger winds, the pollen brawler can move up to the wind's speed, but they can only fly in the wind's direction and they take a –2 circumstance penalty to attack rolls for as long as they remain off the ground. A pollen brawler can spend 1 action to stabilize themself and negate this penalty until the end of their turn.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/cVmnNTnajHN8Ihz5":{"lang":["Common","Truespeech, communicates through writing only"],"lore":[["Postal Lore",26]],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"I Know Where You Live","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["detection","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A postgeist carrying the written name of a location always knows the fastest traversable path to that location. If they carry the written name of a creature that the writer was familiar with, they know the direct path to the location where the creature last made their daily preparations. If the location or creature is under any effect that would block detection, the postgeist attempts a counteract check against that effect (counteract modifier +22); if the counteract check fails, the postgeist can't attempt to counteract that same effect again.</p>"},{"n":"Swirling Letters","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet, 3d8 slashing, DC 27 basic Reflex. The postgeist can suppress or activate this aura as a single action with the concentrate trait.</p>"},{"n":"Return to Sender","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["concentrate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature targets the postgeist with an auditory or linguistic effect</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The postgeist attempts a counteract check against the effect (counteract modifier +22). On a success, the magical words or sounds from the effect are transcribed in a letter. The next time the postgeist targets that creature with a letter Strike, the letter flies to that creature and opens before it, targeting it with the counteracted effect. The effect uses the attack roll bonuses, DCs, and other statistics from the original source, not the postgeist's, and neither applies nor counts toward any creature's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Telekinetic Shove","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The postgeist's last action was a successful boot Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The postgeist attempts to Shove the creature, using their spell attack modifier instead of Athletics. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the postgeist's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Paper Weight","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The postgeist's last action was a successful letter Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The postgeist hampers the movements of the creature they hit with their Strike. The creature must succeed on a DC 30 Reflex save or become Off-Guard until the end of the postgeist's next turn and Slowed 1 (Slowed 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Swift Delivery","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The postgeist Flies up to their Speed. Each creature that is within 10 feet of the postgeist at any point during this movement takes 6d10 slashing damage (DC 30 basic Reflex save). The postgeist can't use Swift Delivery again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/1t0jhDC7zOtNrGpg":{"lang":["Astral","Chronan","Common","Telepathy 120 feet, Truespeech"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Fortune Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A pruned future takes additional damage from attacks whose attack roll was altered by a fortune effect.</p>"},{"n":"Thoughtsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The pruned future senses all non-mindless creatures in the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Borrow Future","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>At the beginning of their turn, a pruned future can gain 10 temporary Hit Points. The pruned future can't use this action if they are currently under any effects with the misfortune trait.</p>"},{"n":"Split Future","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["fortune","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The pruned future branches their timeline temporarily and then decides between the two possible futures. The pruned future creates a temporal copy of themselves. Both they and their copy Stride up to their speed and roll a Strike against a different target. The pruned future then chooses which version of themselves is the true one. The true version's Strike occurs normally, while the copy disappears instead of harming their target. The copy has identical statistics to the original at the time the copying occurs, and any damage or conditions that the copy incurs do not affect the original.</p>"},{"n":"Discern Stratagem","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fortune","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The pruned future peers into a creature's future to prepare a killing blow. The pruned future attempts an Occultism vs. Will DC check against the Will DC of a target they can sense, then makes a Strike against that target, automatically succeeding on any flat check due to the Concealed or hidden conditions. If the Occultism check was a success, the pruned future rolls twice and takes the better result on the Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Fatal Fortune","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A pruned future's melee and ranged Strikes gain the fatal d12 trait when benefiting from a fortune effect.</p>"},{"n":"Curse of Unraveled Fate","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["curse","misfortune","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature struck by the pruned future's pruning shears must attempt a DC 34 Fortitude save as the frayed ends of the pruned future's fate tug on those of the creature.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1 round, Doomed 1, and must roll twice and take the worse result on the next check it makes.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1 minute, Doomed 2, and must roll twice and take the worse result on every check it makes for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Pjr7QbGS4I9yUxZX":{"lang":["Fey","Thalassic"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Hop","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature successfully deals damage to the puddle hopper</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The puddle hopper Leaps up to 15 feet. They can instead use Water Hop if they are within range of a body of water that is large enough.</p>"},{"n":"Unnerving Leap","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["concentrate","emotion","fear","mental","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The puddle hopper rolls initiative while Hiding in water</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The puddle hopper jumps out of the water, stretching their limbs wide in an attempt to frighten nearby creatures. The puddle hopper Leaps and attempts to Demoralize all creatures within 10 feet of where they land. If they critically succeed to Demoralize a creature, that creature drops whatever it was holding.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Puddle Reach","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a puddle hopper is in contact with a body of water, they can target other creatures within 30 feet that are in the same body of water with their fist Strike. They can also attempt to Palm an Object off of them.</p>"},{"n":"Water Hop","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move","primal","teleportation","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The puddle hopper Leaps into a body of water within range and teleports to another body of water within 60 feet. This body of water must be large enough for the puddle hopper to occupy without Squeezing.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/AHBLTimP4FbtX7N2":{"lang":["Khaotan","Melodian"],"abilities":[{"n":"Echolocation 120 Feet","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A quantum hummer can use their hearing as a precise sense at the listed range.</p>"},{"n":"Superposition","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The quantum hummer is not Immobilized, and there are at least three unoccupied squares adjacent to the quantum hummer</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The quantum hummer moves rapidly to distort space and appear in multiple adjacent spaces, becoming Hidden. While they distort their position in this way, they become a Large swarm, with immunity to the Grabbed, Prone, and Restrained conditions as well as weakness 5 to area damage and splash damage. The bird remains in this state until they are immobilized or Unconscious, or until their precise location is observed, typically through an effect that negates invisibility or a critically successful Perception check to Seek them. A quantum hummer can Dismiss Superposition.</p>"},{"n":"Humming Resonance","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","auditory"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The quantum hummer hears a Swarming Song from another quantum hummer within 40 feet</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The quantum hummer enters a Superposition. If the quantum hummers is already in a Superposition, they instead perform a Swarming Song.</p>"},{"n":"Swarming Song","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The quantum hummer exists in a Superposition</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Each enemy in the swarm's space takes 3d6 sonic damage (DC 24 basic Fortitude save). A creature that fails its save against Swarming Song becomes Deafened for 1 round. In addition to the typical DC 5 Flat to perform actions with the auditory trait while deafened, creatures that are deafened from Swarming Song must succeed at DC 5 Flat to perform concentrate actions.</p>"},{"n":"Quantum Body","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The quantum nature of the quantum hummer's body attack allows them to Strike from multiple places at once. If the quantum hummer is in a place where teleportation effects are suppressed, their reach decreases to 0 feet, the damage of their quantum beak is reduced to 2d6, the damage of their quantum wing is reduced to 2d4, and their Strikes lose the teleportation trait.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/bfIBIrft88Ghp2w0":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Draconic","Empyrean","Melodian","Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Hush","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature affected by the quietus's silence spell successfully Strikes the quietus</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The quietus puts a finger to their lips and hisses loudly, assaulting the mind of whoever dared disturb their peace. The creature takes 4d6 mental damage (DC 32 basic Will save).</p>"},{"n":"Performance Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A quietus can't bear to be in the presence of people sharing mirth through music, dance, or other forms of art. When a creature Performs for an ally who can hear them and their Performance check is higher than quietus's Will DC, the quietus takes 3d6 mental damage.</p>"},{"n":"Steal Voices","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The quietus attempts to steal the voices of nearby creatures. All creatures within 30 feet take 5d8 mental damage and must attempt a DC 32 Will save, after which they are temporarily immune to Steal Voices for 1 hour.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage. The creature can't speak or use effects with the concentrate trait for one round, during which time the quietus can speak using the creature's voice.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, except the creature can't speak or use effects with the concentrate trait for 3 rounds. During this time, the quietus can cast spells using the creature as the origin point.</p>"},{"n":"Louden Spell","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","divine","spellshape"],"f":"","d":"<p>The three mouths of the quietus whine in discordant harmony, making sure they are heard above all others. If the next action the quietus uses is to Cast a Spell with the auditory or sonic trait, creatures that fail their saving throw against the spell's effects also become Deafened until the start of the quietus's next turn. While deafened, they can still hear the quietus's voice.</p>"},{"n":"Hypocritical Silencing","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A quietus's auditory abilities, speech, and spellcasting are unaffected by their own Silence spell, including when speaking using another's voice by means of Steal Voices.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/oGEzTB4EAiHzXH3O":{"lang":["Luxan","Petran"],"notes":{"per":"radiant resonance (precise)","speed":"earth glide"},"abilities":[{"n":"Radiant Resonance","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The refulgent prismite's crystalline form is attuned to the light that they emit, allowing them to detect creatures that they have bathed in bright light as a precise sense. This ability typically allows them to see in the area of their radiant gleam aura, but its radius can be temporarily extended by the refulgent prismite's other abilities. They lack typical vision, as they can't detect light from other sources.</p>"},{"n":"Refract","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fire","light","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The refulgent prismite is within the light radius of another refulgent prismite's Brilliance</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The refulgent prismite enhances their ally's brightness. The radius of the fiery emanation increases by 10 feet and the radius of the bright light increases by 100 feet. If this would cause the light radius to include a new refulgent prismite, that prismite can then Refract.</p>"},{"n":"Radiant Gleam","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","light","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>60 feet. A refulgent prismite constantly sheds intense light, making it difficult to look directly at them. Creatures that end their turn within the aura must attempt a DC 27 Fortitude save. On a successful save, the creature is temporarily immune to radiant gleam for 1 minute.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Brilliance","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","incapacitation","light","manipulate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The refulgent prismite concentrates their light so severely that it sears flesh, dealing 8d6 fire damage to all creatures in a 30-foot emanation (DC 29 Fortitude save). After using Brilliance, the refulgent prismite shine emits bright light in a 100-foot radius until the end of their next turn. It can't use Brilliance again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to being Blinded or Dazzled by a refulgent prismite for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is dazzled for 1 round and takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is blinded for 1 round and takes full damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is blinded for 1 minute and takes double damage.</p>"},{"n":"Earth Glide","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A refulgent prismite can Burrow through earthen matter, including rock. When they do so, they move at their full burrow Speed, leaving no tunnels or signs of their passing.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/YgDGRRkFDpEwDqbh":{"lang":["Common","Requian"],"abilities":[{"n":"Out, Out Brief Candle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","earth"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature damages the rictus mask while the rictus mask is within 10 feet of a statue they created with their Echoes of the Damned ability</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The rictus mask causes one of their statues from Echoes of the Damned within 10 feet to explode, reducing the amount of damage the rictus mask takes by 10. The remnants of the statue gather on the rictus mask, reshaping their facial features to match the creature who triggered this reaction. The creature depicted on the mask doesn't reduce the value of their frightened condition automatically at the end of their turns until the mask takes on another person's appearance or 1 minute passes, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Echoes of the Damned","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine","earth"],"f":"","d":"<p>The rictus mask creates two Medium statues within 10 feet. Each of these statues is a dusty facsimile of a creature that has previously taken damage from the rictus mask. The statues are inanimate objects with object immunities, 10 Hit Points, and 20 AC; for all other defensive statistics, they use the rictus mask's bonuses. If the rictus mask uses Echoes of the Damned again, any statues they previously created turn to dust.</p>"},{"n":"Tomorrow, And Tomorrow, And Tomorrow","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The rictus mask accelerates time in a 10-foot burst within 120 feet until the end of their next turn. Within this area, flesh falters, plants shrivel, and even stone begins to crumble. Any creature that enters or begins its turn in the area of accelerated time takes 8d6 force damage (DC 25 basic Fortitude save) and is then temporarily immune to this ability for 1 day. The rictus mask can Sustain the effect up to twice on future turns to extend its duration; each time they do, the radius increases by 10 feet.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/UZ5kdaiW1kp78USz":{"lang":["Common","Spirituan","Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Umbra Shield","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","darkness","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the rommor's void aura is targeted by an attack</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The rommor unleashes shadowy wisps to protect the targeted creature, granting a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the attack misses, the targeted creature can immediately teleport to any unoccupied space within the void aura.</p><p>Effect: Umbra Shield</p>"},{"n":"Umbral Shroud","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["arcane","aura","darkness"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet. Shadows emanates from the rommor, as a 7th-rank Darkness spell. Creatures of the rommor's choice gain greater darkvision and a +1 status bonus to AC while they are within the aura.</p>"},{"n":"Spirit Nova","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","spirit"],"f":"","d":"<p>The rommor unleashes a wave of spiritual energy, dealing 14d6 spirit damage to creatures in a 20-foot emanation (DC 33 basic Fortitude save). The rommor can exclude any number of creatures in the area from the blast. Creatures that fail the save are knocked 5 feet away from the rommor (or 10 feet on a critical failure). The rommor can't use Spirit Nova again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Cloak of Stars","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","extradimensional","incapacitation","manipulate","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The rommor's cloak is not already holding 8 creatures</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The rommor shrouds an adjacent creature in their cloak, transporting the creature into an extradimensional sea of stars. An unwilling creature can attempt a DC 33 Will save, after which it becomes temporarily immune to Cloak of Stars for 10 minutes. A willing creature receives the results of a failure, except the rommor can allow the creature to remain in the extradimensional space until the creature wants to leave.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature blinks into the extradimensional space momentarily before reappearing in an unoccupied space of the rommor's choice within the void aura.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is sent into the extradimensional space until the end of its next turn.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature remains in the extradimensional space for up to 1 minute. The creature can attempt a new Will save to exit the cloak at the end of each of its turns. Each held creature appears as a constellation on the cloak. A rommor can eject a held creature as a free action. If the rommor is slain, all held creatures reappear in the nearest unoccupied space.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/HXxyZNQEUZEZKaho":{"lang":["Necril","Speak with wasps"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Speak with Wasps","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>A rothive can communicate with wasps and use Diplomacy to Make an Impression on wasps and Request things from wasps.</p>"},{"n":"Consume Swarm","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["healing","olfactory","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> a rothive is reduced to 0 Hit Points and a wasp swarm is within 40 feet</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> the rothive releases a pheromone that calls the wasp swarm to reinforce their crumbling body. The wasp swarm uses its reaction to fly into the rothive, destroying itself and transferring all its remaining Hit Points to the rothive. Wasp swarms whose Intelligence modifier is greater than –5 can attempt a DC 18 Will save to resist the effect; when used against such swarms, the effect gains the incapacitation trait.</p>"},{"n":"Disorienting Drone","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["auditory","aura","emotion","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>10 feet. The hum of wings from within the rothive bends the minds of those who come too close. All creatures within the aura must attempt a DC 18 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is temporarily immune to Disorienting Drone for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Stupefied 1 until the end of its next turn.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Stupefied 2 until the end of its next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Smokesleep","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["air","olfactory"],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a rothive begins their turn or enters a space where there is enough smoke to grant the Concealed condition, the rothive must attempt a DC 25 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The rothive is Stunned 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The rothive is Stunned 2.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The rothive is Stunned 3 and becomes indifferent to all other creatures for 1 minute. During this time, the rothive's attitude can worsen toward a creature only if that creature takes a hostile action against them.</p>"},{"n":"Corpse Honey","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 18 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Sickened 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Sickened 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> sickened 2 and the creature can't reduce its sickened value below 1 (1 round).</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/rpHYBm2ldBqm8P4M":{"lang":["Arboreal","Fey","Can't speak any language"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. primal spells","per":"detect magic (primal only)"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Rotten Influence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","death","primal","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. A creature who enters or begins its turn in the aura takes 1d8 void damage (DC 21 basic Fortitude save). Plant creatures take a –2 circumstance penalty to this saving throw. All non-creature plants in the area that are Small or smaller and are not magical wither, eliminating any difficult terrain, cover, or concealment they provided.</p>"},{"n":"Fungal Burst","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 15 feet hits the rotwood with an unarmed or melee weapon Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Fungi embedded in the rotwood's bark discharge a burst of spores toward the creature. Each creature in a 15-foot cone must attempt a DC 22 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Dazzled for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Blinded for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Withering Touch","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["primal","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The rotwood's last action was a successful rotting bough Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The rotwood channels corruption into the target of their Strike, dealing 3d8 void damage (DC 22 basic Fortitude save).</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is Enfeebled 1 for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage and is Enfeebled 2 for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Spew Insects","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The rotwood vomits forth a great swarm of termites and mosquitoes that bite and stinging all in their wake, dealing 7d6 piercing damage in a 30-foot cone (DC 25 basic Reflex save). Any creature that fails its save is also Sickened 1. The rotwood can't use Spew Insects again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Throw Rock","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>The monster picks up a rock within reach or retrieves a stowed rock and throws it, making a ranged Strike.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/7x4kMhvRpnl65hKL":{"lang":["Necril","Plus any one language they knew when they were alive"],"gear":["Sarcophagus Lid"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing","ac":"void healing"}},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/SkFYQTSgoKL6b0BM":{"lang":["Aetheran","Astral","Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Utopian"],"lore":[["Axis Lore",13]],"abilities":[{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The scupa deals 2d4 extra precision damage to Off-Guard creatures. If the creature became off-guard due to Analyze Armor, they instead deal 2d8 extra precision damage.</p>"},{"n":"Analyze Armor","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The scupa carefully surveys the defenses of a creature they can see within 60 feet, searching for weak points. If the creature is benefiting from an item bonus to AC, such as from armor, bands of force, or mystic armor, the scupa can attempt a Crafting check to find a weakness in that defense. The DC of the Crafting check is equal to the standard DC for an item of that level or spell of that rank. If the creature is not benefiting from an item bonus, the Crafting check automatically fails.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Off-Guard against the scupa's attacks for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> No effect.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The scupa can't attempt to Analyze Armor on the same target again for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Display Tailfeathers","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","mental","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The scupa fans out their tailfeathers, creating fascinating patterns. Each non-scupa creature within 30 feet must attempt a DC 19 Will save. The effects of Display Tailfeathers last for 1 round, but if the scupa uses this ability again on subsequent rounds, they extend the duration by 1 round for any creature already affected.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is immune to Display Tailfeathers for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Fascinated by the scupa.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, plus the creature is Dazzled.</p>"},{"n":"Invisible Hands","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a scupa casts Telekinetic Hand, they generate a pair of hands. This pair of hands has all of the typical properties of a single <em>telekinetic hand</em>, except that when the hands are in the scupa's square or an adjacent square, the scupa can use the hands to perform manipulate actions.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/g8YuMWTr9gu42UCs":{"lang":["Necril","Plus any one language they knew when they were alive"],"gear":["Sarcophagus Lid"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing","ac":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Alchemical Weakness","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sealed mummy's weakness to alchemical items not only applies to damage from alchemical items, but the sealed mummy also takes 10 untyped damage when splashed with non-damaging alchemical items or dosed with alchemical poisons, even if they're immune to their other effects.</p>"},{"n":"Raise Lid","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lid of the sealed mummy's sarcophagus is attached, and the lid isn't broken</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The sealed mummy raises their sarcophagus's lid defensively, using it as a shield. This grants them a +2 circumstance bonus to AC and allows them to use the Shield Block reaction with their lid instead of with a shield. While the lid is raised, the mummy loses their alchemical weakness.</p>"},{"n":"Shield Block","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Telekinetic Lift","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sealed mummy attempts an Athletics check to Grapple a creature they can see within 30 feet. The sealed mummy does not require a free hand to attempt this check, but they can only have one creature grappled by Telekinetic Lift at a time. On a success, in addition to the normal effects of Grapple, the creature is lifted in the air up to 20 feet off the ground (this is forced movement), and when the condition ends, it falls. The effect automatically ends if the sealed mummy moves.</p>"},{"n":"Unseal","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult"],"f":"once per minute","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per minute</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The lid of the sealed mummy's sarcophagus is attached, and the lid isn't broken</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The sealed mummy detaches their sarcophagus lid and animates the lid as a minion for up to 1 minute. The lid then takes its two actions for the turn. As a minion, the lid is a separate Medium creature with its own space and attacks, initially detaching from the sealed mummy in an adjacent square. The lid has a fly speed of 40 feet, AC 28, and its listed Hardness and Hit Points; this is typically Hardness 8, HP 64, and BT 32, but the lid might be missing Hit Points from the sealed mummy's previous Shield Blocks. The lid uses the mummy's saving throw values and has object immunities. It can make a lid bash Strike at +20 for 2d10 bludgeoning damage. If the lid ends a move action adjacent to the sealed mummy, the mummy can choose to Dismiss the effect as a free action, reattaching the lid. If the mummy does not attach the lid within 1 minute, it falls to the ground, and the sealed mummy can use an Interact action while adjacent to reattach it manually. While the lid is detached and acting as an independent minion, the sealed mummy can't use Raise Lid.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ey7HjiwkdozbK6Ih":{"lang":["Necril","Venenan"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Liquid Body","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A sepsis serpent can effortlessly reshape their body to easily flow through narrow crevices. They can move at their full Speed through any opening large enough to fit their head.</p>"},{"n":"Motion Sense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A sepsis serpent can sense nearby motion through vibration and air movement.</p>"},{"n":"Sepsis Serpent Venom","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 23 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 2d6 poison damage and Enfeebled 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 4d6 poison damage and enfeebled 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 4d6 poison damage, enfeebled 1 (1 round) and Drained 1</p>"},{"n":"Venomous Reproduction","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If a creature dies while under the effect of Septic Invasion, the creature's blood coagulates and forms a new sepsis serpent 1 minute after its death. This newborn serpent's size is Tiny and they can't use Septic Invasion. Additionally, the new serpent is Sickened 2 and can't reduce or remove the condition in any way for 1 week.</p>"},{"n":"Activate Invader","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sepsis serpent activates a clone from Septic Invasion that is residing inside a creature within 30 feet. The creature is exposed to sepsis serpent venom, after which it is temporarily immune to Activate Invader for 1 minute. On a successful save (but not a critical success), the creature takes 2d6 poison damage or the poison damage for their current stage of septic serpent venom, whichever is greater.</p>"},{"n":"Septic Invasion","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The sepsis serpent damages a creature with their fangs Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The sepsis serpent releases a minuscule copy of themselves into the bloodstream of a living creature. The copy remains dormant inside the creature until sepsis serpent activates it. The copy becomes inert and dies if it is not activated for 24 hours. The host or an adjacent creature can spend 1 manipulate action and use a healer's toolkit to attempt a DC 24 Medicine check to remove the copy with the following results.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The septic invasion is removed without harm to the host.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The septic invasion is removed, and the host takes 1d6 slashing damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The removal fails and the host takes 1d6 slashing damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The removal fails miserably. The host takes 1d6 slashing damage and the copy activates, as if the sepsis serpent had used Activate Invader.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/vtgjgsv0aWUBGysN":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Draconic","Empyrean","Necril","Truespeech"],"notes":{"hp":"dualistic nature"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Aura of Noon and Midnight","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","darkness","divine","light","shadow"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. The shadowblooded emits an aura that controls the light level around them. They can choose between bright light, dim light, or darkness. When they choose bright light, all creatures in the aura's light are Dazzled. When they choose darkness, even creatures with darkvision (but not greater darkvision) treat targets seen through the aura's darkness as Concealed. The shadowblooded can change the nature of their aura by spending an action with the concentrate trait.</p>"},{"n":"Dualistic Nature","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The body of a shadowblooded interacts in unusual ways with both vitality and void energy, shifting instantaneously depending upon the lighting conditions. In bright light, the shadowblooded is immune to vitality damage and can be healed by effects with the vitality trait. In darkness, the shadowblooded is immune to void damage and is healed by effects with the void trait. In dim light, the shadowblooded is immune to both vitality and void damage but can't be healed by effects with either the vitality or void trait.</p>"},{"n":"Spectral Strike","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>All of the shadowblooded's strikes have the benefits of the <em>ghost touch</em> property rune.</p>"},{"n":"Shadowlight","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The damage type that the shadowblooded's Strikes deal depends upon the lighting conditions: fire damage in bright light, cold damage in darkness, and half fire damage half cold damage in dim light.</p>"},{"n":"Dualistic Vampirism","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","manipulate","vitality","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadowblooded reaches draws in vitality energy, void energy, or both, affecting different creatures depending on the lighting conditions. All affected creatures within 60 feet take 16d6 untyped damage (DC 42 basic Fortitude). In bright light, creatures with void healing are affected, and the effect deals vitality damage. In darkness, living creatures are affected, and the effect deals void damage. In dim light, both living creatures and creatures with void healing are affected, with each taking whichever of vitality or void damage is worse for them. The shadowblooded then gains a number of temporary Hit Points equal to the amount of damage taken by the creature that took the most damage from this effect (or half this number of temporary Hit Points in dim light). The shadowblooded can't use Dualistic Vampirism for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Shadow Jump","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","manipulate","shadow","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The shadowblooded is in an area of dim light</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The shadowblooded steps into a shadow, reappearing out of another shadow that they can see within 300 feet. If they end this movement adjacent to a creature, they can make a melee Strike against that creature. The target is Off-Guard against this attack.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/zMjTv37TMUZQ6dt3":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Shadowtongue"],"gear":["Bastard Sword"],"notes":{"hp":"rejuvenation, void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shadow Bargain","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["curse","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadowthief makes a bargain with a willing creature, who agrees to give away their shadow in exchange for payment or a service. A creature who has lost their shadow has an unsettling presence. It takes a –2 penalty to Diplomacy checks, and the initial attitude of animals it encounters is one step worse than normal (for instance, unfriendly instead of indifferent). Sapient creatures who notice the missing shadow might mistake the creature for a vampire.</p>"},{"n":"Lashing Kick","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature adjacent to the shadowthief attempts to use a move action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The shadowthief uses Stomp on Shadow against the triggering creature. This attack neither applies nor counts toward the shadowthief's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Rejuvenation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When the shadowthief is reduced to 0 Hit Points, they appear as the missing shadow of the nearest a creature that is currently cursed by Shadow Bargain, where they lie dormant. If the curse is not removed in the next 2d4 days, the shadowthief reforms out of the shadow, fully healed, and the Shadow Bargain automatically ends.</p>"},{"n":"Extend Shadow","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadowthief extends their shadow outward and links it with the shadow of another creature within 60 feet. While the link remains, the shadowthief can momentarily project their body through the linked shadows, allowing them to make melee Strikes on the linked creature. This effect ends when either the shadowthief or the creature moves, or when the shadowthief uses Extend Shadow again to link to a different creature's shadow.</p>"},{"n":"Stomp on Shadow","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The shadowthief makes a foot Strike. If the Strike hits, the shadowthief stomps on the target's shadow. The target is Immobilized and Off-Guard until the start of the shadowthief's next turn or until they are no longer adjacent to the shadowthief, whichever comes first.</p>"},{"n":"Void's Grasp","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["occult","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a shadowthief wields a melee weapon, it temporarily becomes a <em>+1 striking weapon</em> that deals an additional 1d8 void damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/E0iKYyBMI2b9Bkmv":{"lang":["Fey","Muan","Thalassic"],"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Personal Swamp","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","earth","primal","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. The shrubmerged's roots spread out and saturate the ground with water, creating thick mud that is difficult terrain. The area is also difficult terrain for swimming creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Muddy Water","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the shrubmerged damages a creature with a water jet Strike, mud particles collected in the water encumber them. The target must attempt a DC 24 Reflex save. On a failure, the target takes a –10-foot status penalty to its Speeds for 1 minute or until it Escapes; on a critical failure, the target is Immobilized for 1 round or until it Escapes and then takes –10-foot status penalty to its Speeds for 1 minute or until it Escapes.</p><p>Effect: Muddy Water</p>"},{"n":"Murky Camouflage","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Mud collected on the shrubmerged's roots makes the water around them murky. When fully submerged in water, the shrubmerged can Hide from other creatures even if they don't have cover against them and aren't Concealed from them.</p>"},{"n":"Water Stride","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The shrubmerged can stand and move on the surface of water without falling through. This ability allows them to ignore the difficult terrain from their Personal Swamp. They can go underwater if they wish, but they must Swim to do so.</p>"},{"n":"Wall of Shrubbery","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","manipulate","plant","primal","wood"],"f":"","d":"<p>The shrubmerged rouses nearby foliage and extends their roots into the soil, creating a thick wall of plant matter with the effects of a 4th-rank Wall of Thorns spell, but the shrubmerged can move through the wall unimpeded without taking any damage and each of the wall's segments has weakness 9 to fire damage. The shrubmerged can't use Wall of Shrubbery again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Entrapping Roots","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The shrubmerged's turn begins</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Roots attempt to drag one creature within the shrubmerged's personal swamp closer. The creature must attempt a DC 24 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and becomes temporarily immune to Entrapping Roots for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is pulled 5 feet closer to the shrubmerged. This is forced movement.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature is pulled 10 feet closer.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/v4UF2K2hmyvi7nD3":{"lang":["Aklo","Can't speak any language"],"abilities":[{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Web Tether","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by the sirenspider's web Strike is Restrained and tethered to the sirenspider, preventing it from moving farther away from the sirenspider. The sirenspider can have one creature tethered at a time. The DC to Escape or Force open the web is 36. The tether can be severed with a Strike (AC 20, Hardness 5, HP 30), but this doesn't free the restrained creature.</p>"},{"n":"Resonant Carapace","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The sirenspider is within the area of an auditory effect</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The sirenspider's carapace resonates with the sound, amplifying it. The area of the triggering effect extends to include a 15-foot emanation around the sirenspider. In addition, if the effect requires a saving throw and the sirenspider rolls a success, they get a critical success instead.</p>"},{"n":"Drain Essence","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A Grabbed, Paralyzed, Restrained, or Unconscious creature is within the sirenspider's reach</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The sirenspider sinks their fangs into the creature to draw out its vital essence. The sirenspider attempts an Athletics vs. Fortitude DC check against the creature's Fortitude DC. On a success, the creature becomes Drained 1 and Stupefied 1, and the sirenspider gains 20 temporary Hit Points. Draining Essence from a creature that's already drained and stupefied increases the value of one of the conditions of the sirenspider's choice (to a maximum of 4). A victim's stupefied condition decreases by 1 per hour.</p>"},{"n":"Ensnaring Melody","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","incapacitation","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sirenspider emits an entrancing melody. Each non-sirenspider creature within a 60-foot emanation must attempt a DC 33 Will save. The effect lasts until the end of the sirenspider's next turn, but the sirenspider can Sustain it. A creature that succeeds at its save is temporarily immune for 24 hours.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Fascinated with the sirenspider for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is fascinated with the sirenspider and must spend each of its actions on its turn to move closer to the sirenspider as expediently as possible while avoiding obvious dangers. If a fascinated creature is adjacent to the sirenspider, it stays still and doesn't act. If the creature is attacked, the fascination ends.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the fascination doesn't automatically end if the creature is attacked. Instead, the creature can attempt a DC 33 Will save each time it is attacked to end the fascination.</p>"},{"n":"Paralyzing Tones","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","incapacitation","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The sirenspider's metallic carapace chimes with a melody pitched to immobilize its prey. Each non-sirenspider creature within 15 feet of the sirenspider must attempt a DC 33 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Stunned 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Paralyzed for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is paralyzed for 3 rounds. At the end of each of its turns, the creature can attempt a new Will save to reduce the remaining duration by 1 round, or end it entirely on a critical success.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/jPkF2iFr6yMXA9sf":{"lang":["Common","Pyric","Spirituan","Sussuran","Talican"],"gear":["Repair Toolkit (Superb)"],"notes":{"speed":"Seize Flight"},"abilities":[{"n":"Seize Flight","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["air","arcane","concentrate","emotion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The skyheart falls</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The skyheart is at least 10 feet above ground</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The skyheart attempts a DC 30 Will save.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The skyheart ceases falling, then gains a fly speed of 60 feet and Flies in place. This fly speed lasts for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> Treat the skyheart's fall as up to 240 feet shorter.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The skyheart falls normally.</p>"},{"n":"Turbine Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An adjacent creature can attempt to disrupt one of the skyheart's two magical turbines with Disable device. On a success, the skyheart is Stunned 1. On a critical failure, the skyheart immediately attempts a turbine Strike; this Strike neither applies nor counts toward the skyheart's multiple attack penalty. If both turbines are disabled, the skyheart can't use turbine Strikes until they spend 10 minutes Repairing themself.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Large, 3d6 slashing plus 3d6 fire, Rupture 25</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Gasp","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["air","arcane"],"f":"","d":"<p>The skyheart inhales sharply. Each creature in a 60-foot cone must succeed on a DC 34 Fortitude save or be moved 20 feet closer to the skyheart (40 feet on a critical failure); this is forced movement. Creatures that are already adjacent to the skyheart must instead succeed at DC 34 Reflex save or be knocked Prone.</p>"},{"n":"Reckless Launch","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire","move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The skyheart deals 10d6 fire damage in a 15-foot emanation (DC 31 basic Reflex save), then moves in a straight line up to 30 feet vertically and 120 feet horizontally. The skyheart can't use Reckless Launch again for 2 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Raised Spirits","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["air","arcane","emotion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>While the skyheart has a fly speed and is at least 10 feet above ground, they gain a +2 status bonus to saving throws and attack rolls. Additionally, each creature within 60 feet gains the same fly Speed for as long as it remains within range.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/VNp4r9ibhS8rs6e7":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Spirituan","Telepathy 120 feet"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Prison Demiplane","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The soul collector is trapped on a finite demiplane. Typically, both time and gravity function normally within the demiplane, but its other features have been gradually molded into a foreboding environment that suits the soul collector's tastes. When a creature dies within the demiplane or has its soul pulled in by soulcall aura, its soul is trapped. The soul collector can release souls from the demiplane with imbue soul, but souls can otherwise only be freed by wish or the direct intervention of a deity. If a soul collector is destroyed, the demiplane collapses, freeing all trapped within.</p>"},{"n":"Soul Decanter","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["occult","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>The bridge between a soul collector's prison demiplane and the Universe is a magical soul decanter. The soul collector's senses extend out in a 120-foot radius around the decanter. They can cast spells, telepathically communicate, and use abilities with the occult trait with the decanter as the origin point. They can also use Fly to telekinetically move the decanter up to their fly Speed. A soul collector is immune to most effects from creatures outside of the demiplane. However, if the decanter is destroyed (Hardness 15, HP 150, BT 75), all living creatures within the demiplane are ejected and the demiplane is temporarily disconnected from the Universe. After 24 hours, a new soul decanter forms.</p>"},{"n":"Soulcall Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","incapacitation","occult","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>60 feet (centered on the soul decanter). All creatures with a soul in the aura are drawn into the prison demiplane, arriving as close to the soul collector as they were to the soul decanter. Unwilling creatures can attempt a DC 42 Will save to resist. Souls of creatures that die in the aura are drawn in automatically. Living creatures that remain in the demiplane for 1 hour are expelled back to their original space and are temporarily immune to the aura for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Far-Reaching Control","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a soul collector casts Dominate or Suggestion, the range increases to 120 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Imbue Soul","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["occult","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a soul collector uses create undead to make a non-mindless undead, they can use a soul from their prison. If they do, they can see through the undead's eyes and communicate with them telepathically at any distance. Additionally, they can graft excess soul energy onto the undead to make it seem alive. These undead receive an automatic result of 40 on Deception checks to pass as living creatures.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ueZuFVYw8SWFebjB":{"lang":["Common","Melodian","Necril"],"lore":[["Music Lore",18]],"gear":["+1 Striking Ghost Touch Baton"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Lead the Band","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>Through rehearsals, the spectral conductor helps improve future concerts. Creatures that spend at least 2 hours rehearsing with the spectral conductor gain a +2 circumstance bonus to Performance checks involving the music practiced during the rehearsal as well as to Performance checks rolled because of the spectral conductor's Take it from the Top for 1 week.</p><p>Effect: Lead the Band</p>"},{"n":"Take it from the Top","a":"f","c":"interaction","t":["auditory","occult","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> Initiative would be rolled</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> All creatures in a 120-foot emanation use a Performance check for their initiative roll. Unwilling creatures can resist this effect with a successful DC 26 Will save.</p>"},{"n":"Accelerando","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","manipulate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The spectral conductor quickens the tempo of their concert. The spectral conductor and all of their allies within a 60-foot emanation gain 10 temporary Hit Points and are Quickened for 1 round; they can use this extra action for only Stride or Strike actions. The spectral conductor can't use Accelerando again until after they have used Ritenuto.</p>"},{"n":"Ritenuto","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","manipulate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The spectral conductor reduces the tempo of their concert. The spectral conductor is Slowed 1 until the end of their next turn. All foes within a 60-foot emanation must attempt a DC 26 Will save. The spectral conductor can't use Ritenuto again until after they have used Accelerando.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 2d6 sonic damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 4d6 sonic damage and is slowed 1 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes 8d6 sonic damage and is slowed 1 for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/7CVaWes8wThgMad8":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Spirituan","Can't speak any language"],"notes":{"hp":"void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Ethereal Illumination","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The spiritflame lantern emits a soft, ghostly radiance, casting dim light in a 10-foot emanation. This illumination is magical and can't be extinguished by non-magical means.</p>"},{"n":"Spiritfire Burst","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The spiritflame lantern unleashes a bright burst of ethereal flames in a 10-foot emanation. All creatures within the area take 1d8 fire plus 1d8 void damage (DC 21 basic Reflex save). Creatures who fail the saving throw are Dazzled for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Spiritflame Beam","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The spiritflame lantern focuses their spectral energy into a concentrated beam. The imprisoned spirits relish a brief taste of freedom as they surge forth, clinging to whomever they reach. Each creature in a 60-foot line must roll a DC 21 Reflex save. The spiritflame lantern can't use Spiritflame Beam again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 1d12 fire damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 1d12 fire plus 3 persistent fire plus 1d12 void damage. It is Frightened 1 and can't reduce or remove this condition until it removes the persistent fire damage.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes 2d12 fire plus 3 persistent fire plus 2d12 void plus 3 persistent void. It is frightened 1 and can't reduce or remove this condition until it removes the persistent fire and void damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/WvNvFibg8kaCDErD":{"lang":["Common","Shadowtongue"],"notes":{"speed":" (burrow in wooden floors only)"},"abilities":[{"n":"All-Around Vision","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>This monster can see in all directions simultaneously and therefore can't be flanked.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shadow Invisibility","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The splintertooth is Invisible in areas of dim light or darkness. When they make a jaws Strike or use Splinter Spray, they become visible until the start of their next turn.</p>"},{"n":"Shadow Step","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["occult","shadow","teleportation"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The splintertooth that was in an area of dim light or darkness is exposed to bright light</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The splintertooth retreats toward dimmer areas, teleporting to an unoccupied square within 30 feet that is not in bright light.</p>"},{"n":"Swallow Whole","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["attack"],"f":"","d":"<p>Large, 2d8+4 bludgeoning, Rupture 20</p><hr><p><p>The monster attempts to swallow a creature of the listed size or smaller that it has grabbed or restrained in its jaws or mouth. If a swallowed creature is of the maximum size listed, the monster can't use Swallow Whole again. If the creature is smaller than the maximum, the monster can usually swallow more creatures; the GM determines the maximum. The monster attempts an Athletics vs. Reflex DC check opposed by the grabbed creature's Reflex DC. If it succeeds, it swallows the creature. The monster's mouth or jaws no longer grab a creature it has swallowed, so the monster is free to use them to Strike or Grab once again. The monster can't attack creatures it has swallowed.</p>\n<p>A swallowed creature is Grabbed, is Slowed 1, and has to hold its breath or start suffocating. The swallowed creature takes the listed amount of damage when first swallowed and at the end of each of its turns while it's swallowed. If the victim Escapes this ability's grabbed condition, it exits through the monster's mouth. This frees any other creature grabbed in the monster's mouth or jaws. A swallowed creature can attack the monster that has swallowed it, but only with unarmed attacks or with weapons of light Bulk or less. The swallowing creature is Off-Guard against the attack. If the monster takes piercing or slashing damage equaling or exceeding the listed Rupture value from a single attack or spell, the swallowed creature cuts itself free. A creature that gets free by either Escaping or cutting itself free can immediately breathe and exits the swallowing monster's space.</p>\n<p>Effect: Engulf and Swallow Whole</p>\n<p>If the monster dies, a swallowed creature can be freed by creatures adjacent to the corpse if they spend a combined total of 3 actions cutting the monster open with a weapon or unarmed attack that deals piercing or slashing damage.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Grab","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Improved Grab as an action and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Improved Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Splinter Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["occult","wood"],"f":"","d":"<p>The splintertooth spits splinters of wood in a 30-foot cone that deals 8d4+8 piercing damage (DC 26 basic Reflex save). It can't use Splinter Spray again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Sudden Swallow","a":"r","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature enters the splintertooth's space</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The splintertooth is unnoticed by the triggering creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The splintertooth attempts a jaws Strike against the triggering creature. If the splintertooth successfully Grabs the triggering creature, it uses its Swallow Whole against it. The splintertooth is then Immobilized and can't use Shadow Step; these limitations persist until the creature Escapes or until the end of the splintertooth's next turn, whichever comes first.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/9ojfqM3d8OzCevsw":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Pyric","Sussuran","Venenan"],"notes":{"ac":"hateful reformation, void healing","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","per":"smoke vision"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Smoke Vision","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Smoke doesn't impair a staccarix's vision; they ignore the Concealed condition from smoke.</p>"},{"n":"Extinguish Knowledge","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the staccarix's reach uses a concentrate action</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The staccarix makes a beak Strike against the creature. On a hit, they disrupt the action. This Strike neither applies nor counts toward the staccarix's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Ash Storm Mantle","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. All creatures in the aura are Concealed by swirling smoke and ash, and all creatures outside the smoke become concealed to creatures within it. Any creature that needs to breathe must hold its breath while in the aura or begin to suffocate. A creature that breathes in the ash takes 2d6 fire plus 2d6 poison damage.</p>"},{"n":"Hateful Reformation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a staccarix dies, their ashes are borne away by a sudden fell wind. Unless quickly gathered and kept within the confines of a holy temple, these ashes reconstitute the staccarix's body over the course of 1d6 days.</p>"},{"n":"Weakness to Scattering","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When the staccarix is hit by or fails a saving throw against an effect with the air trait, or when they start their turn in an area of wind that is strong enough to provide greater difficult terrain, they take 15 bludgeoning damage.</p>"},{"n":"Ashen Flight","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The staccarix discorporates into a cloud of superheated toxic ash and Flies twice. Their amorphous form allows them to pass through the squares of other creatures or into small cracks, and their Flight does not trigger reactions based on movement. Creatures within 20 feet of each square the staccarix moves through takes 4d6 fire plus 4d6 poison damage (DC 28 basic Fortitude save); creatures that fail the save are also exposed to choking embers.</p>"},{"n":"Choking Embers","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>With their Strikes and Ashen Flight, the staccarix's body releases painful embers that spew a sickening smoke. Affected creatures must succeed at a DC 36 Fortitude save or take 1d6 persistent fire plus 1d6 persistent poison damage and become Sickened 1. On a critical failure, they become Sickened 2 and can't reduce or remove the sickened condition until they end the persistent poison damage.</p>"},{"n":"Darkened Skies","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The staccarix doesn't need a secondary caster for their Control Weather ritual. In addition to the normal options, they can invoke an ashfall or volcanic tornado made of hot, poisonous gases.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/4cr0JWI1VjU8kfiK":{"lang":["Aetheran","Aklo","Empyrean","Khaotan","Protean","Truespeech"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","speed":"unfettered movement"},"abilities":[{"n":"-20 Penalty to Sense Motive","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Voidwalker","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The starborn doesn't need to breathe, and it's also immune to the effects of pressure extremes from the environment, such as the effects of being deep undersea or in outer space.</p>"},{"n":"Gravity Well","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 100 feet casts a spell or makes a Strike that targets the starborn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature must attempt a DC 42 Will save. On a failure, the starborn determine the targets, destination, and other effects of the spell or Strike, as though they were the caster or attacker.</p>"},{"n":"Collapsing Star","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["death","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a starborn dies, their body collapses into an event horizon. All creatures within 100 feet must succeed at a DC 42 Fortitude save or be pulled 10 feet toward the sphere (20 feet on a critical failure). A creature that makes contact with the event horizon takes 20d6 void damage; if this reduces them to 0 Hit Points, they are annihilated.</p>"},{"n":"Wandering Star","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>Due to their connection to gravitational magic and the space element, the starborn is under the effects of subjective gravity at all times, regardless of the true gravitational features of the plane they are on.</p>"},{"n":"Enforce Gravity","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The starborn enforces gravity in a 40-foot cube within 100 feet. First, they attempt to counteract all effects within the area that allow creatures to fly, hover, or otherwise avoid falling (counteract modifier +39). Then, they choose one of the cube's sides and set it as the new direction of gravity. All creatures in the area must succeed at a DC 47 Reflex save or be knocked Prone by the disorienting shift. Creatures that can't fly immediately fall in the new direction. If they collide with a solid surface, they take the typical bludgeoning damage from falling. The starborn can't use Enforce Gravity again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/rrQWASJf4HM9dxhh":{"lang":["Common","Melodian","Necril","Voltan"],"lore":[["Music Lore",19]],"notes":{"hp":"rejuvenation, void healing"},"abilities":[{"n":"Void Healing","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A creature with void healing draws health from void energy rather than vitality energy. It is damaged by vitality damage and is not healed by vitality healing effects. It does not take void damage, and it is healed by void effects that heal undead.</p></p>"},{"n":"Stormbound","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A storm conductor can't enter buildings or underground areas. They must remain outside under an open sky.</p>"},{"n":"Conductor's Rebuke","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":["electricity","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 60 feet that the storm conductor can hear fails a Performance check</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> A bolt of lightning emerges from the sky and zaps the creature who offends the storm conductor's ears. The triggering creature takes 4d12 electricity damage (DC 28 basic Reflex save). On a failure, the creature is Deafened for one round.</p>"},{"n":"Rejuvenation","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>When a storm conductor is destroyed, they re-form after 2d4 days within 100 feet of where they were previously destroyed, fully healed. A storm conductor can be permanently destroyed only if they hear a truly inspiring and flawless concert.</p>"},{"n":"Tuneless Target","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>If the storm conductor takes sonic damage, they become consumed with rage directed at the source of the offensive discordance. Until the end of their next turn, all of the storm conductor's offensive actions must target the source of the damage. If the storm conductor took sonic damage from multiple sources, they can choose these targets from among them.</p>"},{"n":"Tuning","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","emotion","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The storm conductor attempts to prime their unwilling subjects for the coming performance. The conductor attempts a Performance vs. Will DC check against the Will DCs of each enemy within 30 feet.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Tuning for 1 minute.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature must Perform or use another action that requires a Performance check as it first action on its next turn.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, and the creature is also Stupefied 1 for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/goMX5Hkka6sqx98W":{"abilities":[{"n":"Curl","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The stormadillo coils into a ball to defend itself. It gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC. The stormadillo's speed is reduced to 10 feet, and it can't use its claw attacks or take other actions that require it to use its limbs while in its Curl. It can unfurl as a single action with the manipulate trait, ending the effects of Curl.</p>"},{"n":"Static Cling","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The stormadillo can cling to electrically charged terrain (such as terrain affected by Electrify Domain) and roll along it at great speeds. As long as the stormadillo is clinging to such a surface, it can't be knocked Prone or subject to forced movement, and it can move along walls and ceilings at its full Speed. The stormadillo's Speed increases to 40 feet, or 60 feet while using Curl. If a stormadillo using Static Cling moves out of electrified terrain at any point, its movement immediately ends.</p>"},{"n":"Trample","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Medium or smaller, shell, DC 24 basic Reflex. Trample deals an additional 1d8 electricity damage if the Stormadillo is using Static Cling.</p><hr><p><p>The monster Strides up to double its Speed and can move through the spaces of creatures of the listed size, Trampling each creature whose space it enters. The monster can attempt to Trample the same creature only once in a single use of Trample. The monster deals the damage of the listed Strike, but trampled creatures can attempt a basic Reflex save at the listed DC (no damage on a critical success, half damage on a success, double damage on a critical failure).</p></p>"},{"n":"Electrify Domain","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The stormadillo slams its claws on the ground, creating a 10-foot wide, 120-foot long line of electricity that travels along surfaces (including walls and ceilings), dealing 2d8 electricity damage to all creatures along the line and leaving a lingering band of electrified terrain that persists for 1 minute. Any creature in the line must attempt a DC 24 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes no damage.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full damage and takes a –10-foot penalty to its Speeds for 1 round. As normal, this penalty can't reduce a creature's Speed below 5 feet. Effect: Electrify Domain</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double damage and is Immobilized for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/sJOTFVO8q0cvqEtZ":{"lang":["Common","Diabolic","Shadowtongue","Venenan"],"lore":[["Synthecite Lore",15]],"notes":{"per":"painsight"},"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Painsight","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>A synthecite automatically knows whether a creature they see has any of the Doomed, Dying, and Wounded conditions, as well as the value of those conditions.</p>"},{"n":"Radical Surgery","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The synthecite vivisectionist is adjacent to an Immobilized or Prone creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The synthecite vivisectionist makes two scythe arm Strikes at a –2 penalty against a prone or immobilized target. These attacks count toward the vivisectionist's multiple attack penalty, but the multiple attack penalty doesn't increase until after they make both attacks. If both attacks hit and the creature has been poisoned with synthecite substrate, the poison advances by 1 stage.</p>"},{"n":"Synthecite Substrate","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 23 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> Drained 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> Doomed 1 and Drained 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> doomed 1 Drained 3 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 4</strong> doomed 1 and Drained 4 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 5</strong> dead and transforms into a new vivisectionist (see Sentient Poison)</p>"},{"n":"Sentient Poison","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a creature dies from synthecite substrate, their body transforms into a new synthecite vivisectionist after 1d4 rounds. The transformation takes time to finalize; for the first 24 hours after being created, a synthecite vivisectionist is Slowed 1 and can't use synthecite substrate.</p>"},{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/wVA6f8rAb103Umyh":{"lang":["Common","Pyric","Spirituan"],"gear":["Hatchet (2)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Chilling Presence","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","cold","emotion","fear","mental","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet, DC 18 Will.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The tabilda's heartflame is extinguished</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> As Frightful Presence, except creatures that fail their Will save gain a weakness to cold damage equal to 1 + their frightened value.</p><p>Effect: Chilling Presence</p><p><p>A creature that first enters the area must attempt a Will save.</p>\n<p>Regardless of the result of the saving throw, the creature is temporarily immune to this monster's Frightful Presence for 1 minute.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected by the presence.</p>\n<p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Frightened 1.</p>\n<p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 2.</p>\n<p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is Frightened 4.</p></p>"},{"n":"Heartflame","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>An open fire called a heartflame burns in the tabilda's chest cavity. The heartflame is fragile and difficult to maintain. If the tabilda takes damage, they must succeed on a DC 11 Flat at the start of their next turn or the flame is extinguished. The flame is immediately extinguished if the tabilda takes damage from or fails a saving throw against an effect with the air, cold, or water traits. While the flame is extinguished, the tabilda takes persistent 1d6 cold damage. The flame reignites if the tabilda is exposed to fire or successfully uses Kindle.</p>"},{"n":"Soothing Fire","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet.</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The tabilda's heartflame is burning</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The heartflame emanates warmth and bright light. All creatures in the aura gain resistance 5 to cold. The temperature in the aura is two categories warmer than the ambient temperature, to a maximum of normal temperature (for example, extreme cold becomes mild cold).</p>"},{"n":"Elemental Infusion","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A tabilda's melee Strikes deal 1d6 additional damage; this damage is fire if their heartflame burns or cold if it is extinguished.</p>"},{"n":"Kindle","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","fire","manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>The tabilda attempts a DC 22 Survival check. On a success, they can either reignite their heartflame if it is extinguished or set an unattended, flammable object in an adjacent space alight.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/kVnAJHIGESI6fDHr":{"lang":["Common","Spirituan","Thalassic","Telepathy 100 feet"],"lore":[["Farming Lore",24]],"gear":["Kama (2)"],"notes":{"per":"rain sight","speed":" water walk"},"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Rain Sight","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The tanbogami ignores concealment from fog, mist, and rain, even if they are magically created.</p>"},{"n":"Ward","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>The tanbogami is bound to a rice field. They can merge with or emerge from their ward as a single action with the concentrate trait. While merged, they are Immobilized, but they recover Hit Points each minute as if they spent an entire day resting.</p>"},{"n":"Aura of Rain","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. The tanbogami is surrounded by a downpour of rain, which extinguishes nonmagical flames in the aura. Creatures in the aura are Concealed and gain fire resistance 10.</p>"},{"n":"Rend (Kama)","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A Rend entry lists a Strike the monster has.</p>\n<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster hit the same enemy with two consecutive Strikes of the listed type in the same round.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster automatically deals that Strike's damage again to the enemy.</p></p>"},{"n":"Holy Raindrop Dive","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","holy","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The tanbogami Flies 40 feet straight up into the air, then Flies in a straight line to an empty space of their choice on the ground within 80 feet, crashing down in a crushing deluge of rain. The rain deals 2d8 bludgeoning plus 3d6 spirit damage to all creatures in a 15-foot emanation (DC 30 basic Reflex save). Creatures with the unholy trait take an additional 3d6 spirit damage.</p>"},{"n":"Holy Droplets","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","holy"],"f":"","d":"<p>A tanbogami's melee Strikes deal an additional 1d8 spirit damage, or 2d8 spirit damage vs. unholy targets.</p>"},{"n":"Dual Onslaught","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The tanbogami makes two kama Strikes against the same target, one with each of their kamas. The tanbogami combines the damage of any attacks that hit and applies resistances and weaknesses only once. Both attacks count toward the tanbogami's multiple attack penalty, but the penalty increases only after both attacks. If the tanbogami misses with both kama Strikes, they still deal the damage from one kama to the target, though they still miss completely if both attack rolls were critical failures.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Knockdown","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"}],"strikeNotes":{"Holy Rain Spray":"<p>(8 spirit splash vs. unholy creatures)</p>"}},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/U4q3wiF5enw2wjCo":{"lang":["Aklo","Fey","Sakvroth"],"abilities":[{"n":"Spelltwisting Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>20 feet, creatures who Cast a Spell in the aura, including the cranklejack, must succeed at a DC 23 Will save or the spell becomes a surge of wild magic. Either roll on the Wild Magic table from Battlezoo Dragons: Misfit Dragons or on any other wild magic table you prefer.</p>"},{"n":"Chaotic Gizmos","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The cranklejack unleashes an unpredictable flurry of attacks that even the cranklejack themself can't predict. Roll 1d6 twice. For each roll of 1 or 2, nothing happens. For each roll of 3, the cranklejack makes a hammer Strike, for each roll of 4, the cranklejack make an impaling spike Strike, for each roll of 5, the cranklejack makes a saw Strike, and for each roll of 6, the cranklejack makes a volt fist Strike. If the cranklejack makes two Strikes, they can choose which order to make them.</p>"},{"n":"Twice for Bad Luck","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["misfortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The cranklejack hits the same foe with a second Strike on the same turn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Once is a coincidence, but twice is just bad luck. The foe becomes extremely unlucky (DC 26 Will save; the foe must roll this Will save twice and take the worse result). On a failure, the creature must roll twice and take the worse result on all checks for 2 rounds.</p><p>Effect: Twice for Bad Luck</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/2dKNLlms0fpynzXf":{"lang":["Envisioning"],"notes":{"hp":"regeneration 15 (deactivated by spirit)","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic"},"abilities":[{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Eye of the Storm","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["air","aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>25 feet. The tempestuan is always surrounded by an aura of breathable air. In the absence of magical weather effects, the air within 20 feet of the tempestuan is still, while the air between 20 and 25 feet away from them is constantly experiencing hurricane-force winds. The winds repel creatures and objects, making physical ranged attacks with typical arrows impossible and imposing a –4 circumstance penalty to ranged attacks with siege weapons and other similarly large projectiles. Moving through the winds to exit or enter the eye of the storm requires a successful DC 35 Athletics check. Creatures that enter or exit the aura due to the tempestuan's movement do not need to attempt an Athletics check. The tempestuan can choose to exclude any number of creatures within this aura from their spells and abilities.</p>"},{"n":"Quiet Wind","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 60 feet that the tempestuan can see uses a spell or other effect with the air trait</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> the tempestuan attempts to counteract the triggering spell or effect (counteract modifier +35). If the counteract check succeeds, the caster takes 3d10 persistent sonic damage. If the check fails, the caster is temporarily immune to Quiet Wind for 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Unleash Storm","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","divine","electricity"],"f":"","d":"<p>The tempestuan unleashes the pent-up energy in the hurricane that surrounds them. All creatures in a 60-foot emanation must attempt a DC 40 Reflex save as they are struck by lightning and battered by wind. The wall of hurricane-force wind disappears from Eye of the Storm for 1d4 rounds, and the tempestuan can't use Unleash Storm again until the wall returns.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 4d12 electricity damage and is pushed 25 feet away from the tempestuan.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes 4d12 electricity damage and 10d6 bludgeoning damage and is pushed 50 feet away from the tempestuan.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double the amount of electricity and bludgeoning damage from a failure and is then pushed 100 feet away from the tempestuan.</p>"},{"n":"Master of Storms","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The tempestuan can cast the Control Weather ritual in one hour and doesn't require a secondary caster.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Push 30 Feet","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Improved Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/LDWiSl3QVxJjuisU":{"abilities":[{"n":"Startling Appearance","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The terrordactyl's unsettling appearance transcends language. It does not take a penalty on its checks to Demoralize for not sharing a language with its target.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Pursue Prey","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> An enemy within the terrordactyl's reach attempts to move away from the terrordactyl</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The terrordactyl keeps pace with the retreating foe. The terrordactyl Flies up to its fly Speed, following the enemy and keeping it in reach throughout its movement until the enemy stops moving or the terrordactyl has moved its full fly Speed.</p>"},{"n":"Drop From Above","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The terrordactyl is Hiding while hanging upside down from a surface that is at least 15 feet off the ground, such as a cave ceiling or a rocky cliff face</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The terrordactyl swoops down, Flying up to twice its Speed and then it makes a jaws or talon Strike against a creature in its reach.</p>"},{"n":"Swooping Bite","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The terrordactyl Flies, making jaws Strikes against any number of creatures that are adjacent to its path. Its multiple attack penalty applies to these Strikes normally.</p>"},{"n":"Blend with Shadows","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Terrordactyls are particularly adept at Hiding in shadowy areas. They have the Concealed condition in dim light against creatures with low-light vision (but not creatures with darkvision), and in darkness against creatures with darkvision (but not creatures with greater darkvision).</p>"},{"n":"Terrifying Ambush","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The sudden appearance of a terrordactyl terrifies its prey. When a terrordactyl hits a creature that is Off-Guard against it with a Strike, that creature takes 1d6 additional precision damage and must succeed at a DC 24 Will save or become Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ki4PBlk1PDQVXEG1":{"lang":["Chthonian","Common","Diabolic","Empyrean","Fey","Melodian","Necril","Requian"],"gear":["Soul Feather (10)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"False Guide","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The thananycti's magic repels efforts to pierce their disguise. They automatically attempt a counteract check (counteract modifier +35) against effects or abilities that would determine their traits. On a success, the effect seems to work but falsely claims that they are a monitor without the unholy trait.</p>"},{"n":"Take Under Wing","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","occult","unholy"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> At least one of the thananycti's soul feathers doesn't contain a soul</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The thananycti traps the soul of a creature of up to 18th level in an empty soul feather on one of their wings. This functions as seize soul, using a feather in place of a valuable item, except the target must be either a creature who died within the last minute while drained from Sorrowful Melody or an incorporeal undead that is drained from Sorrowful Melody. When a living creature's soul trapped, its body swiftly turns to dust. The feathers generally can't be destroyed while attached to a living thananycti, but an adjacent creature can pluck a soul feather by spending two actions and succeeding on a DC 40 Thievery check.</p>"},{"n":"Spirit Touch","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A thananycti's Strikes have the benefit of a <em>ghost touch</em> property rune and deal an additional 3d6 void damage to living creatures or 3d6 vitality damage to undead.</p>"},{"n":"Sorrowful Melody","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","incapacitation","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The thananycti sings an eerie song. Each living or undead creature within a 60-foot emanation must attempt a DC 38 Will save. Despite being a mental effect, this ability affects mindless undead.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is temporarily immune to Sorrowful Melody for 24 hours.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is Stupefied 1 for one round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is stupefied 1 for one minute and Drained 1. If the target was already drained, the value of the condition increases by 1 (to a maximum of Drained 4). Additionally, the creature is entranced by the thananycti and must spend the first action on its next turn to move closer to the thananycti as expediently as possible while avoiding obvious dangers. If it is already adjacent to the thananycti, it instead spends its first action standing still.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the creature must spend all of its actions on its next turn to move toward the thananycti, standing still once it is adjacent.</p>"},{"n":"Devour Soul","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["occult","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> A soul has been trapped in a soul feather for 24 hours</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The thananycti consumes the soul. The soul is utterly destroyed, and the thananycti regains HP equal to three times the creature's level.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/TjKN1EdH5UAHUUz8":{"abilities":[{"n":"Time Magic Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a time warp is targeted by or in the area of a spell that has the time trait or that grants the Quickened or Slowed conditions, it takes 5d8 force damage instead of the spell's normal effects. If the spell requires an attack roll, this vulnerability only applies if the attack roll hits.</p>"},{"n":"Decelerate Time","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","mental","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The time warp decelerates time in area around it, slowing nearby creatures and causing them mental distress. Creatures in a 30-foot emanation take 6d6 mental damage and experience additional effects based on the results of a DC 29 Will save. The time warp can't use this ability again until it uses Accelerate Time.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage, and they are also Slowed 1 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full damage, and they are also slowed 1 and Stupefied 1 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double damage, and they are also Slowed 2 and Stupefied 2 for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Accelerate Time","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["force","manipulate","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p>The time warp accelerates time in the area around it, quickening nearby creatures and subjecting them to entropic forces. Creatures in a 30-foot emanation take 6d6 force damage and experience additional effects based on the results of a DC 29 Fortitude save. Creatures that are Quickened from can only use the extra action to Stride or Strike. The time warp can't use this ability again until it uses Decelerate Time.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes no damage and is quickened for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage and is quickened for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full damage and is quickened and Enfeebled 1 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double damage and is Enfeebled 2 for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Disrupt Chronomancy","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["mental","occult","time"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The time warp hits a target with a time lash Strike, and the target is affected by a magical effect that has the time trait or that grants the Quickened or Slowed condition</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The time warp attempts to remove the effect from that creature, rolling a counteract check against the effect (counteract modifier +21). If successful, the effect ends on the creature (but not any other affected creatures), and the creature takes 4d8 mental damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/SgOQYk15XW8eDCaV":{"lang":["Common","Can't speak any language"],"abilities":[{"n":"Plush Defense","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature targets the toyblox with an attack and the toyblox can see the attacker</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The toyblox manifests a plush toy between itself and the incoming blow, gaining a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Toy Chest","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The toyblox has a hollow interior, which it can use to store up to 25 Bulk worth of items without being encumbered. It can release any number of objects held within by spending a manipulate action. It can also allow other creatures to take what it is holding. When the toyblox is within a creature's reach, a creature can Interact with the toyblox to stow or retrieve items as if it were a mundane box. If the toyblox is not willing to have the object stowed or retrieved, the creature must first succeed at a DC 25 Athletics check.</p>"},{"n":"Temporary Toy","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","manipulate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>1 minute. The toyblox conjures forth a temporary toy, which must have a total size of 1 cubic foot or smaller and lasts for 1 hour. The toy can include multiple pieces, such as a jigsaw puzzle, and it can include moving parts. The toy is sturdy enough to survive typical use, though it isn't usually suitable for use as an improvised weapon. It can take the form of a common level 0 piece of adventuring gear with a value of 1 gp or less, but it can't typically replicate more complex or expensive items.</p>"},{"n":"Tidy Up","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The toyblox tidies up its environment. All unattended objects within 30 feet fly into the toyblox's internal toy chest. If the items would exceed the toy chest's bulk limit, the toyblox chooses which items to leave behind. Non-magical dust, dirt, and grime disappear from all objects and surfaces within the range. The toyblox attempts a counteract check (counteract modifier +12) against magical sources of mess in the area, such as the grease spell. If the counteract check fails, it can't attempt to Tidy Up that same effect a second time.</p>"},{"n":"Put That Away!","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The toyblox last action was a successful slamming lid Strike against a creature of size Large or smaller</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The toyblox disapproves of the use of dangerous objects like weapons. The toyblox attempts to Disarm the creature, ignoring the typical requirement of having a free hand. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the toyblox's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Conjure Guardian","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["occult","summon"],"f":"","d":"<p>The toyblox conjures a giant toy soldier, which uses the statistics of animated armor. It can Sustain the toy soldier for up to 1 minute. The soldier is metaphysically linked to the toyblox's life force. If the toy soldier is reduced to 0 Hit Points, the toyblox takes 10 untyped damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/jAaTydbGggb8hUgN":{"lang":["Aetheran","Astral","Common","Plus all languages spoken by its creator"],"lore":[["Creator Lore",13]],"gear":["Ring of Sigils"],"abilities":[{"n":"Creator's Memories","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hand gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Perception checks when it Seeks its creator, to Survival checks when it Tracks its creator, and to damage rolls when it Strikes its creator.</p>"},{"n":"Scramble","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The treacherous telekinetic hand is targeted by a melee attack by an attacker it can see</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The treacherous telekinetic hand gains a +2 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack. After the attack resolves, the hand Strides, Climbs, or Flies up to 10 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Choke. Choke. CHOKE!","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The hand deals 2d6 bludgeoning damage to a creature that it has Grabbed or Restrained (DC 20 basic Fortitude save). If the creature is restrained, the treacherous telekinetic hand also attempts a check to Demoralize it.</p>"},{"n":"Squeeze Throat","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that is Grabbed by the treacherous telekinetic hand has difficulty speaking or swallowing and must spend an extra action to perform any action that requires speaking, such as casting spells.</p>"},{"n":"Tenacious Strangler","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A treacherous telekinetic hand can grapple creatures up to size Medium, and it can grapple its creator no matter how large they are. However, the hand's grip is particularly easy to dislodge with assistance. If a creature is Grabbed or Restrained by the hand and another creature succeeds at a check to Aid their Escape, the grabbed or restrained creature can immediately attempt to Escape as a reaction.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/aNpCv8zW8bJGTH47":{"lang":["Thalassic"],"lore":[["Deep Sea Lore",28]],"notes":{"per":"heatsense (imprecise) 120 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Heatsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Trench lords sense all nearby sources of heat, such as hydrothermal vents and living creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Waterbound","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When not touching water, the trench lord is Slowed 1 and can't use reactions.</p>"},{"n":"Benthic Compression","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["primal","water"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature spends an action to move into a square within 15 feet trench lord while underwater</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trench lord momentarily pressurizes the water around the creature, exposing its body to rapid compression and decompression. The creature takes 2d10 bludgeoning damage (DC 34 Fortitude save). On a failed save, it becomes Drained 1 (or Drained 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Sulfide Cloud","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet. A creature that starts its turn in the aura takes 2d6+7 poison damage (DC 31 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Improved Push 15 feet","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Improved Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Pull 15 Feet","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The trench lord hits with their surge Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The trench lord uses Pull.</p><hr><p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a success with a Strike that lists Pull in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Reposition the creature, moving it closer to the monster. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Pull lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pulled on a success to that distance.</p></p>"},{"n":"Boiling Assault","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>Fire damage dealt by the trench lord results from volatile chemical reactions. It ignores half of the target's resistance to fire.</p>"},{"n":"Riptide Rush","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The trench lord moves up to 500 feet in a straight line through the water without triggering reactions. Creatures within 15 feet of a square that the trench lord passes through during this movement must succeed at a DC 34 Reflex save or be Off-Guard for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Torrent","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","primal","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The trench lord vastly increases their internal pressure before releasing it in a concentrated blast of boiling water. All creatures in a 90-foot line take 4d12 bludgeoning plus 2d12 fire damage (DC 34 basic Reflex save). A creature that fails this save is pushed 30 feet away from the trench lord, or 60 feet on a critical failure.</p>"},{"n":"Vent","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fire","poison","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The trench lord's body expels the superheated chemicals that churn within. All creatures in a 30-foot emanation take 6d6 poison plus 6d6 fire damage (DC 34 basic Fortitude save). A creature that fails this save is also Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure). The trench lord can't use Vent again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/OwOUJlqRJuIcWzlK":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Pyric","Spirituan"],"abilities":[{"n":"Fear Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>An ugadalu is their own worst nightmare. When an ugadalu starts their turn frightened, they take 1d8 mental damage. If an ugadalu that was not already frightened sees an ugadalu within 30 feet, whether it be another ugadalu, a creature wearing an ugadalu's mask, or a clear reflection of their own face, the ugadalu becomes Frightened 1. While within 30 feet of this fearful sight, the ugadalu can't reduce the value of their frightened condition below 1.</p>"},{"n":"Jump Scare","a":"1","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature moves within 30 feet of the ugadalu while the ugadalu is in Statue Form</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> Initiative has not yet been rolled</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The ugadalu attempts an Intimidation check to Demoralize the triggering creature, using their Intimidation result for their initiative.</p>"},{"n":"Feast on Fear","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The ugadalu's jaws Strike deals an additional 2d6 precision damage to frightened creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Spew Flame","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ugadalu concentrates their stream of fire and emits a burst of flames that deals 8d6 fire damage in a 30-foot cone (DC 25 basic Reflex save). They can't use Spew Flame again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Statue Form","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","polymorph","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The ugadalu transforms, taking the form of a wooden statue of a warrior. Perception checks don't typically reveal the ugadalu's true nature, but a creature who examines the statue attempts a secret DC 25 Crafting check; on a success, they are able to determine that the statue is alive. While in statue form, an ugadalu can observe everything around them, but they can't receive a result better than a failure on Reflex save, so if they roll a success or critical success, they get a failure instead. They can't act other to Dismiss this effect or use Jump Scare.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/nlYfiMrcHJbJ1vbp":{"lang":["Arboreal","Common","Fey","Speak with plants"],"lore":[["Forest Lore",30]],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Improved Pull 50 Feet","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unbound arboreal hits with their boundless root Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal uses Pull.</p><hr><p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a success with a Strike that lists Pull in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Reposition the creature, moving it closer to the monster. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Pull lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pulled on a success to that distance.</p></p>"},{"n":"False Felling","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"once per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per day</p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unbound arboreal is reduced to 0 Hit Points, and their wounded value is 2 or less</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal's trunk splits, crashing down on their foes before rewinding time to remain standing. All creatures in a 20-foot line take 6d8 bludgeoning damage (DC 33 basic Reflex save). The arboreal avoids being knocked Unconscious and remains at 1 Hit Point, but their wounded value increases by 1.</p>"},{"n":"Stumbling Roots","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature attempts to uses an action with the move trait to exit a square within 15 feet of the unbound arboreal</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal raises the base of one of their roots out of the ground, attempting to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the unbound arboreal's multiple attack penalty.</p>"},{"n":"Autumn's Abscission","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by autumn</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal unleashes a shower of razor-sharp leaves, dealing 8d6 slashing damage to all creatures in a 15-foot emanation (DC 36 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Spring's Blossoming","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["healing","primal","vitality"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by spring</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal draws on spring's new growth, shedding healing petals. The unbound arboreal and all living creatures of the arboreal's choice in a 15-foot emanation recover 6d8 healing Hit Points, and all undead creatures within 15 feet take 6d8 vitality damage (DC 36 basic Fortitude save).</p>"},{"n":"Summer's Tangle","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["plant","primal"],"f":"once per round","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per round</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by summer</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal spreads summer's wild growth, causing all squares in a 15-foot emanation to become greater difficult terrain until the start of their next turn. The unbound arboreal is not impeded by this growth. In addition, a creature that ends its turn in an affected space must succeed at a DC 33 Reflex save or become Grabbed by the unbound arboreal until the end of that creature's next turn (Escape).</p>"},{"n":"Winter's Withering","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["cold","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The unbound arboreal is influenced by winter</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal invokes the withering chill of winter, enervating those in their vicinity. Each creature in a 15-foot emanation takes 10d6 cold damage (DC 36 basic Fortitude save); creatures that fail additionally become Slowed 1 for 1 round, or for 1 minute on a critical failure.</p>"},{"n":"Confluence of Seasons","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The unbound arboreal's turn begins</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The unbound arboreal can control their passage through the cycle of seasons if they don't want to remain in their current season. The arboreal becomes influenced by either the previous season in the cycle or the next. The influencing season determines which abilities they can use. An unbound arboreal typically begins an encounter influenced by the current season.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ggwd8gqyyYCtdb5f":{"abilities":[{"n":"Bite Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>Due to being made out of food, the vengeful crab bowl takes 5 additional damage from jaws Strikes, fangs Strikes, or other similar Strikes with a creature's mouth. When it is Grabbed or Restrained by a creature's jaws, fangs, or mouth, the DC to Escape is increased by 2.</p>"},{"n":"Spill Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a vengeful crab bowl is knocked Prone, some of its broth spills out onto the ground. It becomes Drained 1; this is cumulative with other drained conditions from Spill Vulnerability, to a maximum of Drained 4. Additionally, all creatures within a 10-foot emanation take 2d6 fire damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Goopy Egg","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature hit by the vengeful crab bowl's egg drop Strike is covered in sticky egg goop, taking a –10 circumstance penalty to their Speeds for 1 minute or until they move a total of 40 feet.</p><p>Effect: Goopy Egg</p>"},{"n":"Boil Over","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire"],"f":"","d":"<p>The vengeful crab bowl flies into a boiling rage, superheating its broth. For the next minute, it takes a –1 circumstance penalty to its AC, but deals an additional 1d6 fire damage to creatures it hits with a Strike. Additionally, any creature that hits the crab soup with an unarmed Strike or otherwise touches it during this time takes 3d6 fire damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Rice Ball","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","fire","water"],"f":"","d":"<p>The vengeful crab bowl launches a glob of steaming hot rice with a range of 60 feet. When the glob hits the ground, it explodes in a 20-foot burst of hot steam that persists for 2 rounds. Creatures that start their turn in the area take 5d6 fire damage (DC 24 basic Reflex save). All creatures within the steam become Concealed, and all creatures outside the steam become concealed to creatures within it. The vengeful crab bowl can't use Rice Ball for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/FEGVklTE5yEyBocO":{"lang":["Common","Can't speak any language"],"notes":{"speed":"mudstrider"},"abilities":[{"n":"Dirty Retribution","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["arcane","earth"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature succeeds at a melee Strike against the vengeful doormat</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The doormat angrily summons forth and flings dirt at the offending creature, attempting to disgust it. The creature must succeed at a DC 15 Fortitude save or be Sickened 1.</p>"},{"n":"Foot Vulnerability","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A vengeful doormat takes 2 additional damage from Strikes made with feet. A creature can Grapple a vengeful doormat without a free hand by entering the doormat's square and stepping on it.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Mud Spray","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once per hour</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The vengeful doormat shakes itself off, spraying massive quantities of mud out in a 15-foot cone. The muddy area is difficult terrain. The mud persists for 1 hour before reappearing on the doormat's body.</p>"},{"n":"Unwelcome Mat","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vengeful doormat flattens and folds its body down to the ground. Until the next time it acts, the vengeful doormat appears to be a mundane doormat. It has an automatic result of 27 on Deception checks and DCs to pass as a doormat.</p>"},{"n":"Mudstrider","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vengeful doormat moves at full speed through difficult terrain caused by mud.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/NMIvy0ScC2YkbEUI":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Venenan"],"notes":{"saves":"+1 circumstance vs. poison","per":"emotionsense (imprecise) 60 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"+1 Circumstance to All Saves vs. Poison","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Venomous Mind","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["mental","occult","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature uses a mental effect on the venopath, attempts to communicate telepathically with the venopath, or attempts to read the venopath's mind</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The venopath deals 5d6 poison damage to the triggering creature with a DC 26 basic Will save. The damage increases to 8d6 poison if the creature attempted to read the venopath's mind.</p>"},{"n":"Emotive Toxin","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["emotion","mental","occult","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 26 Will</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 6 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 1d6 mental plus 1d6 poison damage, and Stupefied 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 2d6 mental plus 2d6 poison damage and Stupefied 2 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 3d6 mental plus 3d6 poison damage, and Stupefied 3 (1 round).</p>"},{"n":"Toxic Intimidation","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","emotion","fear","mental","occult","poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>The venopath chooses a creature within 30 feet and fills its thoughts with toxic imagery. The venopath attempts an Intimidation vs. Will DC check against the target's Will DC.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target takes 6d8 poison damage and becomes Frightened 2.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes 3d8 poison damage and becomes Frightened 1.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target is unaffected and is temporarily immune to Toxic Intimidation for 1 hour.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/zGsgfo7RsM8Pebx9":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Melodian","Sussuran","Voltan"],"notes":{"per":"stormsight"},"abilities":[{"n":"Booming Cloak","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p>Attempts to hinder the vernal's passage are met with a punishing crack of thunder. A creature that successfully Strikes the vernal with a reaction triggered by movement takes 4d6 sonic damage (DC 25 basic Fortitude save). On a failure, they are also Deafened for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Drown Out","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within 60 feet uses an ability with the auditory or sonic traits</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> With overwhelming sound, the vernal attempts to counteract the effect, with a counteract modifier of +17 and a counteract rank of 4.</p>"},{"n":"Thunderous Retreat","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["air","primal","sonic"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The vernal is adjacent to at least one enemy</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Letting loose a sonic boom, the vernal Strides or Flies twice to a space not adjacent to any enemies. All enemies adjacent to the vernal at any point take 6d6 sonic damage (DC 25 Fortitude save). Any creature that fails its save is pushed back 5 feet from the movement path (or 10 feet on a critical failure). The vernal can't use Thunderous Retreat again for 1d4 rounds.</p>"},{"n":"Lightning Improviser","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A vernal can cast their Electric Arc cantrip with a single action to target only one creature, or they can instead use three actions to target three creatures and increase the damage dice to d6s.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/zQSl56dEyy20YFhb":{"lang":["Requian","Can't speak any language, Manifest empathy"],"abilities":[{"n":"Living Flame","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vigil flame is a literal flame contained in a lantern, and so it sheds bright light in a 60-foot radius and dim light in the next 60 feet.</p>"},{"n":"Manifest Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vigil flame can communicate on a rudimentary level with all intelligent creatures by moving their flame and changing their color. This communication is limited to basic concepts and emotions.</p>"},{"n":"Snuff the Flames","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["divine","fire","vitality","void"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The vigil flame is reduced to 0 Hit Points</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> In a last, bright flash, the vigil flame consumes themselves completely. All allies within 20 feet of the vigil flame regain 2d6 healing Hit Points, and all foes within 30 feet take 2d6 damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save); this damage is 2d6 void to living creatures or 2d6 vitality to undead.</p>"},{"n":"Stoke the Flames","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","fire","vitality","void"],"f":"","d":"<p>The vigil flame's flame burns brighter and hotter, both aiding those in need and punishing their foes. Living allies within a 20-foot burst gain a +1 status bonus to attack rolls, damage rolls, and saves against fear effects for 1 round. Living foes in the radius take 3d6 fire plus 3d6 void damage, and undead foes in the radius take 3d6 fire plus 3d6 vitality damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save). The vigil flame can't use Stoke the Flames again for 1d4 rounds.</p><p>Effect: Stoke the Flames</p>"},{"n":"Shepherd's Touch","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A vigil flame's Strikes always have the benefit of a <em>ghost touch</em> property rune, and they deal an additional 2d6 void damage to living creatures or an additional 2d6 vitality damage to undead.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Tz3SiS6dq1TVzzkz":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Jyoti","Spirituan"],"notes":{"per":"plantsense 60 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Plantsense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vitatella is aware of all plants within 60 feet as a precise sense. They can sense anything in contact with these plants as an imprecise sense.</p>"},{"n":"Growth Aura","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","plant","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>30 feet. Plants in the aura sprout and flourish. The area is difficult terrain for all creatures that are not vitatella. Each square of difficult terrain can be removed by spells or abilities that deal fire damage to an area. The vitatella can use a single concentrate action to regrow all destroyed plants.</p>"},{"n":"Pollen Cloud","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The vitatella causes large flowers to sprout and release pollen. The pollen floats in the vitatella's growth aura for 1 round. All creatures within the mist become Concealed, and all creatures outside the mist become concealed to creatures within it; the vitatella can see clearly through their own pollen. Each creature that enters the area or that starts its turn in the area must attempt a DC 26 Fortitude save. The vitatella can't use Pollen Cloud again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes 2d6 poison damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature becomes afflicted with Lung Clot Pollen at stage 1.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature becomes afflicted with Lung Clot Pollen at stage 2.</p>"},{"n":"Lung Clot Pollen","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["poison"],"f":"","d":"<p>While a creature who is afflicted by this poison attempts a verbal action, it must succeed at a DC 5 Flat or the action is lost</p><p><strong>Saving Throw</strong> DC 26 Fortitude</p><p><strong>Maximum Duration</strong> 5 rounds</p><p><strong>Stage 1</strong> 2d6 poison damage and Sickened 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 2</strong> 3d6 poison damage and sickened 1 (1 round)</p><p><strong>Stage 3</strong> 4d6 poison damage and Sickened 2 (1 round)</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/6pFKNWj3Bfl9R50V":{"lang":["Common","Necril","Petran","Pyric"],"gear":["Magma Shield"],"abilities":[{"n":"Eruptive Shield","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity knight carries a magma shield. In the knight's hands, the shield has Hardness 15, HP 120, and BT 60. The knight can spend 10 minutes to create a new Eruptive Shield; doing so destroys any existing shield.</p>"},{"n":"Overwhelming Heat","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>15 feet, 8d6 fire, DC 33 basic Fortitude</p>"},{"n":"Reactive Strike (Special)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity knight can use Reactive Strike when a creature within their reach takes persistent fire damage, in addition to its normal trigger. If the triggering creature already had persistent fire damage, the calamity knight triggers a secondary eruption. The triggering creature and all creatures in a 5-foot emanation take 2d10 fire damage (DC 36 basic Reflex).</p><hr><p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature within the monster's reach uses a manipulate action or a move action, makes a ranged attack, or leaves a square during a move action it's using.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts a melee Strike against the triggering creature. If the attack is a critical hit and the trigger was a manipulate action, the monster disrupts that action. This Strike doesn't count toward the monster's multiple attack penalty, and its multiple attack penalty doesn't apply to this Strike.</p></p>"},{"n":"Shield Block (Special)","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity knight gains 1 extra reaction each round, which they can use only to Shield Block.</p><hr><p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster has its shield raised and takes damage from a physical attack.</p>\n<hr>\n<p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster snaps its shield into place to deflect a blow. The shield prevents the monster from taking an amount of damage up to the shield's Hardness. The monster and the shield each take any remaining damage, possibly breaking or destroying the shield.</p></p>"},{"n":"Volcanic Defense","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The Calamity knight Raises a Shield. All creatures in a 5-foot emanation take 2d10 fire damage and 2d10 persistent fire damage (DC 36 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Layering Lava","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>As the calamity knight continually piles magma on a target, it becomes harder to remove. Whenever the calamity knight would deal persistent fire damage to a creature that already has persistent fire damage, the DC of the flat check to remove the persistent fire damage increases by 1 (to a maximum DC of 20).</p><p>Effect: Layering Lava</p>"},{"n":"Magma Prison","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["earth","fire","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity knight cools the magma on one of its foes into a rocky prison by transferring the heat into the foe's body. The knight chooses a creature within 60 feet who is taking persistent fire damage from one of their abilities. The creature takes 4d10 fire damage, becomes Clumsy 1, and takes a –10 status penalty to its Speeds until it Escapes. The persistent fire damage automatically ends.</p><p>Effect: Magma Prison</p>"},{"n":"Pyroclastic Rush","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["move"],"f":"","d":"<p>The calamity knight transforms into a pyroclastic flow. They travel up to 200 feet in a straight line, passing freely though creature's squares (though this movement can still trigger reactions). All creatures in their path take 7d6 fire plus 7d6 bludgeoning damage (DC 38 basic Reflex), and debris left behind makes the path difficult terrain. The calamity knight can't use Pyroclastic Rush for 1d4 rounds.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/e0Q5qWbdR1rIRm6y":{"abilities":[{"n":"Reactive Zap","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature hits the volt ram with a melee attack roll using either an unarmed attack or a metal weapon</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The volt ram has Stored Charge</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> Some of the electricity stored in the volt ram's fleece surges into the target, dealing 1d6 electricity damage (DC 18 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Store Charge","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A volt ram's wool is exceptionally capable of storing electricity. Whenever a volt ram is targeted by or in the area of an effect that deals electricity damage, or when it uses Running Charge, its wool captures and stores the electric charge.</p>"},{"n":"Discharge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The volt ram releases stored static electricity in a blast of crackling lightning. All creatures in a 10-foot emanation around the volt ram take 2d6 electricity damage (DC 16 basic Reflex save). A creature that critically fails the saving throw is also Stunned 1. The volt ram can't use Discharge again until it Stores Charge.</p>"},{"n":"Running Charge","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The volt ram runs and charges up the static electricity as it does. It Strides twice and Stores Charge.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/toJlCvwy0iVqOeI5":{"lang":["Aklo","Common","Voskan"],"gear":["Scroll of Heal (Rank 4)","Leather Armor","Shortsword","Thieves' Toolkit","Repair Toolkit (Superb)","Electrosphere"],"abilities":[{"n":"Ethereal Flight","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A voska's wings are optimized for flight in areas with subjective gravity, such as the Ethereal Plane. A voska's fly speed in areas of subjective gravity is 60 feet. With exposure and diligent training, some voskas, such as the voska bounty hunter, develop the ability to fly in normal gravity.</p>"},{"n":"Zap","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A creature that takes damage from a voska bounty hunter's electrosphere is Shocked for 1 round. A shocked creature is Off-Guard against attacks that deal electricity damage (even if it's only additional electricity damage, such as a shock weapon) and takes –2 circumstance penalty on Fortitude and Reflex saving throws against electricity effects. The shocked condition ends early if the creature takes any amount of electricity damage from a source other than persistent electricity damage, or if they spend an Interact action to discharge the electricity harmlessly.</p>"},{"n":"Electrosphere","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The voska bounty hunter carries a jury-rigged magic item called an <em>electrosphere</em>. While holding the <em>electrosphere</em> in one hand, they can make electrosphere pulse Strikes and Electrosnares. The <em>electrosphere</em> also causes any nonmagical metal weapon held in their other hand to deal an additional 1d12 electricity damage.</p>"},{"n":"Trick Magic Item","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["manipulate"],"f":"","d":"<p>As the Trick Magic item skill feat, except the voska bounty hunter can roll a Crafting check in place of Arcana, Nature, Occultism, or Religion. When required, their spell DC is 25 and their spell attack modifier is +17.</p>"},{"n":"Electrosnare","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["arcane","electricity","incapacitation","nonlethal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The voska bounty hunter is holding their electrosphere and a creature within 60 feet has the shocked condition</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The voska bounty hunter activates their electrosphere to supercharge the electricity cracking through the body of a shocked target within 60 feet, causing its muscles to lock up. The creature takes 1d12 electricity damage and might have its movement impaired based on the results of a Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target takes half damage and is Stunned 1 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target takes full damage is Stunned 2 for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target takes double electricity damage is Paralyzed for 1 round.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/8xbTrq6MiN8tPh5z":{"lang":["Chthonian","Diabolic","Empyrean","Requian","Telepathy 100 feet, Truespeech"],"abilities":[{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Phantasmal Tormentor","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"3 times per day","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per day for each mask</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The wagabago activates one of their three masks, causing it to fly off their face and spin an illusory body that mimics a Medium creature. This functions as a 6th-rank Illusory Creature, except that creatures who disbelieve the illusion do not recover any damage taken and continue to take full damage from the illusion. Additionally, the illusion can use a special ability based on its mask.</p><ul><li><strong>Trauma</strong> The illusion takes on the form of a long-buried memory.</li><li><strong>Persecution</strong> The illusion takes on the form of an authority figure that abuses their power.</li><li><strong>Temptation</strong> The illusion takes on the form of a person who promises hope, redemption, power, or pleasure.</li></ul>"},{"n":"Walk the Ethereal Line","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["divine","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The wagabago slides off the Ethereal Plane to walk the thin line between the Ethereal Plane and the Universe, existing on both planes simultaneously. They can spend one action to exit this boundary; if they do, they only exist on the Ethereal Plane.</p>"},{"n":"Lingering Terror","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>Creatures hit by a fear spear Strike do not reduce their frightened condition automatically at the end of their turns.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/GbB8QdaHBaGKzDlG":{"abilities":[{"n":"Twist the Knife","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The illusion's last action was a successful Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The illusion aggravates the wound it just inflicted, dealing 3d6 persistent bleed damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/bKAlt8e7QE8jSUh6":{"abilities":[{"n":"Beautiful Illusion","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","illusion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>All non-fiend creatures within 20 feet must succeed a DC 30 Will save or become Dazzled for 1 round (or 3 rounds on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/bvk3bmx17qyD1Gll":{"abilities":[{"n":"Traumatic Memories","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","illusion","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>All non-fiend creatures within 20 feet must succeed at a DC 30 Will save or become Sickened 1 (Sickened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/Lp7wnIL4pwfdfCVm":{"lang":["Arboreal","Common","Spirituan","Can't speak any language"],"gear":["Musical Instrument (Virtuoso handheld) (4)"],"abilities":[{"n":"Death of Music","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["curse","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a creature kills a waltzing willow, it must succeed at a DC 29 Will save or become cursed. While cursed in this way, the creature can no longer hear music at all. The creature is Deafened only to instruments and sung voices and the creature can no longer benefit from composition spells.</p>"},{"n":"Improved Knockdown","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature as a free action. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"},{"n":"Spirit Lights","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":["light","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The waltzing willow is surrounded by the glowing spirits of four musicians, which each shed light in a 60-foot radius. Once per round, the willow can spend one action with the concentrate trait to move each spirit up to 60 feet. At the end of each spirit's movement, the willow can attach it to an adjacent creature, who must attempt a DC 32 Reflex save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The spirit attaches itself to the creature for 1 round. While the spirit is attached, the creature is Dazzled. If it was invisible, it becomes Concealed, and if it was already concealed for any other reason, it is no longer concealed.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> As success, except the spirit remains attached for 3 rounds.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As success, except the spirit remains attached for 1 minute.</p>"},{"n":"Spotlight","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","emotion","light","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>The waltzing willow fills a 30-foot burst within 120 feet with light as their spirit's performance swells to a crescendo. All creatures in the spotlight must attempt a DC 32 Reflex save or a DC 28 Performance check as they are swept into a dance. Waltzing willows are not immune to Spotlight, but they receive the results of a critical success if they roll a success. The Waltzing willow can't use Spotlight again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target dances exceedingly well. If they rolled a Performance check, they are Quickened from the momentum until the end of its next turn; they can use this extra action only to Stride.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target stumbles over its feet, becoming Off-Guard until the end of the waltzing willow's next turn or until it Steps.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target's dance places horrific strain on its body as it fails to keep up with the music. It takes 12d6 bludgeoning damage and falls Prone.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> As failure, but the target takes double damage.</p>"},{"n":"Two Step Waltz","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The waltzing willow Steps twice and can cast a cantrip.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/kuFQolHcEUddmS9y":{"lang":["Sussuran","Voltan"],"notes":{"speed":"grounded"},"abilities":[{"n":"Deflecting Gust","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["air","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The weatherbane is the target of a physical ranged attack</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The weatherbane is aware of the attack and not Off-Guard</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The weatherbane gains a +4 circumstance bonus to AC against the triggering attack.</p>"},{"n":"Electroblast","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["electricity","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>With a smell of ozone, the weatherbane calls for the might of the storm. They attempt an electrobolt Strike. If the Strike hits, the target and any creatures within a 15-foot emanation around the target take 1d6 electricity damage (DC 20 basic Fortitude save). Any creature that fails its save also takes a –10-foot status penalty to its Speeds for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Blowback","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A Large or smaller creature takes damage from the weatherbane's gust Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The weatherbane attempts to blow the creature away from them, rolling a Nature check against the creature's Fortitude DC. The creature is blown back 10 feet on a success, or 20 feet on a critical success.</p>"},{"n":"Wind Blast","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["air","manipulate","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The weatherbane changes the direction of the wind in a 60-foot emanation until the start of their next turn. They can choose to make the wind in the entire area point in a specific direction, to draw the wind toward themselves, or to push the wind away from themselves. All Large or smaller creatures in the area must attempt a DC 18 Fortitude save. Large or smaller creatures that later enter the area while the winds persist must also attempt this save. The weatherbane can't use Wind Blast again for 1d4 rounds.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature can't move against the wind.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is pushed 30 feet in the wind's direction and knocked Prone. If it was flying, it experiences the effects of critical failure instead.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is pushed 60 feet in the wind's direction, knocked prone, and takes 2d6 bludgeoning damage.</p>"},{"n":"Grounded","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>As an enraged spirit in a metal prison, a weatherbane can only spin in place. They can't move or be moved, except through teleportation or similar magical means. If a weatherbane is moved, the grounding connection is severed, freeing the spirit within and destroying the weatherbane.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/wVvrX49kTdaZPMSL":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Thalassic"],"notes":{"per":"lucksense (imprecise) 330 feet"},"abilities":[{"n":"Lucksense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>A wellwisher senses the threads of fate that dance around creatures affected by fortune or misfortune effects.</p>"},{"n":"Wish Twist","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["fortune","misfortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature who previously made a wish in the well would attempt a check in pursuit of fulfilling their wish, or a creature who took damage from one of the wellwisher's Strikes in the last minute would attempt a check</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The creature must immediately attempt a DC 13 Flat. On a success, the creature rolls twice and takes the better result on the triggering check; on a failure, it rolls twice and take the worse result. After using Wish Twist on a creature, the wellwisher can't use Wish Twist on that creature again until that creature makes another wish or they hit the creature with another Strike.</p>"},{"n":"Trinary Luck","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":["fortune","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The wellwisher rolls a 3 or 13 on a check</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The wellwisher can choose to resolve the check as if they had rolled a 20 instead. If they do, the next time they roll a 20 on a check against an opponent of at least level 5; they treat this 20 as if they had rolled a 3 instead. This mandatory conversion is not a fortune or misfortune effect and happens after all fortune or misfortune effects are applied. After turning a 3 or 13 into a 20, they can't do so again until after a 20 has been turned into a 3.</p>"},{"n":"Knockdown","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Knockdown in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Trip the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty.</p></p>"},{"n":"Improved Push","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Trigger</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Improved Push in its damage entry</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The monster attempts to Shove the creature. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the monster's multiple attack penalty. If Improved Push lists a distance, change the distance the creature is pushed on a success to that distance.</p></p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/dHbYxUPOegI4rAS3":{"lang":["Fey","Thalassic"],"lore":[["Ocean Depths Lore",24]],"gear":["Bone Harpoon"],"notes":{"per":"wavesense (varies) 1 mile"},"abilities":[{"n":"Aquatic Animal Empathy","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The whalefeller can ask questions of, receive answers from, and use the Diplomacy skill with aquatic animals.</p>"},{"n":"Aquatic Tracker","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The whalefeller can follow trails through the water via careful surveillance of currents, disturbed fauna, and other telltale signs obvious only to a dweller in the deep. They can use Survival to Track even in aquatic environments.</p>"},{"n":"Wavesense","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The whalefeller's wavesense is precise out to a range of 120 feet, imprecise out to 300 feet, and vague out to 1 mile.</p>"},{"n":"Bone Harpoon","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A whalefeller's bone harpoon is a part of their body. Unlike a typical harpoon, it doesn't have a visible rope or chain; instead, the whalefeller is magically connected to their harpoon and can recall it with Reclaim Harpoon. If another creature within 1 mile is holding the bone harpoon, the whalefeller can attempt to Disarm it, no matter how large the creature is. If the harpoon is ever destroyed, the whalefeller must succeed at a DC 30 Fortitude save or be Sickened 2.</p>"},{"n":"Colossus Hunter","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The whalefeller deals 4 additional damage with their Strikes against creatures that are Large or larger.</p>"},{"n":"Dart Away","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The whalefeller is targeted with a melee or ranged attack by an attacker they can see that is currently taking persistent damage from Tear Free</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whalefeller gains a +2 status bonus to AC against the triggering attack. If the attack misses, the triggering creature takes 2d6 piercing damage from fragments of bone left in the wound.</p>"},{"n":"Reclaim Harpoon","a":"f","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The whalefeller's harpoon is within 1 mile and is not being held by any creature</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whalefeller's bone harpoon returns to their hand.</p>"},{"n":"Tear Free","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The whalefeller's last action was a successful harpoon Strike</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whalefeller sprouts additional barbs from the harpoon before violently recalling it with Reclaim Harpoon. The target takes 2d6 persistent bleed damage and takes a –10-foot status penalty to their swim Speed for as long as they are taking this persistent damage. Even once healed, the wound makes the target easier to track; the whalefeller gains a +2 circumstance bonus to Survival checks to Track the target for 24 hours.</p><p>Effect: Tear Free</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/wy8gy9ZrQ7dh9HHj":{"abilities":[{"n":"Minstrel's Mimic","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["occult"],"f":"","d":"<p>A whittler's serpent does not understand languages, but it can emulate speech, poetry, and music that it has heard, even producing instrumental sounds such as maracas, drums, or pipes. It instinctively accompanies nearby music. If it rolls a failure or critical failure on a check to Aid a Performance, it gets a success instead.</p>"},{"n":"Warning Rattle","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["auditory","emotion","fear","mental","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature attempts a melee attack roll against the whittler's serpent</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The whittler's serpent rattles its body in a sound reminiscent of a rattlesnake or a maraca, in an attempt to divert the attack and discourage further violence. The creature must succeed at a DC 17 Will save or become Frightened 1 (Frightened 2 on a critical failure).</p>"},{"n":"Enigma's Refrain","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["fortune","occult"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> Once every 1d4 rounds</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The inspiration that drives bards and other entertainers is left as a remnant in the whittler's serpent. The whittler's serpent makes a bite Strike, rolling the attack twice and using the better result. The attack ignores circumstance penalties to the attack roll and any flat check required due to the target being Concealed or hidden.</p>"},{"n":"Whistling Wind","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>A whittler's serpent can Feint using Performance instead of Deception. The Feint gains the auditory trait and loses the mental trait.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/ZuKdYLhfCh2zLSOc":{"lang":["Fey","Muan"],"abilities":[{"n":"Tree Merge","a":"2","c":"interaction","t":["concentrate","plant","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck merges their body into an adjacent tree. While merged, they can't take any actions that require their body (including Cultivate Imagination), but they can still use their mind and senses as normal while merged. They can exit the tree into any space adjacent to the tree as a two-action activity, ending the effect.</p>"},{"n":"Splinter","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a woodpluck wields a melee weapon they created with Cultivate Imagination, the weapon produces splinters on impact, dealing an additional 1d4 piercing damage.</p>"},{"n":"Cultivated Performance","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["auditory","concentrate","incapacitation","mental","primal","visual"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck sings a powerful song, and their sprout dances along with them. The woodpluck chooses up to four creatures within 30 feet, which must each attempt a DC 18 Will save.</p><hr><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature is Fascinated for 1 round.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature is fascinated and stunned for 1 round.</p>"},{"n":"Cultivate Imagination","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","plant","primal","wood"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck imagines a common level 0 non-magical weapon, shield, piece of adventuring gear, or simple tool of no more than 1 Bulk, which then grows on their head. The cultivated item is made entirely from wood and other plant matter, but otherwise functions as the base item. The woodpluck can then Interact to grab the item. The most common weapons imagined by woodplucks are listed in their Strikes above. Cultivating an item in this way causes any items previously created by the woodpluck's imagination to break down into ordinary plant matter.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/z4hdFCI8xXXLIVJJ":{"lang":["Fey","Muan"],"abilities":[{"n":"Dense Swarm","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The individual creatures in a woodpluck chorus are Small. Unlike most swarms, they can't share their space with other creatures, and they aren't immune to precision damage or resistant to physical damage.</p>"},{"n":"Cultivated Volley","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodplucks cultivate javelins and then throw them as a volley. This volley is a 10-foot burst within 30 feet that deals 4d6 piercing damage (DC 22 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Group Imagination","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","plant","primal","stance"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck chorus collectively imagines components of a large project they then quickly assemble as needed, granting one of the following benefits of their choice. This benefit lasts for 1 minute or until the woodpluck chorus uses this ability again.</p><ul><li>A climb, swim, or fly Speed of 20 feet.</li><li>Wooden Flurry and Cultivated Volley also deal 1d6 persistent bleed damage.</li><li>Access to the Cultivated Party action.</li></ul>"},{"n":"Wooden Flurry","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodplucks lash out with cultivated weapons at each foe within 5 feet, dealing 1d6+3 piercing or 1d6+3 slashing damage (DC 24 basic Reflex save). The chorus can independently choose whether the damage is piercing or slashing for each foe.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/BdaAoJecY11FBMbD":{"lang":["Common","Fey","Muan"],"abilities":[{"n":"Tree Merge","a":"2","c":"interaction","t":["concentrate","plant","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck merges their body into an adjacent tree. While merged, they can't take any actions that require their body (including Cultivate Imagination), but they can still use their mind and senses as normal while merged. They can exit the tree into any space adjacent to the tree as a two-action activity, ending the effect.</p>"},{"n":"Splinter","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>When a woodpluck wields a melee weapon they created with Cultivate Imagination, the weapon produces splinters on impact, dealing an additional 1d8 piercing damage.</p>"},{"n":"Cultivate Imagination","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","plant","primal","wood"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck imagines a common non-magical weapon, shield, piece of adventuring gear, or simple tool of up to level 3 and no more than 3 Bulk, which then grows on their head. Any weapon created with this ability is a <em>+1 striking</em> weapon and gains the effects of a <em>returning</em> rune if it has the thrown trait. A woodpluck elder can wield a weapon that requires two hands in its one hand. The cultivated item is made entirely from wood and other plant matter, but otherwise functions as the base item. The woodpluck can then Interact to grab the item. The most common weapons imagined by woodplucks are listed in their Strikes above. Cultivating an item in this way causes any items previously created by the woodpluck's imagination to break down into ordinary plant matter.</p>"},{"n":"Cultivate Mount","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","plant","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The woodpluck imagines a Medium or Large creature or simple vehicle, which then grows from a secondary sprout to form a wooden mount underneath it. The elder's size increases to that of the imagined creature, and the elder chooses to either increase its Speed to 40 feet or gain a fly Speed of 25 feet. The mount is an extension of the elder, not a separate creature. The elder can Dismiss this effect.</p>"},{"n":"Stampeding Mount","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Requirements</strong> The woodpluck elder has a Cultivated Mount</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The woodpluck elder jumps off their mount and sends it charging forward, dealing 8d6 bludgeoning damage to creatures and unattended objects in an 80-foot line. Creatures in the line must attempt a DC 26 Reflex save. If the mount collides with an object or creature of a size larger than it, the line stops early unless the object or creature is reduced to 0 Hit Points, After the charge, the mount breaks down into ordinary plant matter.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The creature is unaffected.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The creature takes half damage.</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The creature takes full damage and is knocked Prone.</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The creature takes double damage, is knocked prone, and becomes Clumsy 1 for 1 minute.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/H7hsdULvwcUSTeK2":{"lang":["Common","Fey"],"abilities":[{"n":"Sneak Attack","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The wripie deals 1d6 extra precision damage to Off-Guard creatures.</p>"},{"n":"Grab","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The monster's last action was a successful Strike that lists Grab in its damage entry, or the monster has a creature Grabbed or Restrained</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> If used after a Strike, the monster attempts to Grapple the creature using the body part it attacked with. This attempt neither applies nor counts toward the creature's multiple attack penalty.</p><p>The monster can instead use Grab and choose one creature it's grabbing or restraining with an appendage that has Grab to automatically extend that condition to the end of the monster's next turn.</p></p>"},{"n":"Not That One!","a":"r","c":"defensive","t":["primal","teleportation"],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> A creature targets the wripie with an attack and they can see the attacker, and the wripie is with 30 feet of at least one of their copies</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The wripie swap places with a copy within 30 feet. If the attack hits the copy, the copy explodes, spraying razor-sharp flower petals in a 5-foot emanation. All non-wripie creatures in the area take 2d6 slashing damage (DC 16 basic Reflex save).</p>"},{"n":"Create Copy","a":"1","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","illusion","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>The wripie creates a duplicate of themselves within 30 feet. This copy has the same statistics as the wripie, but disappears if it takes any damage. The wripie and all of their copies share their actions and multiple attack penalty. A creature that Seeks can determine of a wripie is real or a copy with a successful DC 18 Perception check. A copy lasts for 1 minute. A wripie can maintain up three copies of themselves at a time; if they create a new copy while three copies are active, the oldest copy disappears.</p>"},{"n":"Petal Dancing","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["move","primal"],"f":"","d":"<p>With an explosion of flower petals, the wripies burst into motion. The wripie and all of their copies Stride, gaining the Concealed condition during this movement.</p>"},{"n":"Final Prank","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The wripie is reduced to 0 Hit Points</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The wripie decides if their foes have been good sports or poor sports when dealing with their pranks before disappearing, leaving behind a 20-foot emanation of green smoke.</p><p><strong>Good Sports</strong> The emanation fills with soft flower petals and soothing smells. Each creature in the area heals 2d8 healing Hit Points.</p><p><strong>Poor Sports</strong> The emanation fills with thorned vines, dealing 2d6 slashing damage (DC 16 basic Reflex save). The area becomes difficult terrain. If the terrain is not a viable environment for the vines, they wither after 24 hours.</p>"},{"n":"Puckish Prankster","a":null,"c":"offensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>All damage that a wripie deals is nonlethal unless they consciously decide to deal lethal damage.</p>"}]},"battlezoo-bestiary-es-pf2e.bestiary/QA66yZfnpV7G3Zsb":{"lang":["Envisioning"],"lore":[["Mathematics Lore",33]],"notes":{"hp":"half life","saves":"+1 status to all saves vs. magic","per":"temporospatial reckoning"},"abilities":[{"n":"Envisioning","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":["aura","divine","mental"],"f":"","d":"<p>100 feet. A xenarian can communicate mentally with any creatures in the aura using wordless psychic projections. They don't need to share a language, though the aeon's meaning to non-aeons can be vague and is often mysterious. An aeon can use this ability to communicate flawlessly with any other aeon on the same plane as themselves.</p>"},{"n":"+1 Status to All Saves vs. Magic","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":""},{"n":"Fractions of Life","a":"f","c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><strong>Frequency</strong> once per each creature's turn</p><p><strong>Requirements</strong> The xenarian is at 1 Hit Point and would take damage</p><hr><p><strong>Effect</strong> The xenarian falls back on tiny fractions of their remaining Hit Point to remain conscious. They do not take damage.</p>"},{"n":"Half Again","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["aura","divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>160 feet. A creature that approaches the xenarian with a move action can't move more than half the remaining distance toward the xenarian. As a reminder, adjacent creatures are 5 feet apart.</p>"},{"n":"Half Life","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine"],"f":"","d":"<p>Whenever a xenarian takes damage and is not at a damage threshold, the damage can't reduce them below their next damage threshold. When they regain Hit Points and are not at a damage threshold, they can't increase their Hit Points above their next damage threshold. Their damage thresholds are 64, 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, and 1. Even if a damaging effect deals damage of multiple types, such as a flaming weapon, or fires multiple attacks, such as a force barrage, all damage is first added together before the xenarian's Hit Points are reduced. If a xenarian has multiple types of persistent damage, they are also all added together first.</p>"},{"n":"Inexorable","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p>The xenarian recovers from the Paralyzed, slowed, and stunned conditions at the end of their turn. They're also immune to penalties to their Speeds and the Immobilized condition, and they ignore difficult terrain and greater difficult terrain.</p>"},{"n":"Temporospatial Reckoning","a":null,"c":"defensive","t":["divine","revelation"],"f":"","d":"<p>A xenarian automatically detects and identifies space-altering magic (including teleportation effects) and time-altering magic and is only affected by the magic if they choose to be.</p>"},{"n":"Constant Spells","a":null,"c":"interaction","t":[],"f":"","d":"<p><p>A constant spell affects the monster without the monster needing to cast it, and its duration is unlimited. If a constant spell gets counteracted, the monster can reactivate it by spending the normal spellcasting actions the spell requires.</p></p>"},{"n":"Bisector","a":"2","c":"offensive","t":["divine","incapacitation"],"f":"","d":"<p>The xenarian reaches into the wells of essence that animate each creature in a 20-foot burst within 500 feet and attempts to cut them in half. Creatures in the area must attempt a DC 36 Fortitude save.</p><hr><p><strong>Critical Success</strong> The target is unaffected and becomes temporarily immune to Bisector for 1 hour.</p><p><strong>Success</strong> The target's Hit Points are reduced to three-quarters of their current Hit Points (rounded up).</p><p><strong>Failure</strong> The target's Hit Points are reduced to half of their current Hit Points (rounded up).</p><p><strong>Critical Failure</strong> The target's Hit Points are reduced to one-quarter of their current Hit Points (rounded up).</p>"},{"n":"Summon Fractrix","a":"3","c":"offensive","t":["concentrate","divine","manipulate","summon"],"f":"","d":"<p>The xenarian summons a fractrix to fight on their side assist in other tasks. They can Sustain the summon for up to 1 minute.</p>"}]}});
